{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting","id":124026,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Shapeshifting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-02T15:01:56-07:00","id":124026,"title":"Idigam Chronicles Weekly Discussion: Shapeshifting","content":"The changing forms for the sons and daughters of Luna<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Changing Man &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My current thoughts,<br /> <br /> Hishu: No real qualms about the form, yet Uratha are constantly portrayed as having supernatural senses even in their most mundane form, I do think at least a +1 to perception rolls or the ability to track by scent (at a penalty of course) would be a decent course of action. Not too powerful, but maybe enough to turn the tide over a simple mundane<br /> <br /> Dalu: I have no problems with this form as is, especially if the Hishu changes are implemented. Would merely be an enhanced for of Hishu<br /> <br /> Gauru: This form I both love the changes and am disappointed a bit. First of all the heals all bashing and lethal damage per turn definitely makes the form useful especially against hard hitting opponents. What I am sort of disappointed on is the always uses down and dirty combat rules against lesser foes. My reasoning is it is some of those encounters that take you by surprise. A group of low ranking level 1 spirits can actually take down a Gauru werewolf if they use the correct numen. Additionally, humans can band together and even a rampaging Gauru if known is no match for 2 or 3 people with a silver slug each if they get lucky. Lunacy itself should be the equalizer, not a blanket mechanic such as a condition.<br /> <br /> Urshul: I almost think this form is a bit too strong since losing a defense for the rest of the scene is massive. My suggestion is have the damage act more like beats such as arm wrack. If the damage is healed, they gain the defense back. This way, a sufficiently powerful werewolf or vampire can keep going. Even a Gauru werewolf attacked by a few Urshul werewolves would find it odd that his defense does not come back when all of the damage dealt has been healed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Urhan: I like the pre-emp action in combat for 1 essence, but I would make it contested if the opponent had an ability such as Celerity, or used Urhan form of their own. Against mundane abilities, makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":444,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","user":"Dessembrae","date":". 05-02-2014, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:17:51-07:00","id":124037,"title":"","content":"....GOD DAMNIT, I FORGOT THIS WAS COMING!<br /> <br /> *tips his hat* Well played.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:19:45-07:00","id":124040,"title":"","content":"I love the new Gauru:<br /> <br /> <b>Rules for a Fair Fight: </b>Just surrender. He may spare you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:22:11-07:00","id":124041,"title":"","content":"I like it. I'm interested in how Primal Urge has changed. Before it kind of made you stand out in the crowd, now it seems to help you slink in, at least in human form. I really like the Gauru using Down and Dirty, I always liked the Extras system from Exalted, and while not exactly alike it has some similarities. I'd want to be clear on the duration, though. Is that per day, just once you do it, once a month, or what? I like the Death Rage and attack closest parts of it, but if you can't do it much I'm not sure how often you'd even use gauru except for clearing out a bunch of extras or getting a quick heal. Which, of course, is what it's for so I guess that makes sense.<br /> <br /> I suppose more information on what 'back down' means for the Dalu would be important. Perhaps a condition for it.<br /> For Ushul, I'm guessing the defense penalty is talking about the group-penalty. It certainly mixes well with GMC, where group fighting is the way to go. Making proper enemies might be difficult, having to consider how many are likely to attack in urshul form, you could have a big defense difference.<br /> I think Urhan's initiative jump ability should be interesting in gameplay, though I could see trouble. I suppose it depends on the cost of essence, so to speak (whether you can spend it often). Before we got much talk about it, I thought someone said that they could get essence from attacking spirits with their bites.<br /> <br /> Since they're keeping the same Attribute modifiers, I suppose they should be posted somewhere:<br /> Dalu: +1 STR, +1 STA, -1 MAN, +1 Size<br /> Gauru: +3 STR, +1 DEX, +2 STA, +2 Size<br /> Urshul: +2 STR, +2 DEX, +2 STA, -3 MAN, +1 Size<br /> Urhan: +2 DEX, +1 STA, -1 Size","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2014, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:28:48-07:00","id":124049,"title":"","content":"Oh Goodie! Crunch. I shall break down my thoughts into three categories:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Things That Are Great</u></b>:<ul><li>Love that all five forms have clear applications in and around the hunt.</li> <li>Love that Gauru regenerates ALL Bashing and Lethal (though I have some reservations about <b>all </b>lethal).</li> <li>Love that Gauru uses Down &amp; Dirty combat inherently against extras (though I do feel allowances should be made with certain spirits, even if their rank is lower).</li> <li>Love that Dalu can part crowds and intimidate (though I might suggest Wits as a defense in a chase)</li> </ul><b><u>Things That I'm Not So Hot On</u></b>:<ul><li>The Hishu crowd penalty doesn't make a whole lot of sense to me. Perhaps that's something to be justified with fluff.</li> <li>&quot;Can't Spend Willpower to Attack a Gauru Werewolf&quot; really bothers me for some reason. It feels almost like it should be the other way around, that a Werewolf should be horrifying to aggress. But that'd be a bit much, perhaps lesser returns on Willpower expenditure or something to convey that fighting a massive wolfman is mentally exhausting.</li> <li>Limited Gauru duration. Restricting Gauru duration in this manner feels so...artificial, but it's nothing terrible.</li> <li>&quot;Urshul defense penalties last the whole scene&quot; this makes very little sense, a character who has time to back off and recover shouldn't continue to suffer a penalty from onslaught. Maybe instead have Urshul double onslaught penalty, regardless of damaging success. That might better enforce the forms position as 'prey harrier'.</li> </ul><b><u>Things That I Absolutely Oppose</u></b>:<ul><li>&quot;Apply full Defense against firearms attacks&quot; &lt;- That. Not for some goofy crossover reason, not for combat balance, but because it means a wolf with middling to high defense doesn't have to fear a silver bullet. And that's just not right.</li> </ul>Beyond that last one, which is a humongous deal breaker. This is all just stellar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:33:45-07:00","id":124052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124049#post124049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Apply full Defense against firearms attacks&quot; &lt;- That. Not for some goofy crossover reason, not for combat balance, but because it means a wolf with middling to high defense doesn't have to fear a silver bullet. And that's just not right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate to nitpick (not really), but that is only for the intermediary forms, dalu, gauru and urshul. A human and a wolf would still be easily hit by a silver bullet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:34:12-07:00","id":124053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124049#post124049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urshul defense penalties last the whole scene&quot; this makes very little sense, a character who has time to back off and recover shouldn't continue to suffer a penalty from onslaught. Maybe instead have Urshul double onslaught penalty, regardless of damaging success. That might better enforce the forms position as 'prey harrier'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree with this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124052#post124052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hate to nitpick (not really), but that is only for the intermediary forms, dalu, gauru and urshul. A human and a wolf would still be easily hit by a silver bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main problem is even though I WANT this to be since I love werewolf, I can only potentially see this against Gauru form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:38:06-07:00","id":124056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124052#post124052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to nitpick (not really), but that is only for the intermediary forms, dalu, gauru and urshul. A human and a wolf would still be easily hit by a silver bullet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The massive wolf-man being weak only to silver bullets is absolutely iconic of Werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:38:49-07:00","id":124057,"title":"","content":"I....really don't have much to say about this. The Gauru are now as they should be, and I like the elements of utility to the rest, but I just don't have much to say otherwise. It's...kind of cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:39:40-07:00","id":124059,"title":"","content":"I hope we get Kuruth next week, that'll shed some light on the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:40:59-07:00","id":124060,"title":"","content":"Presumably you'd still be weak (I don't think we know how silver works yet), just harder to target. If silver does aggravated, gauru won't be able to heal it 'normally.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2014, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:46:00-07:00","id":124067,"title":"","content":"There was bait here, I took it, and then realized I was being a whiny bitch. I am the king of self-infliction folks. Otherwise, it's removed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-02-2014, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:47:39-07:00","id":124069,"title":"","content":"I'll be the dissenting voice this week, though I like most of the changes. As a WtA fan, the five forms are possibly the straightest copy from the previous game (with changes admittedly).<br /> <br /> The time limit to Gauru is still there, which is rather bleh. It seems Urshul will still be a go to battle form.<br /> <br /> But mainly, Urhan as a form is still a bit strange to me. I understand it is for long distance running, but the form is a bit lackluster in Forsaken, as the Uratha don't really have the same connection to the wild wolves that justified the lupus form in Apocalypse. This means its a normal looking wolf-form that limited to where it can run due it being a wolf, is basically used solely for long running because other forms can hunt well, and in general feels like an artifact from WtA.<br /> <br /> Adding to it, the other Forsaken forms have a purpose beyond the Hunt. Hishu is dealing with humans, Dalu is for rituals/controlled fights with weapons, Gauru is for brutal beatdown, Urshul is for gauru-style combat without the Death Rage. Urhan.. doesn't. I guess if it could appear domesticated with a gift/ability, to spy on the prey.<br /> <br /> Though, if you've had/used urhan well, great. Just from personal experience I feel the form could be dropped or modified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:49:59-07:00","id":124071,"title":"","content":"I always preferred urshul over urhan. 'Murica.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:50:40-07:00","id":124073,"title":"","content":"I expect (because I haven't yet seen the actual full first draft for forms yet either) that the full draft will answer some of the issues, like how the stickiness of the Urshul Defence penalty interacts with prey who have an opportunity to back out and recuperate, or situations where lesser foes shouldn't be Down &amp; Dirtied by Gauru.<br /> <br /> As for silver, werewolves <i>are</i> still vulnerable to it; but bringing an automatic weapon loaded with silver isn't an instant win against the People. Silver deals Aggravated and that's the <i>one</i> damage type that sticks to werewolves effectively; the effectiveness swing for regular mortals with silver bullets is still fairly hefty.<br /> <br /> Anyway, you can now see why I was saying that it's possible to build a Rahu who can take shrug off hits from tank rounds if they're in Gauru <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Gauru time limit will, I suspect, have the same in-character justification as the old one; notably, it now keys in well with the extreme regeneration of the Gauru form, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Looks like I got it wrong on werewolves dealing Bashing to vampires; oh well, live and learn <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It does mean that an Uratha with That Death Facet I Talked About will be pretty horrendous opponents for undead in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:51:14-07:00","id":124074,"title":"","content":"Some sort of Merit or Gift that allows for either a lessened time limit on Gauru or turning the explicit ban on it outside of combat into just a heavy penalty would be lovely. The wolfman is iconic and having it just turn up or combats that resemble a blender set to the highest setting exclusively would be lame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:52:41-07:00","id":124077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124060#post124060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably you'd still be weak (I don't think we know how silver works yet), just harder to target. If silver does aggravated, gauru won't be able to heal it 'normally.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming Gauru can be hit at all. No Willpower to attack means there are pretty good odds of a chance die, and even on a success it's very unlikely to deal enough damage to kill or even drive the Werewolf to retreat. <br /> <br /> Given how many bullets it'd take to incapacitate Gauru in the first place (only lethal that has rolled over to Aggravated will stick around, so the first ~11 damage each turn would be erased), the extreme speed and distance covering possibilities (Urhan is almost guaranteed to preempt a shooter), and the potential for armoring gifts, I don't really think they need any more help against gunmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:56:16-07:00","id":124078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124077#post124077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how many bullets it'd take to incapacitate Gauru in the first place (only lethal that has rolled over to Aggravated will stick around, so the first ~11 damage each turn would be erased), the extreme speed and distance covering possibilities (Urhan is almost guaranteed to preempt a shooter), and the potential for armoring gifts, I don't really think they need any more help against gunmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, that's working off the assumption of one man with a silver bullet vs at least two werewolves. Why not shoot the urhan? This is the kind of thing that is going to want playtesting, rather than white rooming. Just a few months ago people were complaining that guns were overpowered to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2014, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T15:59:50-07:00","id":124080,"title":"","content":"On the comment about Gauru's &quot;Cannot be Willpower Auged attacked&quot;, it's worth remembering that Lunacy is mind raping you at the same time. A person who overcomes full on Lunacy deserves the right to be able to attack.<br /> <br /> He does not, however, have to have the inner resolve to think it's even possible to win. It seems a fair compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:01:39-07:00","id":124084,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm not too fond of Gauru regenerating All lethal. I'm ok with bashing though.<br /> <br /> Just figure: how do two Gauru beat each other if they are always regenerating? They have to deal at least every turn their opponent's Health +1 to deal 1 aggravated. I don't think it's functional at all. Also, I don't see any kind of human being a threath, not even with shotguns.<br /> Anyone without at least being a master of combat can't do anything to a Gauru werewolf. Anyone without a chainsaw, exceptional success and Heavy weapons 5 to deal 1 aggravated. Even then, they'll easily die some turns after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:02:15-07:00","id":124085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124078#post124078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, that's working off the assumption of one man with a silver bullet vs at least two werewolves. Why not shoot the urhan? This is the kind of thing that is going to want playtesting, rather than white rooming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it's working off the assumption of reflexive shape-shifting with Essence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yes, naturally this all requires playtest. Those were just my initial feelings on the matter.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>Perhaps I should explain where that concern is coming from. In a recent game (GMC rules) I had a Ghoul, a old military veteran, armed with a heavy machine-gun lobbing out silver bullets. He hit his target Werewolf (in Gauru) dead on, no defense applied. Rolled an exceptional success, plus another 3 automatic damage on top of that. Werewolf had no armor, her Stamina was 3. This <b>did not kill the Werewolf</b>. With defense applied he'd have done less than half that damage.<br /> If a military trained, supernaturally augmented, heaven weapons wielding marksman spraying high caliber silver full auto cannot gun down Gauru (or Dalu for that matter) under the current rules, I'm a touch concerned about improving their bullet resilience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-02-2014, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:08:44-07:00","id":124089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124084#post124084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'm not too fond of Gauru regenerating All lethal. I'm ok with bashing though.<br /> <br /> Just figure: how do two Gauru beat each other if they are always regenerating? They have to deal at least every turn their opponent's Health +1 to deal 1 aggravated. I don't think it's functional at all. Also, I don't see any kind of human being a threath, not even with shotguns.<br /> Anyone without at least being a master of combat can't do anything to a Gauru werewolf. Anyone without a chainsaw, exceptional success and Heavy weapons 5 to deal 1 aggravated. Even then, they'll easily die some turns after.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was the point, it is massively hard for a mundane...or anything for that matter by itself to take down the war form. It requires teamwork and probably more than a few explosives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:10:49-07:00","id":124090,"title":"","content":"Ah, Stew has posted some more clarifications in the article's comment threads about the use of Down &amp; Dirty, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:11:30-07:00","id":124091,"title":"","content":"I think the deal with Urshul inflicting permanent Defense penalty (just one per character inflicting it, mind) has to do with the relentless of the form. Also, first good strike wins the fight. The forms are designed to find prey, chase it, harry it, kill it and the disappear in the crowd.<br /> <br /> Why the intermediary forms can dodge bullets? heightened senses. Urhan gets pseudo Celerity without a limit like how many dots they have, that's cool. Primal Urge 2 Uratha in Urhan can thoroughly ruin any ambusher's day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:27:41-07:00","id":124104,"title":"","content":"Another snippet of info Stew has revealed in the article comments: Werewolves' basic Bashing regeneration rate increases at higher Primal Urge levels, and spending 1 Essence turns it all to Lethal regeneration for a turn instead..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:41:36-07:00","id":124118,"title":"","content":"I like what I see in these forms. My thoughts on things about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Intermediates v. Bullets</b><br /> As I gather the point of this rule is to make it so much so that the Gauru isn't the go-to way to fight guns and that werewolves fighting werewolves are just as well using claws and such against one-another than bother with uzis. Silver bullets hurt as-is (it sticks to full) and I think that's the main point. It makes it so Dog Soldiers makes more sense to me at least. No amount of machine guns matter unless they're silver rounds or they're tanks.<br /> <br /> I also expect the silver claws Facet to be about again still (probably in Blood Talons somewhere). This probably will result in the tools werewolves use to kill one-another.<br /> <br /> <b>Gauru Time Limit</b><br /> With how potent this form is, I am not too against how it has a time limit now. If it's going ot remain short, make it the sort of thing you smash the button to kill the shit out of something and risk that frenzy for. That you can't just hang out in this form is nice too since well, I'm not interested in playing the form up as some harmony of man and wolf, but more a wolf-spirit-man killing machine. This does that well.<br /> <br /> <b>WIllpower to Fight</b><br /> I think I missed this rule, where is it? That being said, I do think if you are not someone subject to Down &amp; Dirty, you probably should be able to fight the werewolf. Its stats alone will probably make that person have to work hard to survive it, especially against a pack.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T16:58:35-07:00","id":124127,"title":"","content":"I said something about not white rooming it, but here I come with a suggestion.<br /> <br /> We do have a Play by Post board. And we have access to a Dice roller -&gt; <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgroller.com/nwod/</a><br /> It wouldn't be too hard to start up a Werewolf Arena, if someone was particularly interested. We don't know all the rules about werewolf, sure, but the main complaint herein seems to be the combat ability of the forms. It wouldn't be too hard to whip up some humans ranging from lone gangsters to hunter cells and use some existing werewolf write-ups and show your work. You'd probably want to set up an arena, so it wasn't just, well, a white room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-02-2014, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:13:26-07:00","id":124134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124127#post124127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said something about not white rooming it, but here I come with a vague suggestion.<br /> <br /> We do have a Play by Post board. And we have access to a Dice roller -&gt; <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgroller.com/nwod/</a><br /> It wouldn't be too hard to start up a Werewolf Arena, if someone was particularly interested. We don't know all the rules about werewolf, sure, but the main complaint herein seems to be the combat ability of the forms. It wouldn't be too hard to whip up some humans ranging from lone gangsters to hunter cells and use some existing werewolf write-ups and show your work. You'd probably want to set up an arena, so it wasn't just, well, a white room.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, you could probably arrange it up as a Circuit Chronicle from FCG, with some nose tweaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:26:29-07:00","id":124143,"title":"","content":"To me, the Gauru form feels a bit too durable for the role suggested - to take down the prey when the time is right. All that regeneration suggests a more (though not necessarily extremely) drawn-out conflict, where I feel the Gauru form should be a more 'go for the throat' sort of deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:37:03-07:00","id":124151,"title":"","content":"FYI guys Stew replied saying healing is based on Primal Urge with the example;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2019ll get into this when we cover Primal Urge, but at high PU you might regenerate say 4 bashing/turn. For 1 Essence, that becomes 4 lethal/turn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Personally really like most of what I see here. I'd like to see Urhan base it's defense on &gt;Wits or Dexterity instead of lesser of. Also I completely disagree that Urhan is pointless. It's the only form that allows for interrupting actions. That's pretty huge. And Speed as a dice pool instead of Dex + Athletics is again, a pretty sizable advantage.<br /> <br /> What I like most here is that they are getting away from attribute bonuses in the forms. While it makes sense in Forsaken, it's always a bit of a pain in the ass to track how much Strength or Health you have at any given moment as you transfer between 2-3 forms every fight and then calculating it all back when the last foe drops. Though I will miss (assuming it's gone) 9-again in Dalu/Urshal and 8-again in Gauru. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:51:29-07:00","id":124160,"title":"","content":"I gotta agree, about the attributes, shifting those numbers around, and all the attributes they form, can get tedious.<br /> I think one aspect I like about gauru is the increased healing. Before, you'd want to avoid gauru, since if you hopped into it you were essentially stuck in fight mode, so if you were ambushed or just took a nasty accident, your big choices were run away or go into death rage and hope for the best, especially if you were new (what are 'young' werewolves called? pups?). Now you have that scene where the guy who just found out gets surrounded by antagonistic humans and gauru is more of a survival option. You risk a lot, knowing you'll probably be killing them, but you'll likely survive the experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:57:29-07:00","id":124165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">they keep the same Attribute modifiers</span></span></span></b> </div> </div> </div>I hate it when 2 forms have similar attributes modifiers , that goes for gauru-urshul relationship , since they have the same perception and stamina modifiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The following rules apply to all three intermediary forms (Dalu/Gauru/Urshul)</b><ul><li><b>Apply full Defense against firearms attacks.</b></li> <li><b>Inflict Lunacy appropriate for the form.</b></li> <li><b>Never affected by Beaten Down.</b></li> <li><b>Bite &amp; claw attacks count as weapons, and thus deal lethal damage. They also count as supernatural attacks (e.g. dealing lethal damage to vampires). </b></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Full defence against firearms ? Why ? plus where is the higher of dexterity or wits defense calculation ?</li> <li>Lunacy is a core element, so is good to have it .</li> <li>Beat down immunity also existed in Fprsaken core , but only for Gauru ,Why for other forms as well ?</li> <li>The bite and claw situation is quite interesting , I expected it for Gauru - Urshul , but not for Dalu .</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Hishu</b><ul><li>Used to walk unseen in the world of humans, even on the hunt.</li> <li>Applies Primal Urge as a penalty to any rolls to pick him out of the crowd.</li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>The first part is cool , now it works against all observers , not only supernatural powers of scrutiny , But primal urge as penalty ? That makes me wonder about Primal Urge changes .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Dalu</b><ul><li>Used to isolate and chase foes among humans, where Urhan and Urshul would invite too much attention.</li> <li>+2 Perception bonus.</li> <li>Roll Primal Urge vs. prey\u2019s Composuire to force a crowd to part and give up your prey, or to make a single person human back down.</li> <li>Claws deal +0, bites +1 but require a grapple.</li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Ok about perception .<br /> The second reference though makes me wonder if Dalu is gonna be restricted only to this isolation thing example or generaly in any social action that has to do with human primal reactions .<br /> Claws +0 damage is ok , but the +1 makes Dalu fangs stronger than urhan , should it be that way ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Gauru</b><ul><li>Used to kill prey as quickly and efficiently as possible.</li> <li>+3 Perception bonus (normally used to sniff out closest prey).</li> <li>Must attack nearest opponent (either bite/claw or throwing things) or move towards nearest opponent <i>if</i> you can\u2019t attack. Doing otherwise risks Kuruth.</li> <li>Taking Gauru outside of combat <i>always</i> leads to Kuruth.</li> <li>Limited duration of [Stamina + Primal Urge + Auspice Renown] turns.</li> <li>Always use down &amp; dirty combat against lesser foes (most humans, equal rank or weaker spirits, etc.)</li> <li>Opponents who aren\u2019t victims of Down &amp; Dirty Combat cannot spend Willpower to attack the werewolf.</li> <li>Regenerate <i>all</i> bashing and lethal damage each turn.</li> <li>Claws deal +1, bite deals +2 without grappling.</li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Perception still same as Urshul ,Check</li> <li>Aggressive behavior , Check</li> <li>Taking gauru outside of combat ? I always thought that when taking Gauru makes any situation , well a combat situation. Sounds to me a bit awkward ....</li> <li>Limited duration ,Check , I would prefer a control form penalty rather than time limit . Noticed that now renown always adds to the time limit of the form .</li> <li>Easy kills lesser foes , Check . Well this is a new one , Which seems SO COOL !! I guess gauru gains a try to kill instantly an opponent per turn and this is so good for horror mood , Thank you Stew</li> <li>Regenerate all damage ? or just all bashing OR all lethal ? In any case this is OP . Adding the down &amp; dirty comabt rule makes a gauru stoppable only by silver , that indeed adds to the horror mood .</li> <li>Same modifiers for natural weaponry , Check . Though I would prefer to add +1 modifier in initiative with claws against lower size opponents , or other werewolves who try bite attacks .</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Urshul</b><ul><li>Used to weaken and harry the prey near the end of the hunt.</li> <li>+3 Perception bonus.</li> <li>On a damaging hit, the Defense reduction lasts for the rest of the scene \u2013 this doesn\u2019t stack if the same character damages twice, but does from different werewolves.</li> <li>Claws deal +0 and increase Initiative by 1, bite deals +1 without grappling.</li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b\u200bDefense reduction for the scene ? How about creatures with regeneration ? Wait wait wait , how much defense reduction ?</span></span></span></li> <li>has anyone noticed that the natural weaponry damage modifiers of urshul are the opposite of Dalu ? Also does the claw attack make Urshul to look like bear wolf ?</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Urhan</b><ul><li>Used to chase down prey over long distances, or to harry where Urshul would be noticed.</li> <li>No claws, can bite for +0 damage without grappling. This doesn\u2019t count as a supernatural attack.</li> <li>+4 Perception bonus.</li> <li>Spend 1 Essence to pre-empt another character\u2019s action in combat with your own.</li> <li>In a foot chase, use Speed in place of Strength + Athletics.</li> </ul></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Normal wolves and vampire wolves have +1 damage with bite ....</li> <li>No natural armor from fur ? That also goes for urshul as well . It existd in Blood and smoke Gangrel forms ..... Yes yes yes , I know I know , werewolf is its own game ... but still ....</li> <li>Same perception bonus . Check</li> <li>Natural celerity (solo initiative edition) , Check . Well this could have been the new Clarity gift .</li> <li>the speed in exchange of strength+athletics makes Urhan the cheetah form ?</li> </ul>Harmony for shapeshifting and Kuruth rolls is a very interesting change , But that makees me wonder more about Primal urge and Kuruth .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 05-02-2014, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:06:42-07:00","id":124168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124151#post124151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI guys Stew replied saying healing is based on Primal Urge with the example;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2019ll get into this when we cover Primal Urge, but at high PU you might regenerate say 4 bashing/turn. For 1 Essence, that becomes 4 lethal/turn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Personally really like most of what I see here. I'd like to see Urhan base it's defense on &gt;Wits or Dexterity instead of lesser of. Also I completely disagree that Urhan is pointless. It's the only form that allows for interrupting actions. That's pretty huge. And Speed as a dice pool instead of Dex + Athletics is again, a pretty sizable advantage.<br /> <br /> What I like most here is that they are getting away from attribute bonuses in the forms. While it makes sense in Forsaken, it's always a bit of a pain in the ass to track how much Strength or Health you have at any given moment as you transfer between 2-3 forms every fight and then calculating it all back when the last foe drops. Though I will miss (assuming it's gone) 9-again in Dalu/Urshal and 8-again in Gauru. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In the post Stew stated that the attributes of the forms remain unchanged (Urshul is still +2 to all physicals, Gauru is +3 Strength, +1 Dex and +2 Stam, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:12:06-07:00","id":124173,"title":"","content":"A small note/question. Gauru heals all bashing and lethal damage each action, is it safe to assume that also means recovering from all tilts inflicted by said damage as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:13:33-07:00","id":124174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124173#post124173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small note/question. Gauru heals all bashing and lethal damage each action, is it safe to assume that also means recovering from all tilts inflicted by said damage as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much? That's the logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:52:18-07:00","id":124200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124174#post124174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty much? That's the logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just clarifying. You know how people can be with unclarfied rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124127#post124127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said something about not white rooming it, but here I come with a suggestion.<br /> <br /> We do have a Play by Post board. And we have access to a Dice roller -&gt; <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpgroller.com/nwod/</a><br /> It wouldn't be too hard to start up a Werewolf Arena, if someone was particularly interested. We don't know all the rules about werewolf, sure, but the main complaint herein seems to be the combat ability of the forms. It wouldn't be too hard to whip up some humans ranging from lone gangsters to hunter cells and use some existing werewolf write-ups and show your work. You'd probably want to set up an arena, so it wasn't just, well, a white room.</div> </div> </div> </div>White rooms are terrible, yet here I go...<br /> <br /> Assuming an absurdly average shooter (3's in everything), firing at an improbably average Werewolf (3's in everything, save wits which we'll make 2 for the sake of expediation) who has assumed Gauru form yet against all odds is standing around like a dumbass. Here is roughly how long it'll take to gun down said Gauru with silver bullets (all shooters assumed to be within 20 yards with zero cover of any kind):<ul><li><b>Standard Pistol (+1 damage)</b>: Gunner has one die per shot, hitting 30% of the time. Thus, for every 10 shots he'll average 6 damage. So ~19 turns to kill the Gauru, ~15 for Dalu or Urshul.</li> <li><b>Large SMG (+2 damage, Medium Burst)</b>: Gunner now has 3 dice, thanks to the medium burst. 66% chance of hitting for 3 damage, roughly 2 of 3 shots hit. ~11-13 turns for Gauru (don't forget to reload), ~8-9 for Dalu or Urshul.</li> <li><b>Hunting Rifle (+4 damage)</b>: 1 die again, but way more damage, each shot that hits deals 5 or more. Still ~10 turns for Gauru, between ~5-8 for Dalu and Urshul.</li> <li><b>Assault Rifle (+3, Full Auto)</b>: 4 dice, and at least 4 damage on a hit of any sort. At a 75% hit rate, it'll kill in 3-4 turns for Gauru, and 2-4 for Dalu and Urshul.</li> </ul>Naturally, this requires the white room warning. All the above establishes is approximately how long it'll take to gun down a Werewolf with silver in assorted forms given assorted weapons, while he dances about and makes no effort to attack. It does not account for cunning on either the shooter or Werewolf's part, nor does it factor in potential Willpower usage vs Dalu or Urshul (Willpower cannot be used vs Gauru), Gifts, Merits, or other supernatural influences. This will never, ever occur in play, however a few conclusions can reasonably be drawn.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Pistols aren't gonna help you. Even loaded with silver and held by an expert, it's still going to take a several turns for a pistol to put down a Werewolf, in Dalu, Urshul or Gauru form. Mind you it's possible, a skilled shooter with good defense vs a not-so-combat-savy Werewolf can probably win the day, even in close combat. Though we'll have to wait for Death Rage rules to see. However, even then they'll want to bring a bigger gun.</li> <li>Numbers are your friend. Even the biggest weapon, held by a serious expert won't be killing a Gauru wolf in one turn. Not unless he catches them in Hishu or Urhan form. A group of hunters, all firing in unison is a far better option. The sustained fire from different directions will erode the Werewolf's defense and give each subsequent shooter better damaging odds. This is pretty much the only way a group of hunter will be able to bring down a Werewolf in Gauru form. This or one humongous explosion.</li> <li>Ambush is your bigger, better friend. Biggest takeaway, which should be fairly obvious but nevertheless needs to be said, is that a hunters best option is to shoot a Werewolf while she's still a squishy human. Ideally from a safe location she can't cross to in a single turn, with the highest caliber weapon he can find. If the shot is silver, the hunter might just have good odds of putting the wolf down, even if she does hulk out. If it isn't silver...find silver. Gauru is functionally weapon</li> <li><b>Edit</b>: I should note that while this shows a staggering lack of self preservation on the Werewolf's part, the hunter couldn't possibly have a better scenario. In actual play the Werewolf is be guaranteed to be <b>more</b> difficult to kill, barring the introduction of extra shooters, or heavier weaponry. Indeed, I think it'd be safe to say that this above average gunman (3 Dex and 3 Firearms is a pretty good shot), wouldn't be taking down this Werewolf. Not unless he caught it in a lesser form.</li> </ol>Final results are that I'm slightly more okay with the firearms defense now than I was when I read it. It still doesn't do shit vs an ambush, which is really how you want to kill a Werewolf in the first place. Even so, I think it remains an unnecessary addition. Uratha have enough solutions to firearms in their arsenal (Gauru is borderline immune, Urhan can preempt, there are Gifts to shutdown guns altogether, and probably some for armor and environmental manipulation) that they don't need to be dodging bullets. At least not all of them.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: The numbers without bullet dodging, for comparison.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li><b>Standard Pistol (+1 damage)</b>: Gunner has six dice per shot, 88% of the time for 1 success, 61% for 2, and 32% for 3. Even so it'll take ~4-6 turns to kill the Werewolf in Gauru, 3-5 in Dalu or Urshul.</li> <li><b>Large SMG (+2 damage, Medium Burst)</b>: Gunner now has 8 dice, thanks to the medium burst. 94% for 1 success, 77% for 2, 50% for 3, 27% for 4. Average between 3-5 turns for Gauru, 2-4 Dalu and Urshup.</li> <li><b>Hunting Rifle (+4 damage)</b>: Down to 6, 88% of the time for 1 success, 61% for 2, and 32% for 3. Death is likely in 2-3 turns for Gauru, 1-2 for Dalu and Urshul.</li> <li><b>Assault Rifle (+3, Full Auto)</b>: 9 dice. 95% for 1, 82% for 2, 59% for 3, 35% for 4. Averages 2-3 turns against Gauru, 1-3 for Dalu and Urshul.</li> </ul>If at any point the Werewolf got in close combat, which would be quite easy if the hunter is at the range to shoot unpenalized, defense would again apply and we'd be back to the scenario above.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-02-2014, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T20:07:44-07:00","id":124236,"title":"","content":"Out of all these weekly updates this was the one I was most excited for, and I am disappointed. <br /> <br /> The attributes could use some minor alteration, I feel the reason they weren't moved was because every one and their dog wants something different. not a good excuse but understandable.<br /> <br /> Bullet dodge; why? Urshul and Urhan could get behind but Gauru, Dalu and not Urhan. What about Dalu makes the it seem like it can dodge bullets.<br /> <br /> Where's the armour? is it included in the carried over stats?<br /> <br /> Heal all lethal and bashing; wow, making the only option fleeing until Gauru can't be sustained. is there a cool down period between shifting to Gauru. If not whats the point in sticking a time limit on it. I'm sure it will be only once a scene but it's a relevant detail.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T20:20:53-07:00","id":124241,"title":"","content":"I'm just gonna say this: Wait for the merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T21:28:50-07:00","id":124273,"title":"","content":"Off hand, can someone tell me where I can find the Down and Dirty rule? I forgot my thumb drive so can't access my PDF's, but could someone tell me what that mechanically means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T21:32:55-07:00","id":124276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nickpire84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124273#post124273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off hand, can someone tell me where I can find the Down and Dirty rule? I forgot my thumb drive so can't access my PDF's, but could someone tell me what that mechanically means?</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 195 of GMC, condenses the fight down to a declaration of intent and a single contested roll of [combat pool (not factoring in opposing Defense)] vs [combat pool or escape attempt (Strength/Dexterity+Athletics)].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T21:39:55-07:00","id":124279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nickpire84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124273#post124273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off hand, can someone tell me where I can find the Down and Dirty rule? I forgot my thumb drive so can't access my PDF's, but could someone tell me what that mechanically means?</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat boiled down to a single contested action. Both parties roll either a combat dice pool (Strength + Weaponry, Strength + Brawl, Dex + Firearms, Dex + Athletics, etc) or a relevant dice pool for an escape attempt. The losing party takes damage equal to the difference in successes (plus weapon damage) and the winning party achieves what ever their intent was for the combat, which can include killing the losing party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T21:51:23-07:00","id":124284,"title":"","content":"Wow, brutal... but cool. Thank you both!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T01:21:50-07:00","id":124339,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the lot of you complaining about bullet defense are understanding the phrasing... It seems like you think it means werewolves will be instantly bullet proof, but what it actually reads is &quot;Apply FULL defense&quot; meaning THE CHARACTERS DEFENSE. Most Uratha starting in the old set had what... 2 defense or there abouts? With gmc it is probably closer to 4 but thats still not that big of a modifier if the weapon damage dice is significantly higher. <br /> <br /> The only time it looks incredibly op is with the garou form, where it SHOULD be. <br /> <br /> Failing that explanation, Stew wants us to try it out in new games and see how we like them. I'll probably pull up the ol forsaken demo or coyote falls(?) and try out some of the new things. I feel with the new hunting aspect it may go a bit more stealth oriented, something my players wanted. A big problem they have with apocalypse is it always seems to be a fight scenario, or building up to it. Forsaken they liked for being able to explore the atmosphere better.<br /> <br /> Also Ana Mizuki, it is important to note that while the Uratha are not bonded to wolves as the Garou are in apocalypse, their spiritual form is that of the basic wolf. Stew remarked that it is the form of father wolf and the first born, and in the harmony bar when you are too spirit it is closer to the wolf bar. So they aren't so much wolves as they are spirit wolves, meaning they don't have to feel that physical connection (though according to a few of the supporting books some do... -stare towards the lustful and crazy hunters in darkness- ) to the wolves that the garou would. Once they hit the &quot;too wolf&quot; threshold they're stuck hunting in the spirit wilds, unable to leave or control their shifts fully. <br /> <br /> Another note... could an Uratha become a potent enough spirit to become a pack totem?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T01:24:04-07:00","id":124341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124279#post124279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Combat boiled down to a single contested action. Both parties roll either a combat dice pool (Strength + Weaponry, Strength + Brawl, Dex + Firearms, Dex + Athletics, etc) or a relevant dice pool for an escape attempt. The losing party takes damage equal to the difference in successes (plus weapon damage) and the winning party achieves what ever their intent was for the combat, which can include killing the losing party.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gauru always kills the losing party ......<br /> <br /> Plus what is this about ''cannot spend willpower to attack gauru'' thing ? Does anybody know ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T01:29:42-07:00","id":124346,"title":"","content":"I think as people have pointed out its an effect of lunacy. To translate: The opponent is scared shitless of the monster about to eat him. Having the strength of will to do much of anything beyond run is going to be in the extreme 1%.<br /> <br /> Garou form SHOULD always kill the losing party OF LESSER ENEMIES. This does not necessarily apply to hosts, super claimed, Pure tribes, Bale hounds, the ancient ones, and especially the Idigam.<br /> <br /> If you have an Uratha in a grocery store facing off against 5 gang bangers and he goes Garou? They're dead. realistically and now in rule form. But put the same Uratha against a Spider host solo? He's gonna have a hell of a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T01:40:12-07:00","id":124349,"title":"","content":"The defense versus firearns thing doesn't bother me, it seems appropriate to either gun down a werewolf with a master marksman or an entire swat team.<br /> <br /> I'm now picturing a pack that includes a wolfblooded sniper with up to 30 dice to throw with those silver bullets when the shit hits the fan.<br /> <br /> I do wonder why the bite of a werewolf in wolf form is less dangerous than the bite of a werewolf in a barely feral man form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 05-03-2014, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T01:55:13-07:00","id":124357,"title":"","content":"Well feral man form requires a grapple, which probably lends to easier access to hurtful places. Plus the augmented neck and head muscles for bite strength.<br /> <br /> I was a bit confused but that too though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:35:50-07:00","id":124376,"title":"","content":"I wonder what a fight between two werewolves in Gauru looks like. They tear each other to pieces and heal all damage they do to each other every turn, until one of them can't stay in Gauru; at which point the other werewolf dominates the fight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T03:12:11-07:00","id":124392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124376#post124376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what a fight between two werewolves in Gauru looks like. They tear each other to pieces and heal all damage they do to each other every turn, until one of them can't stay in Gauru; at which point the other werewolf dominates the fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine werewolves avoiding gauru in a wolf-on-wolf fight for precisely that reason, outside of an actual hunt (where the hunters use gauru after the quarry's burned through his in desperation). In 'normal' combat I would think that urshul is more of a go-to form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T06:18:34-07:00","id":124440,"title":"","content":"Chris: Probably. I'd still solve it with Down and Dirty, unless someone got potential for Aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T08:31:36-07:00","id":124516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124376#post124376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what a fight between two werewolves in Gauru looks like. They tear each other to pieces and heal all damage they do to each other every turn, until one of them can't stay in Gauru; at which point the other werewolf dominates the fight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, assuming they have no other edges to rely on. Or resort to... heavy handed tactics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T09:41:33-07:00","id":124570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124392#post124392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can imagine werewolves avoiding gauru in a wolf-on-wolf fight for precisely that reason, outside of an actual hunt (where the hunters use gauru after the quarry's burned through his in desperation). In 'normal' combat I would think that urshul is more of a go-to form.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Here's Stew's response for those that haven't seen yet, <i>&quot;It\u2019s a knock-down, drag-out fight like that, yeah. The real trick is to stack on enough damage that you wrap-round from lethal to aggravated, so your opponent can\u2019t regenerate it. Mostly, it comes down to whoever can remain in Gauru longer \u2014 which is either the more experienced, or the one who falls to Kuruth.</i></span></span></span><br /> <i><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">As with War Agains the Pure, I don\u2019t see many werewolf-on-werewolf fights being straight up to the death, even Forsaken/Pure fights. It\u2019s more about demonstrating dominance and power. I see the Pure using powerful spirits when they want to kill, while the Forsaken tool up with silver.&quot;</span></span></span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T11:25:58-07:00","id":124630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xaielao</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124151#post124151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though I will miss (assuming it's gone) 9-again in Dalu/Urshal and 8-again in Gauru. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was never there in the first place. That's a Hack from <i>Mirrors</i>, not a core rule.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T16:36:39-07:00","id":124849,"title":"","content":"After some quick testing I will tentatively rescind some of my concern about the bullet dodging properties, but I'm still generally concerned about Gauru's immense durability.<br /> <br /> The two test scenarios, included a classic encounter between a completely fresh (i.e. 0xp) Werewolf and four middling human hunters with a bit of silver. And a not so classic encounter between the same Werewolf and a tricked out Vampire soldier without any silver. Both can be viewed here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IHEaW4Fx5kDSga2z-0Q9yBd7dUVIzH0n-Wmk0F4qbqo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf vs Plucky Country Folk</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18QKBVuXJKDqE6xOfRkR1RCsPXxc00qppQ9Nx0pK-Nxw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf vs Vampire Super Soldier</a><br /> <br /> The big find, well confirmation really, is that without silver or another source of aggravated damage there odds of killing Gauru in single combat are next to zero. Even in large groups attackers must be extremely well coordinated or their attacks will be healed away like they're nothing. The claims that a Rahu can take on a tank (as in the armored siege weapon) are not BS, it might not even need Gifts...<br /> <br /> At the same time I found the damage from a Werewolf's claws and bite a little lack luster. Claws were offset by heavy clothing, which seems a little weak.<br /> <br /> Suggestions:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>Use the Higher of Wits or Dexterity for defense in Gauru, Urshul and Urhan.</li> <li>Increase claw and bite damage in Gauru to +2 and +4 respectively (being grappled by Gauru should be horrifying).</li> <li>Reduce Gauru Lethal healing to a high, but manageable number. Stamina (including the +2 from Gauru) might do, that'd have had the test Werewolf recovering 5 lethal per action, enough to largely undo the effects of the four hunters, but not totally outpace the combat-monstrosity vampire.</li> <li>Allow controlled rage a little more flexibility with its options. Attacking each turn is fine, but being able to choose who to attack would make the form a lot scarier.</li> </ul><b>Edit: </b>A little bit more testing has revealed Stamina + Primal Urge, makes a werewolf ample durable. That leaves our sample wolf recovering 6 per turn, half her health, and enough to make the Plucky Country Folk scenario play out nearly unchanged. While the Super Soldier scenario ends in 5-6 turns as opposed to the previous ~15.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-04-2014, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T17:05:26-07:00","id":124856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124630#post124630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was never there in the first place. That's a Hack from <i>Mirrors</i>, not a core rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Armory Reloaded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:01:46-07:00","id":124887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124849#post124849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big find, well confirmation really, is that without silver or another source of aggravated damage there odds of killing Gauru in single combat are next to zero. Even in large groups attackers must be extremely well coordinated or their attacks will be healed away like they're nothing. The claims that a Rahu can take on a tank (as in the armored siege weapon) are not BS, it might not even need Gifts...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Looking at your Gauru, it doesn't seem to have renown, are you working off the idea that it's always in gauru? Cause remember he's got a time limit there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:09:55-07:00","id":124889,"title":"","content":"Kuruth would allow for a much more extended time of frame there, as Stew mentioned in the comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:26:39-07:00","id":124897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124887#post124887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Looking at your Gauru, it doesn't seem to have renown, are you working off the idea that it's always in gauru? Cause remember he's got a time limit there.</div> </div> </div> </div> This was exclusively a test of Gauru and Gauru alone. I did not give it Gifts or Merits, nothing beyond Gauru. In scenarios like this too many factors complicate conclusion. So while I cannot conclude anything about Gifts I can say confidently the Werewolf in those examples can only get stronger. Still I was kinda assuming two dots of primary renown, I'll make a note of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:32:05-07:00","id":124901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124349#post124349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The defense versus firearns thing doesn't bother me, it seems appropriate to either gun down a werewolf with a master marksman or an entire swat team.<br /> <br /> I'm now picturing a pack that includes a wolfblooded sniper with up to 30 dice to throw with those silver bullets when the shit hits the fan.<br /> <br /> I do wonder why the bite of a werewolf in wolf form is less dangerous than the bite of a werewolf in a barely feral man form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as how Marksmanship has been nerfed to the ground. I don't know how you'd get anymore than 20 dice before the penalties let alone after them and this is after two turns of waiting while your friends get murdered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T19:47:39-07:00","id":124921,"title":"","content":"So far the only suggestion I'd make is to give Urshal +1 to its bite to keep it in line with the wolf form granted by Protean (and presumably a regular non-supernatural wolf). I like everything else I've seen so far. The new form benefits go a long way toward alleviating the &quot;meh&quot; feeling I got from the new Gift structure. It's not that they were bad, just not something that really piqued my interest like the shape-shifting changes have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 05-03-2014, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T19:59:27-07:00","id":124927,"title":"","content":"Urshul already gives +1 lethal with a bite. I assume you meant Urhan, which Stew has said will be changed to +1 lethal to bring it into line with mortal wolves (and shapeshifted vampires).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T11:11:10-07:00","id":125244,"title":"","content":"For the most part I definitely like the changes, but I echo the people saying that the full Defense against ranged attacks is a little dodgy (ha!). I understand the intent, but I think there must be better ways to make them tougher to take down with massed fire. I am also not fond of the idea of their primary weakness being easy to cancel out by creating a dodge-monster character. Was innate armour considered as an alternative?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T00:27:12-07:00","id":125614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124927#post124927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urshul already gives +1 lethal with a bite. I assume you meant Urhan, which Stew has said will be changed to +1 lethal to bring it into line with mortal wolves (and shapeshifted vampires).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, mixed up the terms. First tongue isn't even my fourth language, much less my first. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T01:15:53-07:00","id":125632,"title":"","content":"I would have preferred a less limited time and berserk only Gauru without the extreme regeneration....<br /> <br /> I do appreciate the fact that it is HARD to make the forms all have a purpose and that limiting Gauru form is one way ro achieve it, but still...<br /> <br /> Well, I still think the regeneration should be more like &quot;regenerate lethal instead of bashing without spending essence&quot; or such (simply because it scales instead of being a blanket maximum regeneration) and I also would say a Gauru VS Gauru fight just looks unfun now, however, I think I already am out by now.<br /> <br /> I can appreciate the effort put into the Idigam chronicle but I think both the flavour and the rules will be even farther from the kind of werewolf game I hoped for than before.<br /> <br /> So all I can comment on by now is whether there is any clunky mechanic that grates with the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T01:54:19-07:00","id":125644,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to echo the Gauru vs Gauru concern, though without seeing Gifts one can't really be certain.<br /> <br /> However, I can safely surmise that two Werewolves going at it in Gauru are unlikely to deal one another <b>any </b>lasting damage. The bare minimum one would have to deal in a single strike is 11 lethal, and that's versus a Werewolf with one dot of Stamina. That goes beyond a statistical improbability and approaches impossibility.<br /> <br /> Again, Gifts and Kuruth aren't factored, but unless Kuruth adds a boatload of damage (I'm talking 5+) then there's just no way two non-combat spec Gauru are hurting one another.<br /> <br /> I'll probably test that next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T04:41:09-07:00","id":125716,"title":"","content":"As I've said before, disclaimer that I am not the person writing the forms stuff.<br /> <br /> However, I <i>think</i> the thing of two non-combat-spec Gauru battering each other with no lasting damage <i>if it's just a combat</i> <i>between the two of them for some reason</i> is a feature not a bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T05:39:24-07:00","id":125739,"title":"","content":"Hmh, but, how about bringing another Gauru, possibly in Kurruth down?<br /> Gauru VS Gauru means you likely have to kill him (I assume werewolves still are dead at full aggravated?), just making him collapse might not work depending on whether they fall down at full lethal or not, wrestling them down would be hard since that would need Gauru too to accomplish (and holding someone down without maiming him might mean you keep rolling not to enter Kurruth yourself), though Urshul MIGHt work perhaps?<br /> <br /> It does depend on the effect you want, as it stands, it is a VERY hefty upgrade right from the start with some drawbacks...<br /> <br /> As I said, I would be happier with less upgrade and less drawbacks...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T05:58:03-07:00","id":125749,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that your gauru vs gauru discussion is not factoring in klaives or combat-assisting gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:08:40-07:00","id":125771,"title":"","content":"Regardless of what happens, know that we fixed some stuff before it even made it into the book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We rock! We are having them do a modifier to Urhan form, having them look into rules for Urhan pre-empting other pre-emp effects from other creatures, having them look into the Urshul -1 penalty effects, possibly having the wolf forms use higher or wits or dex for defense, a potential rebalancing of all claw/bite traits in all forms, and maybe gaining +1 to Hishu perception<br /> <br /> Whew","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:13:59-07:00","id":125773,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Gauru on Gauru action (don't judge me!) As to my thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. I like the idea of no lasting damage... most of the time. I'm expecting that Kuruth will fix that right up, though, as the other guy runs out of time and is quickly eviscerated / freaks out and Kuruth's as well (but what happens then??)<br /> <br /> 2. I REALLY want to know what Kuruth will do! I feel like it would really matter to this discussion.<br /> <br /> 3. I'm looking forward to your white-rooming, PenDragon. I'm hoping that it will at least be possible for someone to be grievously wounded some of the time, even if it's a rare and tragic accident.<br /> <br /> 4. Good point, Ray White, about it looking like Gauru will NOT pass out when they fill up on Lethal (since give them a few seconds and it will all be gone.) That means no more &quot;take a big hit, lose consciousness, die when your wounds wrap around&quot; anymore (or at least not if they're in Gauru.) Interesting.<br /> <br /> 5. It certainly does seem like more damage output may be in order. I understand that Gifts can bump it up but to me, tearing someone in two in Gauru form shouldn't be the province of Gifts.<br /> <br /> 6. Lastly, back on Kuruth (also, KURUTH! We needs it!), it certainly does seem like you can't just try to hold a raging packmate down and try to knock him out / wait it out, anymore. This is interesting, and I'm not sure how I feel about it. On one hand, it does feel very anticlimactic (&quot;oh, Bob's gone mad again; just sit on him for a few minutes and he'll be right as rain&quot;), but on the other hand - one bad roll and AN UNSTOPPABLE, UNKILLABLE SOAK-MONSTER will be unleashed. Which leads me onto...<br /> <br /> 7. Kuruth! Again. For good measure. Please vote Kuruth, people! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:18:24-07:00","id":125777,"title":"","content":"With the damage healing, how does that effect Tilts that are the result of such damage? Arm Wreck or Stunned as the result of a blow to the head of a can of mace? Do they go away when damage is healed? What about the mace? since it doesn't actually cause damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2903-disper42","name":"Disper42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:30:13-07:00","id":125787,"title":"","content":"Not on the immediate topic, but I saw some griping about Urhan not being very useful except for running. Not sure if anyone pointed this out already, but it's also the form with the highest Perception and speed, so it's going to be a good form for tracking, which is, y'know, kind of important for hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:32:40-07:00","id":125790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125716#post125716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've said before, disclaimer that I am not the person writing the forms stuff.<br /> <br /> However, I <i>think</i> the thing of two non-combat-spec Gauru battering each other with no lasting damage <i>if it's just a combat</i> <i>between the two of them for some reason</i> is a feature not a bug.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is certainly a striking image: Two wolf-man abominations, futilely trying to tear each other apart, but their wounds healing almost faster than they are dealt... and then about a minute later, they are two exhausted men, heaving from lack of breath, still trying to punch each other to death with the last of their strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:43:04-07:00","id":125797,"title":"","content":"Actually, that has happened in several movies now that I think on it. Two werewolves fighting it out usually leads to the more experienced(powerful) one winning, or an outside force jumping in. Of equal level and it usually has the clawing at each other and coming to a stalemate.<br /> Wow, I can see Forsaken going ham over Silver Jaws now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T07:45:10-07:00","id":125799,"title":"","content":"Two werewolves tearing into each other in the warform and not doing lasting damage is not a feature in my eyes. I understand that it's not smart to hunt the Pure my taking them on one on one, but I want there to be a chance for two werewolves to actually do damage to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T08:04:00-07:00","id":125811,"title":"","content":"Who say's there's no chance of them doing lasting damage to each other?<br /> <br /> You're looking at a very limited part of the system, two perfect-stat characters just attacking each other with a standard attack. It's hardly indicative of the whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-05-2014, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T08:12:14-07:00","id":125816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125799#post125799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two werewolves tearing into each other in the warform and not doing lasting damage is not a feature in my eyes. I understand that it's not smart to hunt the Pure my taking them on one on one, but I want there to be a chance for two werewolves to actually do damage to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I actually kind of like this. Brings out the futility of the brother against brother feud between the Forsaken and the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T08:24:12-07:00","id":125821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125799#post125799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two werewolves tearing into each other in the warform and not doing lasting damage is not a feature in my eyes. I understand that it's not smart to hunt the Pure my taking them on one on one, but I want there to be a chance for two werewolves to actually do damage to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of chance for two werewolves to do lasting damage to each other. Note that, as I was talking about, 'two non-combat-spec Gauru battering each other' is not the time wherein they're likely to achieve that.<br /> <br /> They're quite likely to trash a lot of their surroundings and any poor bastard hapless enough to get caught up in the fight, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T08:55:01-07:00","id":125832,"title":"","content":"It does set up some really nice visuals, though, for hot-blooded fights for dominance (while not being fatal, and thus weakening the pack)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:13:04-07:00","id":125855,"title":"","content":"On Gauru vs Gauru, I can bet that Rage gifts fucks them up quite badly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:17:35-07:00","id":125857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125811#post125811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who say's there's no chance of them doing lasting damage to each other?<br /> <br /> You're looking at a very limited part of the system, two perfect-stat characters just attacking each other with a standard attack. It's hardly indicative of the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, after having done the math.<br /> <br /> The problem with the current setup, given the limited information we have, a white room combat between two werewolves is a challenge about how long individual fighters get to stay in the war form; the first one to take any other form loses. I find that to be uninteresting.<br /> <br /> I urge anyone who'd like to test that theory to run a fight scene using the GMC systems and the spoilers we've been given so far.<br /> <br /> Frankly; these rules need some serious playtesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:22:07-07:00","id":125867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125855#post125855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Gauru vs Gauru, I can bet that Rage gifts fucks them up quite badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this option for the &quot;bro vs bro&quot; issue, too. It makes them put in the effort to hurt one another. Shows who's really pissed off the most and who's truly (dis)honoring their parents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:27:25-07:00","id":125872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125857#post125857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly; these rules need some serious playtesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed - that's the point of playtesting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd still caution 