Kuruth focused on less squishy targets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:35:06-07:00","id":125881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125872#post125872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed - that's the point of playtesting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd still caution against pure white-rooming, though. If you want, I can go through a sample set-up for a werewolf vs werewolf fight that may provide some context for the various factors that can affect such a combat, although obviously there'll be limits on the factors I can include due to not all the Gifts being spoiled yet, Merits, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be nice, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T09:47:00-07:00","id":125892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125872#post125872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed - that's the point of playtesting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd still caution against pure white-rooming, though. If you want, I can go through a sample set-up for a werewolf vs werewolf fight that may provide some context for the various factors that can affect such a combat, although obviously there'll be limits on the factors I can include due to not all the Gifts being spoiled yet, Merits, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, given Tilts aren't gonna be in that equation (much like in B&amp;S), I dunno how it wouldn't be a white-room scenario with a nice room description. I do hope I'm wrong, tho.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124849#post124849\">Look's experimental playtest</a> and his suggestions are pretty amazing IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-05-2014, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:18:54-07:00","id":125926,"title":"","content":"I think most of the detractors from garous new buff are really over thinking it. Given the limitation of the form (time limits and all) I doubt that the garou is the go to for garou combat. Probably more for keeping aggro during that sort of white room fight.<br /> <br /> And honestly how often do you see an even match up between garou forms in SISKUR DA? You probably wont. The only time i see a canceling out of werewolf forms is if its a strait duel or dominance brawl, or keeping a pure opponent busy. So you have a pure opponent come after you who garous, your pack mate takes the garou and keeps him busy knowing full well you'll get eviscerated by his claws, so he takes the time to wait till his form shifts down, then you take the garou and take him out.<br /> <br /> You're really worrying about a few seconds in combat, that if you did the hunt right you probably shouldn't encounter.<br /> <br /> Not to mention gifts and proper speccing.<br /> <br /> Or the time limit and possible limit per day that may well come with it, there is no guarantee that all Uratha will be able to take garou at the moment of convenience. Some trigger happy pup will blow it way to easily.<br /> <br /> Again, as it has been said, white rooming DOES NOT help with this. You need to have real world application with these abilities. I personally love the healing for solving inter-tribal/pack conflict. Means you won't kill your best friend accidentally in war form (Fenris ban aside).<br /> <br /> I think what the detractors are doing is looking at the healing factor, ignoring the limiters (and the fact that people have been wanting a USEFUL war form for a while now) and thinking of worst case scenario for the werewolf. Vampires got a buff why shouldn't we? Let's enjoy this and thing of the proper uses for the form. Its to quickly dispatch foes. Would you rather you were able to eat damage entirely for 20 seconds and make the form useless for its purpose? You already have a hell of a time using weapons or thinking power in Garou, just take the physical might and supernatural power that goes with it. It's why theres a time limit after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:26:03-07:00","id":125933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125872#post125872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed - that's the point of playtesting! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd still caution against pure white-rooming, though. If you want, I can go through a sample set-up for a werewolf vs werewolf fight that may provide some context for the various factors that can affect such a combat, although obviously there'll be limits on the factors I can include due to not all the Gifts being spoiled yet, Merits, etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you or another writer could provide insight to this. For playtesting, do the writers do this? Or do other people do the playtest and give the results back to the writers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:29:44-07:00","id":125937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125926#post125926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's enjoy this and thing of the proper uses for the form. Its to quickly dispatch foes. Would you rather you were able to eat damage entirely for 20 seconds and make the form useless for its purpose? You already have a hell of a time using weapons or thinking power in Garou, just take the physical might and supernatural power that goes with it. It's why theres a time limit after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Ignoring the problem doesn't really deal with the inherent issues.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that this will be fixed once the game is in its playtesting phase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:32:08-07:00","id":125939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125926#post125926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most of the detractors from <b>Gauru</b> new buff are really over thinking it. Given the limitation of the form (time limits and all) I doubt that the garou is the go to for <b>Uratha</b> combat. Probably more for keeping aggro during that sort of white room fight.<br /> <br /> And honestly how often do you see an even match up between <b>Uratha</b> forms in <i>Siskur-Dah</i>? You probably wont. The only time i see a canceling out of werewolf forms is if its a strait duel or dominance brawl, or keeping a pure opponent busy. So you have a pure opponent come after you who <b>Gaurus</b>, your pack mate takes the <b>Gauru</b> and keeps him busy knowing full well you'll get eviscerated by his claws, so he takes the time to wait till his form shifts down, then you take the <b>Gauru</b> and take him out.<br /> <br /> You're really worrying about a few seconds in combat, that if you did the hunt right you probably shouldn't encounter.<br /> <br /> Not to mention gifts and proper speccing.<br /> <br /> Or the time limit and possible limit per day that may well come with it, there is no guarantee that all Uratha will be able to take garou at the moment of convenience. Some trigger happy pup will blow it way to easily.<br /> <br /> Again, as it has been said, white rooming DOES NOT help with this. You need to have real world application with these abilities. I personally love the healing for solving inter-tribal/pack conflict. Means you won't kill your best friend accidentally in war form (Fenris ban aside).<br /> <br /> I think what the detractors are doing is looking at the healing factor, ignoring the limiters (and the fact that people have been wanting a USEFUL war form for a while now) and thinking of worst case scenario for the werewolf. Vampires got a buff why shouldn't we? Let's enjoy this and thing of the proper uses for the form. Its to quickly dispatch foes. Would you rather you were able to eat damage entirely for 20 seconds and make the form useless for its purpose? You already have a hell of a time using weapons or thinking power in Garou, just take the physical might and supernatural power that goes with it. It's why theres a time limit after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrections aside (excuse my OCD), you raise some good points.<br /> <br /> To add to the above, If I was playing an Elodoth setting the terms to a combat challenge, I'd do it at first blood, or outright forbid participants from taking the Gauru form. That form is for killing, not to hold a challenge.<br /> <br /> Then you have to consider that several Gaurus against a single one (usual pack tactic) <b>will</b> likely give aggravated wounds to their victim, while being imperious to the poor sap's pack attempts to save him, unless they're packing Silver, for example. And why bother taking gauru in that situation? Go Urshul, deplete the fucker's defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:36:17-07:00","id":125943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125881#post125881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be nice, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll hammer something together. Can't guarantee when I'll have it done, but it'll turn up in this thread at some point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:43:21-07:00","id":125946,"title":"","content":"And let's not forget that gauru, while near impossible to dammage whitout a way deal aggravated are far from unstoppable.<br /> For one they aren't that much better at fighting. A 1 die difference over urshul isn't going to help them much. For second there are way to stop a rampaging gaurur that do not involve damage. It is a very good defensive form, and a good offensive form against mooks, but it's not the end all be all of werewolf combat.<br /> <br /> Now for the results of playtesting in an actual game session.<br /> Forms used: Urhan, Urshul and Gauru.<br /> <br /> Urhan now has some use that is not negated by having partial change, I am delighted by this. The ability to use speed for foot pursuit and the pseudo celerity means very few things are going to be able to escape or catch a werewolf in urhan. The pseudo celerity is nicely balanced by the lack of opposable thumbs, limiting the way it can be abused.<br /> <br /> Urshul: I suspect the ability of urshul to lower the defense of an enemy semi permanently to be quite deadly with a full pack, but since I was the only werewolf around it was of very limited use. I've seen people wonder about someone getting back their defense if they can escape/catch their breath/heal. To which I'd like to remind that the defense lowering happens for a scene, if someone manage to escape a pack of werewolves and catch their breath it would be something I'd consider to be a different scene. I do wonder about supernatural instant healing though.<br /> <br /> I was facing a gunman and the ST was nice enough to not make the bullet silver or I would have been in great trouble. That guy must have had a massive dice pool because he never missed me. So the whole defense against firearms things tell me that it changed things a little from guns being absolutly terrifying to only be scary in the hands of a trained professional. I'm okay with that.<br /> <br /> Gauru: So the bad guy couldn't hurt me anymore. But I had a very hard time hitting him. The dice did not agree with me that night. Using willpower and everything I could squeeze I still failed to hit a couple times in a row. So while Gauru is powerful defensively, offensively it's not that much better than urshul. Which lend me to think that Gauru is the form you take in one of two situations.<br /> First the fight isn't that critical and you just need to mop up whitout wanting to worry about losing health. Or it's a very important fight and you use Gauru to weaken the opposition whitout exposing yourself too much. You face a super dangerous enemy, a boss of sort, and you need the near invincibility to ensure you can survive long enough to take the enemy down.<br /> <br /> Will post more once I get the chance to see the special ability of Dalu/hishu in action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:51:41-07:00","id":125955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125943#post125943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll hammer something together. Can't guarantee when I'll have it done, but it'll turn up in this thread at some point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Appreciated, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:53:30-07:00","id":125957,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm full of typos this morning (also procrastinating on writing something on Adrianople for my history class), but thaaaaat mess aside...<br /> <br /> I hadn't thought about the new implimentation of Elodoth's moon abilities. One could preside over a duel and adjudicate far easier now. Hell you could set the rule to the first one to Kuruth and the Elodoth can bring him out of it. <br /> <br /> And it isn't ignoring issues. To bring in the comparison across werewolf splats, the Crinos form from werewolf the apocalypse was stupidly strong, had no limiter and was the general go to for anything werewolf fight. What we have for Garou is a war form now that we can use in dire circumstances, and not just for the basic things. What you see as issues I see as a breath of fresh air.<br /> <br /> Remember they are trying to make each form iconic to werewolf fiction (be it movies or books) and so the big man wolf form should be nigh unstoppable for however brief you're able to have it. The dire wolf form also reminds me of American Werewolf in London for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T10:59:11-07:00","id":125963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125957#post125957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it isn't ignoring issues. To bring in the comparison across werewolf splats, the Crinos form from werewolf the apocalypse was stupidly strong, had no limiter and was the general go to for anything werewolf fight. What we have for Garou is a war form now that we can use in dire circumstances, and not just for the basic things. What you see as issues I see as a breath of fresh air.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know how Apocalypse is in any way relevant here. I'm comparing Forsaken's Gauru and Idigam Chronicle's Gauru, and I find the latter not my taste compared to the old Gauru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125957#post125957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember they are trying to make each form iconic to werewolf fiction (be it movies or books) and so the big man wolf form should be nigh unstoppable for however brief you're able to have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No disagreement here. My issue is with the inherent boringness of two unstoppable monsters canceling each other out until one of them runs out of turns of unstoppableness. I'm confident that playtest will fix this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:05:20-07:00","id":125972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125963#post125963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No disagreement here. My issue is with the inherent boringness of two unstoppable monsters canceling each other out until one of them runs out of turns of unstoppableness. I'm confident that playtest will fix this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see it as an issue honestly. If the goal of the conflict is not to murder the other werewolf you don't want to take Gauru anyway because you don't want to risk Kuruth. And if you do want to murder the other werewolf you're going to be using a mean to deal aggravated damage anyway to avoid dragging the fight on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:10:36-07:00","id":125975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125972#post125972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you do want to murder the other werewolf you're going to be using a mean to deal aggravated damage anyway to avoid dragging the fight on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem right there. I want werewolves (not packs of werewolves - I understand that, when hunting a werewolf, it's smart to do so in a pack - I was the first one to point out that fact in this thread) - to be able to kill each other in combat, without combat being boring.<br /> <br /> If you've got two werewolves in the form of war and rage and death, and the next couple combat turns are entirely meaningless because they're not going to do any damage that lasts, then I find that to be boring, from a game point of view.<br /> <br /> You roll. You do damage.<br /> The opponent rolls. He does some damage.<br /> You both heal your entire damage.<br /> Repeat until someone runs out of Gauru turns.<br /> <br /> Not my idea of an interesting scenario. I will be surprised if that kind of thing makes it into the final version of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:10:57-07:00","id":125977,"title":"","content":"Is silver claws still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:11:57-07:00","id":125978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125963#post125963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't know how Apocalypse is in any way relevant here. I'm comparing Forsaken's Gauru and Idigam Chronicle's Gauru, and I find the latter not my taste compared to the old Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do understand where you are coming from, the problem with the old Gauru was that Urshul was almost superior in every single way. Yes, 1 less health and strength with no natural armor, but they had no time limit, could think and use all types of tactics, and even solve the armor problem with a nice little armor fetish courtesy of an Ithaeur. Yes, on paper the Gauru form was slightly stronger, but the downfalls more than compensated it in favor of Urshul<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125963#post125963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No disagreement here. My issue is with the inherent boringness of two unstoppable monsters canceling each other out until one of them runs out of turns of unstoppableness. I'm confident that playtest will fix this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel that this, while it CAN be a scenario, I do not think it is going to be the case very often. Very rarely would I ever imagine an Uratha going off on his own and pound away at another Uratha in Gauru form for a 1v1 fight to the death. If I want to murder the other Werewolf, I am going to bring a pack, ambush them, use silver, or all 3. Even if the event does happen, then why should that exact event not happen? Two are utilizing the most powerful forms to maul each other, and the best one will be left standing at the end...even if it does take a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:16:32-07:00","id":125982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125978#post125978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I do understand where you are coming from, the problem with the old Gauru was that Urshul was almost superior in every single way. Yes, 1 less health and strength with no natural armor, but they had no time limit, could think and use all types of tactics, and even solve the armor problem with a nice little armor fetish courtesy of an Ithaeur. Yes, on paper the Gauru form was slightly stronger, but the downfalls more than compensated it in favor of Urshul</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree!<br /> <br /> I really don't think allowing Gauru werewolves to heal all bashing and lethal damage every turn is the right fix to this problem, however. It's turning Gauru into something that I find to be boring, quite frankly. And a war for that's boring is the last thing this game wants to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125978#post125978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that this, while it CAN be a scenario, I do not think it is going to be the case very often. Very rarely would I ever imagine an Uratha going off on his own and pound away at another Uratha in Gauru form for a 1v1 fight to the death. If I want to murder the other Werewolf, I am going to bring a pack, ambush them, use silver, or all 3. Even if the event does happen, then why should that exact event not happen? Two are utilizing the most powerful forms to maul each other, and the best one will be left standing at the end...even if it does take a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had lots and lots of duels in all of my Werewolf games, for all sorts of reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:22:19-07:00","id":125989,"title":"","content":"Who said you can't have duels? I simply think Gauru form is the wrong form to use for it as most of the time you won't be trying to kill them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:22:33-07:00","id":125991,"title":"","content":"Were they all done barehanded without any willpower or all-out attacks or grapples or gifts or shapechanging?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:33:49-07:00","id":126006,"title":"","content":"Let us not forget that duels can vary from tribe to tribe. Garou v Garou would probably be a Blood Talon deal, where as a Bone Shadow duel would more likely be a test of hisil knowledge or spirit workings.<br /> <br /> The apocalypse ref. harkens back to some of the original complaints that garou form was not crinos. People want to be an unstoppable monster in that form. As I recall a big stopping point for cwod players converting over was a lack of power in the werewolf.<br /> <br /> But again, I am so far perfectly fine with the changes. I was very skeptical at first as change for things I like usually wind up being bad, but these changes are imo best for the game line and its continuing longevity. Maybe with these slight redesigns we will one day see a Forsaken 20th release.<br /> <br /> edit: Feel I should mention I'm not trying to be contrary to you Christian, more over I love your story hook suggestions. I do honestly feel these changes are for the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 05-05-2014, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T11:43:59-07:00","id":126014,"title":"","content":"I'm glad some of you people like the changes. More power to you!<br /> <br /> I think they're not very well thought out, respectfully. I expect to see them changed as the playtest phase starts - Stew's comments clearly show that many things are still bound to change and evolve until the release of the books. And if not, that's cool too - I don't really use the official system for these games, and I already have a system that I'm very happy with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:02:14-07:00","id":126027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125975#post125975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the problem right there. I want werewolves (not packs of werewolves - I understand that, when hunting a werewolf, it's smart to do so in a pack - I was the first one to point out that fact in this thread) - to be able to kill each other in combat, without combat being boring.<br /> <br /> If you've got two werewolves in the form of war and rage and death, and the next couple combat turns are entirely meaningless because they're not going to do any damage that lasts, then I find that to be boring, from a game point of view.<br /> <br /> You roll. You do damage.<br /> The opponent rolls. He does some damage.<br /> You both heal your entire damage.<br /> Repeat until someone runs out of Gauru turns.<br /> <br /> Not my idea of an interesting scenario. I will be surprised if that kind of thing makes it into the final version of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although true when both Werewolves are in Gauru I think in a non white-room scenario things might play out a bit differently. Let me try to explain:<br /> Gauru due to the generation offers effectively two advantages 1. It is a quick mid-battle full heal 2. Due to regen you can (in some cases) ignore defense to go full out on offense, the biggest drawback is the limited time. Sure in the other forms there is also regen but that is unless spending essence (which is limited) only bashing. <br /> <br /> \u200bSo what I think will happen is that both werewolves start out in Urshul eventually one or the other will need to shift to Gauru either to heal or it is the only way to damage the other party in both cases the other parties best options is to stay in Urshul and use his actions to dodge for a couple of turn before turning himself Gauru which will virtually guarantee* that he will be the one outlasting the one who shifted first.<br /> <br /> So with two closely matched Werewolves it will be a tense first couple of turns seeing who will out damage the other after which one has to switch to Gauru or be out of the fight anyway followed by another tense two or three turns to see if the other one is capable of surviving the onslaught and after that it is followed by your example but in that case the fight should already be effectively over (a couple of turns later the first one to shift shift back and is murdered).<br /> <br /> Note that this does not include any gifts/rituals or other aid and assumes it is a duel to the death (which imho should be pretty rare, other type of duel can and should be more common)<br /> <br /> <br /> *If you shifted because you are out of health or shifted because otherwise you didn't enough damage you are in all likelihood also the weaker opponent and thus have probably less turns of Gauru (the other options it is a fluke and in the case of relative evenly matched probably means equal turns in which case shifting first is also a loosing strategy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2735-dutch_wolf","name":"Dutch_Wolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:30:25-07:00","id":126048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125963#post125963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue is with the inherent boringness of two unstoppable monsters canceling each other out until one of them runs out of turns of unstoppableness. I'm confident that playtest will fix this issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>My fix is simple, let them contest eachother with Down and Dirty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T12:42:52-07:00","id":126060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=125799#post125799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two werewolves tearing into each other in the warform and not doing lasting damage is not a feature in my eyes. I understand that it's not smart to hunt the Pure my taking them on one on one, but I want there to be a chance for two werewolves to actually do damage to each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were a Uratha hunting Pure I sure wouldn't go mano a mano with them. I would use silver, lots of silver and maybe a form that allows use for it. If I were a Pure I would call in a big nasty spirit and watch the carnage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:11:59-07:00","id":126094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dutch_Wolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126027#post126027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bSo what I think will happen is that both werewolves start out in Urshul eventually one or the other will need to shift to Gauru either to heal or it is the only way to damage the other party in both cases the other parties best options is to stay in Urshul and use his actions to dodge for a couple of turn before turning himself Gauru which will virtually guarantee* that he will be the one outlasting the one who shifted first.<br /> <br /> So with two closely matched Werewolves it will be a tense first couple of turns seeing who will out damage the other after which one has to switch to Gauru or be out of the fight anyway followed by another tense two or three turns to see if the other one is capable of surviving the onslaught and after that it is followed by your example but in that case the fight should already be effectively over (a couple of turns later the first one to shift shift back and is murdered).<br /> <br /> *If you shifted because you are out of health or shifted because otherwise you didn't enough damage you are in all likelihood also the weaker opponent and thus have probably less turns of Gauru (the other options it is a fluke and in the case of relative evenly matched probably means equal turns in which case shifting first is also a loosing strategy)</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember however that the healing comes at the START of the following turn, not the end of the current turn. This makes it so using it as a midway battle heal is risky. If the opponent goes after you, they still have a turn to deal sticking damage before the Gauru heal kicks in, and if they go in front of you, then it is still the case except they have 2 attacks to do it.<br /> <br /> This means the Werewolf would need to realize very quickly that they are in over their head and either GTFO, or shapeshift quickly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:38:48-07:00","id":126109,"title":"","content":"Start of the whole turn, from the top of the Initiative order, or at the start of the character's own turn, tho?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T13:44:19-07:00","id":126114,"title":"","content":"Do we know if the new rules are keeping the old regeneration rules timing intact to even address that point yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T14:13:56-07:00","id":126134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126114#post126114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we know if the new rules are keeping the old regeneration rules timing intact to even address that point yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, no idea, that was by the assumption of how regeneration currently works. As it currently works, it would be from the end of the Uratha's turn, to the beginning of his next turn. All the people that go in between those 2 time frames have a chance to make damage stick","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T14:40:10-07:00","id":126149,"title":"","content":"Just completed playtest #3, wherein an Irraka, fully equipped with Gifts and Renown drawn from spoilers, and in en environment where those Gifts are highly effective, attempts to bring down a Pure wolf in Kuruth before he can escape and massacre nearby innocents. The fight is long, really long, and provides the Irraka an overwhelming advantage in many situations. The fight factors in a number of damage dealing and disabling factors to substitute for extra pack-mates. Even so the Pure wolf remains bonkers difficult to bring down.<br /> <br /> While reading this I'd remind everyone to keep in mind that this is a Pure werewolf with zero advantages beyond superior combat statistics (of which defense isn't factored and health is average at best), in actual play it would likely be even harder for Irraka to make a meaningful dent.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kLuhUUHw8J23-Vn1Q0KpnWAoR6lbxAwqt8QpfZJfm4g/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Gauru Fight Test: Little Shop of Horros</a><br /> <br /> As I state at the end of the doc, I think Gauru might currently be simultaneously too durable and too weak. Tweaking it to be a little harder hitting, while making it slightly less invulnerable (just slightly) would likely help the form remain terrifying in combat without becoming boring. Gifts and Merits can easily fill for those who want to be truly invulnerable.<br /> <br /> <b>Suggestions: </b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Basically unchanged:<ul><li>Higher of Wits or Dex to defense</li> <li>Claw and Bite to +2 and +4</li> <li>Gauru healing to [Stamina + Primal Urge] Lethal per turn.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T15:25:48-07:00","id":126175,"title":"","content":"As far as their silly toughness goes, how about taking a lesson from Demon? While in Gauru they count as having Primal Urge 10 for the purpose of regeneration. Bashing damage should be absolutely no problem then still, but Lethal still at least requires a token Essence to heal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T15:51:23-07:00","id":126196,"title":"","content":"what if the essence heal was an automatic thing while in garou, and the healing of lethal only lasted so long as one had essence? I.e. char has 4 essence but 6 turns in garou. He only max heals for 4 turns.<br /> <br /> I'd like to think kuruth would negate that though, so one would heal automatically with kuruth no matter what. just to keep death rage a scary thing.<br /> <br /> I'm am up for a boost in damage though. Or causing a bleed effect. But then the down and dirty combat negates the need for any of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 05-05-2014, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:06:43-07:00","id":126210,"title":"","content":"As I've suggested, in terms of healing Stamina (modified by Gauru form) + Primal Urge is a pretty solid number. It means that even the most frail, newborn wolflet will pull back 4 lethal per turn. And that's an abnormally frail Werewolf. The ones in my tests so far would have healed between 6-8 lethal. Even with just 4 that doesn't make the Werewolf easy to kill, an attacker would still have to stack up 11 damage, with each turn stripping 4 away, while also struggling with other external factors (Werewolf attacks, packmates, environmental concerns, his own objectives).<br /> <br /> As it is now a well armored character with a good dodge number could overtake that rate, but if damage were bumped up a bit then there'd be more reliance on dodge rolls and hobbling attacks (Legwrack, blinding shots, knockdown, etc.) which would in turn reduce the damage and thus make it harder to surpass that 4 lethal/turn. <br /> <br /> As for Death Rage, I think Gauru is durable enough, even with suggested debuffs. I'd rather see Kuruth do something serious to the damage output, like double it. So 3 successes on a claw attack would deal 8 lethal, though that bump might be too extreme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T16:40:11-07:00","id":126243,"title":"","content":"I do see the real concerns here - but as a small voice of dissent, the great thing the impregnability of Garou does is encourage all out attacks - fighting berserk with no need for defense - which feels pretty monstrous to me.<br /> <br /> Hmmm. Did I see a houserule somewhere that damage to the head could be upgraded in severity? So headshots/throatshots - suffering the dice-penaltyif these upgraded to aggravated - could be a viable tactic - the only viable tactic, perhaps - to take down a raging wolf? Perhaps I misremember.<br /> <br /> And without knowledge of how Kuruth works, this is still partial. We are assuming a) Kuruth gets all of the benefits of Garou, and b) that the risk of Kuruth is worth surviving for.<br /> <br /> Possibly - one wraparound agg is enough to send the Kuruth into Flight instead of Fight (although I like my wolves angrier than that). Or possibly the risk is worse: every time in Kuruth you go missing for days (thus throwing the plot development to that point) - and also killing your family (read: Primal urge in social merits), packmembers or a schoolyard.<br /> <br /> I am not sure how these would play out, of course - and I acknowledge that with this healing a lot of the threat is negated - and threat is the key to dramatic tension. But of course, death is not the worst thing to fear, in much werewolf fiction, it is often craved. Making Kuruth so dark that it is never an attractive option - something like how cover is lost when Demons go loud - could add the tension to the stories again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","user":"hoodedclaw","date":". 05-05-2014, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T18:42:58-07:00","id":126321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126149#post126149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Suggestions: </b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Basically unchanged:<ul><li>Higher of Wits or Dex to defense</li> <li>Claw and Bite to +2 and +4</li> <li>Gauru healing to [Stamina + Primal Urge] Lethal per turn.</li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Nicely done, nicely put. I think I agree. As stated, the gauru form is 'Used to kill prey as quickly and efficiently as possible.' but even with the bonus from strength, the real thing that is going to determine your ability to quickly and efficiently kill anyone is your brawl skill (providing you're not using a klaive or gifts). I think it'd be entirely fair to beef up the lethal damage, particularly since lethal is so commonplace now (pretty much all weapons do it) and mechanically, being attacked by a werewolf is comparable to being attacked by someone wielding a baton (claws) and crowbar (teeth). Upping the natural damage of these would reaffirm what the form is for, as well as making it a deadly form to enter or possibly death rage in if you weren't a combat-specialized character. As it is, when a wimp goes gauru, while you couldn't take him down, it's reasonable to imagine walking away without much harm.<br /> <br /> In addition, considering the focus is meant to be to kill and do it quickly (though I also like the gauru form to be a sort of fall-back when a werewolf is hurt), lowering the full heal, while not completely crippling it, sounds fair as well. It's a tough thing to figure out, considering werewolves are as vulnerable to multiple attackers as the next guy (though I imagine gifts will help in this).<br /> <br /> For pure whimsy's sake, I'd like to point out that in GMC, one of the primary way of dealing with the combat-superior is inflicting tilts. Called shots to the legs, to the eye, taking an arm out of the equation, that kind of thing. But it does seem more like the werewolf is inherently immune to this stuff. Perhaps, to even it out, some sort of...called shot exception to silver? At first I was imagining a sort of hack 'em up system, limbs flying (imagining the two gauru going at it) and eyes popping out. Perhaps it's just some lingering memories of the Rites of Renown anthology, where I first saw that, apparently, long long ago in another edition, werewolves were brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T19:27:29-07:00","id":126358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126321#post126321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 'Used to kill prey as quickly and efficiently as possible.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently, this is a big point of cognitive dissonance. As while Gauru is absolutely stellar at tanking damage, it's not noticeably superior to Urshul for the act of killing. Indeed depending on the characters combat options it may be outright worse (restricted movement options, inability to use non-attack gifts). The major difference is 1 die, or 3 if he's going all out. <br /> <br /> At this point I think something more than just MOAR DAMAGE may be needed. I'm currently doing a tank test (i.e. Fighting a tank, and a bunch of soldiers) and finding the Rahu less than super lethal, even to foot soldiers.<br /> <br /> Some ideas:<ul><li>Add some armor piercing, -1 for Claws, -2 for Jaws. In addition to increasing them to +2 and +4</li> <li>Add a 'field of hurt' like Flurry or Threat Range. Where just being near Gauru causes 2 lethal every action.</li> <li>Use 8-Again, or a similar dice probability modifier.</li> <li>Have all attacks from Gauru inflict tilts (Unlikely, since they don't have room in book)</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T19:37:53-07:00","id":126365,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd be fine with Gauru being the tank form rather than the execution form, if the fluff was altered to match. But then the turn limit becomes counter to the form's purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T19:38:40-07:00","id":126367,"title":"","content":"Well, the Quick and Dirty combat does help some (though, again, with a werewolf untrained in brawl that can just be a one roll way to lose).<br /> Yeah it's unfortunate tilts won't be in. I don't know about the 8 again. There's another thread, old by now I think, about how 9 again isn't that worthwhile, making it sort of a trap option.<br /> Needless to say, I like just a flat out damage increase.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-05-2014, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T22:21:49-07:00","id":126460,"title":"","content":"Pendragon's ideas help a lot with fixing my issue with Gauru as presented by Stew. Nice work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T22:28:12-07:00","id":126464,"title":"","content":"I find it to be a nice moderate fix. Still like the tanky nature though.<br /> <br /> Or they could affix different stats for garou based on auspice. Irakka have boosted speed and stealth like qualities/glass canon... yada yada...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-05T23:43:36-07:00","id":126496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126464#post126464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it to be a nice moderate fix. Still like the tanky nature though.<br /> <br /> Or they could affix different stats for garou based on auspice. Irakka have boosted speed and stealth like qualities/glass canon... yada yada...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I quite liked the auspice blessed ones. In theory. The big problem was that if you were going to do that kind of thing, you weren't in Gauru. I mean, if an Irraka is going to ambush something, she's only going to shift into Gauru at the very last moment, no need to be stealthy in War Form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T01:21:26-07:00","id":126543,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind in the scenarios which Look was testing... in no point whatsoever did the opponent burn Essence to heal up to their PU in Lethal, on top of the Gauru regen to considerably negate truly astonishing amounts of damage. If I had been the vampire with 200 rounds of ammo and grenades, etc, and that hadn't even slowed down the beast, I would have just fucking ran.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:15:13-07:00","id":126553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126543#post126543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to keep in mind in the scenarios which Look was testing... in no point whatsoever did the opponent burn Essence to heal up to their PU in Lethal, on top of the Gauru regen to considerably negate truly astonishing amounts of damage. If I had been the vampire with 200 rounds of ammo and grenades, etc, and that hadn't even slowed down the beast, I would have just fucking ran.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe they can spend Essence to heal. The way it was described Essence is now spent in forms other than Gauru to convert the natural bashing healing to lethal for that turn. If that's not the case I will put my foot down now and say Gauru is genuinely invulnerable without silver.<br /> <br /> Also, Rihat (the aforementioned vampire) has seen worse. My villains can make Gauru look downright cuddly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T02:36:59-07:00","id":126557,"title":"","content":"I'm part way through my 4th test, one Rahu vs an armored convo, but there is a clear trend that has shown through in all four scenarios: Gauru wants to wrassle.<br /> <br /> The evidence for this is significant. In all four instances grappling is the most effective go-to for the great man-wolf. In the first scenario it's the only way he can threaten the vampire, in the second it outright disables to only relevant hunter, in the third Mr. Pure manages to briefly stay Irraka's trap onslaught, and now in the 4th it's shown to be the definitively superior option for dealing with enemies in armor. Indeed the only reason to forgo grappling is if the Werewolf absolutely <b>needs </b>to deal damage this turn. Otherwise he'll have similar or better results waiting a turn and damaging opponents with his full, unpenalized dice pool.<br /> <br /> In retrospect this is hardly a surprise. With +3 Strength Gauru is highly likely to overwhelm opponents in grappling. Doing so allows a Werewolf to both deal more damage, unopposed by defense and completely paralyze his opponent, stealing their actions. In this sense the form is leagues better than Urshul for the duty of disabling prey, -1 defense vs. total combat irrelevance. Grappling is also the time at which Gauru is most terrifying, indeed in the vampire scenario it's the only time Gauru is terrifying.<br /> <br /> And you know what? I say we embrace that, being caught in the jaws of a massive lupine murder machine <b>should </b>be petrifying. So, pending a few changes, here's my full list of Gauru suggestions:<ul><li>Use the Higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense <b>(Just like natural wolves do)</b></li> <li>Apply Wits or Dexterity (but not Athletics) as defense vs Firearms <b>(This gives some defense, while keeping bullets at least slightly more effective)</b></li> <li>Heal all bashing damage and [Stamina + Primal Urge] Lethal Damage at the start of each turn.</li> <li>Claw Damage: +2 <b>(For dishing out nasty conditions)</b></li> <li>Bite Damage: +4, requires grappling <b>(this gives claws some purpose)</b></li> <li>When attacking in Gauru count three successes as an exceptional success for the purposes of inflicting Conditions, Tilts, and Grappling maneuvers.<b> (So Gauru can lay on shaken, and arm wrack with ease, and reliably deal damage within the first turn of a grapple)</b></li> <li>A wolf in Gauru must spend each turn attacking or pursuing his prey. He may prioritize particular prey, even if they are not the closest, but cannot go after non-prey (doing so risks Kuruth). Any non-combat action risks Kuruth. However, if that action is intended to set up for an attack on the subsequent turn, such as stalking around a barn to catch the hunters within by surprise, add +2 dice to the resistance roll.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-06-2014, 05:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T03:21:03-07:00","id":126572,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. So am I alone in thinking that - as long as we keep the time limit on Gauru, this limitless survivability might go away? Say - if death rage does not have this full healing? A lot of the problems come from assuming these werewolves can maintain Gauru indefinitely - via deathrage. <br /> <br /> The fight between the elder vampire &amp; the greenhorn would have looked very different if the uber-healing was only free for the first six rounds. If there was a difference between the Holy Rage (Gauru form sans deathrage) and, say, a Kuruth where healing had to be paid in essence - and the Kurth-wolf had no compunctions whatsoever in fueling this rage by eating every child &amp; businessman ready to claw - it might be very different.<br /> <br /> I know - I am operating on a lot of ifs - and Looks debuffs here make a lot of sense. I would hope gifts would up the danger of the form (Fifth Rahu gift: add purity reknown to claw/jaw damage, anyone?) - but this unstoppability is so much fun in shifting the narrative - as long as it is not indefinite.<br /> <br /> I'll shut up now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T04:02:58-07:00","id":126597,"title":"","content":"About the limit and Kurruth...<br /> I think you will always have one inherent problem if you have both the timelimit and the theoretically unlimited duration of the Death Rage:<br /> <br /> All the things balanced based on a limited duration suddenly go out of the window as soon as you enter the state.<br /> This is okay if you want to make Kurruth extremely terrifying, however, it can lead to the consequence that ultimately, you can only stop a werewolf in Kurruth by going into it yourself...<br /> And then it spirals out of control.<br /> <br /> Even a very experienced werewolf could have trouble with a completely new one on his first change if Gauru is that powerful...<br /> <br /> I think the primary concern should be: What kind of story does the system create.<br /> <br /> If with this Gauru the kind of stories you want to tell or be able to be told do not work any longer, then you might want to change it.<br /> If it makes the stories you want, then keep it. But do understand what the rules you make mean for the story, because gameplay and story segregation are one thing that easily annoys players a lot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T04:20:14-07:00","id":126604,"title":"","content":"I ignored Death Rage in my criticism of these rules because 1) we don't know how Death Rage works in the new system 2) we have reason to believe it's different and, most importantly, 3) a werewolf in Death Rage is not actively controlled by the player - he's literally out of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T04:55:00-07:00","id":126617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126557#post126557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When attacking in Gauru count three successes as an exceptional success for the purposes of inflicting Conditions, Tilts, and Grappling maneuvers.<b> (So Gauru can lay on shaken, and arm wrack with ease, and reliably deal damage within the first turn of a grapple)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>And were is &quot;Gauru tear them in two&quot; Tilt now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T05:43:16-07:00","id":126642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126094#post126094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember however that the healing comes at the START of the following turn, not the end of the current turn. This makes it so using it as a midway battle heal is risky. If the opponent goes after you, they still have a turn to deal sticking damage before the Gauru heal kicks in, and if they go in front of you, then it is still the case except they have 2 attacks to do it.<br /> <br /> This means the Werewolf would need to realize very quickly that they are in over their head and either GTFO, or shapeshift quickly</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes this is indeed a risk but I think this is in this case more a feature then a bug since as I have (hopefully) shown shifting to early will (probably) be a losing proposition. And thus adding this risk makes the combat (pre shift to Gauru more tense).<br /> <br /> Note the second this of course is still assuming a duel between two werewolves as shown by others the Gauru form might need some tweaks for other situations of course this will also alter the duel case (although healing all bashing and (altered) stamina + PU lethal is still probably enough to keep most of my analysis on target)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2735-dutch_wolf","name":"Dutch_Wolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T05:57:15-07:00","id":126651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126617#post126617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And were is &quot;Gauru tear them in two&quot; Tilt now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, as has been said, we don't have room for Tilts in the book. Since it needs to be stand-alone, we can't be saying things like &quot;reference page XX in <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>&quot; or anything like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T06:17:26-07:00","id":126658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126651#post126651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, as has been said, we don't have room for Tilts in the book. Since it needs to be stand-alone, we can't be saying things like &quot;reference page XX in <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>&quot; or anything like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was a joke, but to be frank, I would like to see a way how Uratha can tear normal people in to - or even unsuspecitng combatants. Where is better place for gore przemoc of World of Darkness than in <b>Werewolf</b> gameline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T06:25:31-07:00","id":126663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126658#post126658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a joke, but to be frank, I would like to see a way how Uratha can tear normal people in to - or even unsuspecitng combatants. Where is better place for gore przemoc of World of Darkness than in <b>Werewolf</b> gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the sort of things that need rules or tilts, it's a description for killing someone with full aggravated<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T06:32:15-07:00","id":126668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126658#post126658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a joke, but to be frank, I would like to see a way how Uratha can tear normal people in to - or even unsuspecitng combatants. Where is better place for gore przemoc of World of Darkness than in <b>Werewolf</b> gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why they use the Down &amp; Dirty rules for &quot;lesser&quot; foes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My thoughts on today's preview:<br /> <br /> I love how indestructible Garou is, but I agree that it's missing something on the offensive side. I love that it can clear out mooks like nobody's business, but mook fights are never very interesting to me anyway: they exist to showcase how dangerous I am. I would like &quot;real&quot; fights to be more interesting, and for that I'll want a Garou form that's more than just a tank.<br /> <br /> Giving their claws and fangs armor penetration is a good start. It reminds me of the &quot;Collateral Damage&quot; rule from Armory: Reloaded where you decreased the durability of all objects to some amount that you thought was appropriate, and I would always lower that setting to the ground. Peeling open an APC like a can of sardines is the kind of thing I want in my werewolf games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, maybe some Gifts will improve the offensive capabilities of Garou. I doubt I'll get to look at them ahead of time, but I'm eagerly awaiting seeing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T06:43:39-07:00","id":126675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126557#post126557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...here's my full list of Gauru suggestions:<ul><li>Use the Higher of Wits or Dexterity for Defense <b>(Just like natural wolves do)</b></li> <li>Apply Wits or Dexterity (but not Athletics) as defense vs Firearms <b>(This gives some defense, while keeping bullets at least slightly more effective)</b></li> <li>Heal all bashing damage and [Stamina + Primal Urge] Lethal Damage at the start of each turn.</li> <li>Claw Damage: +2 <b>(For dishing out nasty conditions)</b></li> <li>Bite Damage: +4, requires grappling <b>(this gives claws some purpose)</b></li> <li>When attacking in Gauru count three successes as an exceptional success for the purposes of inflicting Conditions, Tilts, and Grappling maneuvers.<b> (So Gauru can lay on shaken, and arm wrack with ease, and reliably deal damage within the first turn of a grapple)</b></li> <li>A wolf in Gauru must spend each turn attacking or pursuing his prey. He may prioritize particular prey, even if they are not the closest, but cannot go after non-prey (doing so risks Kuruth). Any non-combat action risks Kuruth. However, if that action is intended to set up for an attack on the subsequent turn, such as stalking around a barn to catch the hunters within by surprise, add +2 dice to the resistance roll.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this a lot - obviously without the full knowledge of Kuruth and other aspects of the book it's hard to fully back any suggestion completely, however these do seem to rectify some of my own concerns presently.<br /> <br /> I've never been a fan of time limits - but I understand why there is one and as Stew is going this route then the +2 resistance roll for setting up an attack seems very plausible.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the Bite Damage is slightly too high especially if they were to also follow the suggestion of three successes as exceptional, but I've not played around with those rules myself yet.<br /> <br /> I completely agree with you with the applying Wits or Dex to Defense against Firearms <i>but not Athletics</i> - I think there is definitely a<b> need</b> to lessen the effect of Firearms against Uratha, but whilst a rampaging Garau weaving through gunfire looks great in my head I can't shake the image of the wolf-man doing matrix style bullet-time if they apply full defense. This suggestion really allows to keep the first image and get rid of the second.<br /> <br /> On a slightly different note, but keeping with the same idea - as I commented on the blog I am wondering if there's going to be any specific supernatural merits or gifts that would give additional bonuses to forms, whether they be suggestions from people on the blog (human form getting extra perception/8-9 again rolls for Garou form from Armory reloaded etc) or old favourites such as Partial Change getting a look in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T07:54:06-07:00","id":126698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126651#post126651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly, as has been said, we don't have room for Tilts in the book. Since it needs to be stand-alone, we can't be saying things like &quot;reference page XX in <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b>&quot; or anything like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, my opinion is that Tilts should be brought in and something sacrificed in order to make word count for them. But that's mostly because I have absolutely no idea what might get sacrificed, which makes it really easy to say that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T07:56:51-07:00","id":126702,"title":"","content":"I really like your suggestions, Pendragon.<br /> <br /> As for more visceral combat, if post GMC books do well, I imagine one of the first 'core' books will be a sort of...Armory Rereloaded. The past books were full of combat hacks for different splats. After all, werewolves aren't the only ones capable of being physical badasses, and forcing everyone to get Idigam Chronicles for a combat tune-up may pad sales a bit but it'd probably piss some folks off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-06-2014, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T09:11:43-07:00","id":126741,"title":"","content":"Eagerly awaiting pendragons next update. Weird considering I usually rely only on dev comments. I just haven't had a chance to play test it yet. But it is good to see people who get the 'garou is a terrifying monster' vibe that we should be getting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T09:50:05-07:00","id":126762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126658#post126658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a joke, but to be frank, I would like to see a way how Uratha can tear normal people in to - or even unsuspecitng combatants. Where is better place for gore przemoc of World of Darkness than in <b>Werewolf</b> gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Down and Dirty is for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:33:34-07:00","id":126862,"title":"","content":"Does anybody else find it ironic that we've been trying to fix the Gauru form for years and now that a new, more powerful Gauru form is coming we're now trying to fix that one too? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The problem with all this &quot;white rooming&quot; is that we don't have the whole picture. I think it's too soon to say that Gauru still needs a buff when we still haven't seen the Strength Gift or Rage Gift yet. Not to mention any new Merits or Fetishes that could augment the Gauru form for the better. I say we wait to see how this works out with the rest of the Werewolve's arsenal before we cast any judgement.<br /> <br /> That being said, my first impression on the Gauru form was a little mixed. I love the absurd durability and how it can just wipe out mooks like a boss. But the thing that always gets me is that stupid time limit and the limited amount of actions you can take with the Gauru form. It's still the form with &quot;little screen time&quot;. What if I want to be in Gauru for the entire Hunt? What if I want to focus on being the ultimate badass in Gauru form? I still can't do that. It's a minor gripe to be sure, but I still would have liked to see those stupid limitations gone. It's still not enough to stop from getting this book though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:43:58-07:00","id":126867,"title":"","content":"As stated previously: all that these tests can do, all that they are intended to do, is establish the baseline of Gauru. The point of power it cannot go below. Kuruth? Gifts? Merits? These will all likely make the form more potent, but it's highly unlikely they'll be making Gauru any <b>less</b> powerful. (Well, Kuruth maybe, but I sure hope not).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm in the camp that even the greenest, newly-changed pup should be frighteningly powerful when in Warform. At least to normal humans, even hunters, but should not be an insurmountable threat to all but the most ludicrously experienced warriors. The changes I'm suggesting come from that outlook. If a player wants to add in Gifts to make Gauru more dangerous or more durable then more power to them, but the baseline form should be a nightmarish killing machine first, and an unstoppable tank second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-06-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:45:57-07:00","id":126869,"title":"","content":"The thing that gets me is that I'm pretty sure the time in Gauru is expanded-wasn't it just Stamina+PU before, where now it's Stamina+PU+Auspice Renown?<br /> <br /> I'm largely in the camp of people who think along the &quot;you can be in the form after this long ,but expect to resist Kuruth for it&quot; line, but it must be said it's still extended naturally more than it was.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Gauru being a potent but limited option. This is something you try and surgically unleash on the world, not just something you go to willy nilly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:48:56-07:00","id":126875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126862#post126862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anybody else find it ironic that we've been trying to fix the Gauru form for years and now that a new, more powerful Gauru form is coming we're now trying to fix that one too? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Different people, Stew and the writers included, like different things. I can't stand the excessive durability, but I've always been perfectly ok with the time limit. Others see things differently. It's all good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126862#post126862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with all this &quot;white rooming&quot; is that we don't have the whole picture. I think it's too soon to say that Gauru still needs a buff when we still haven't seen the Strength Gift or Rage Gift yet. Not to mention any new Merits or Fetishes that could augment the Gauru form for the better. I say we wait to see how this works out with the rest of the Werewolve's arsenal before we cast any judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the context of a thread discussing shapeshifting, I find that gifts (that only a certain percentage of the werewolf population buy) or merits, and especially fetishes, which you have to own to use, are entirely irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126862#post126862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, my first impression on the Gauru form was a little mixed. I love the absurd durability and how it can just wipe out mooks like a boss. But the thing that always gets me is that stupid time limit and the limited amount of actions you can take with the Gauru form. It's still the form with &quot;little screen time&quot;. What if I want to be in Gauru for the entire Hunt? What if I want to focus on being the ultimate badass in Gauru form? I still can't do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not. It wouldn't be thematic or sensible to do so. Different forms serve different purposes. Gauru is for killing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:51:55-07:00","id":126879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126867#post126867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated previously: all that these tests can do, all that they are intended to do, is establish the baseline of Gauru. The point of power it cannot go below. Kuruth? Gifts? Merits? These will all likely the form more potent, but it's highly unlikely they'll be making Gauru any <b>less</b> powerful. (Well, Kuruth maybe, but I sure hope not).<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm in the camp that even the greenest, newly-changed pup should be frighteningly powerful when in Warform. At least to normal humans, even hunters, but should not be an insurmountable threat to all but the most ludicrously experienced warriors. The changes I'm suggesting come from that outlook. If a player wants to add in Gifts to make Gauru more dangerous or more durable then more power to them, but the baseline form should be a nightmarish killing machine first, and an unstoppable tank second.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, especially with the priorities - killing machine first, tank second. Gauru is about doing damage primarily; as Stew himself said in the preview, Gauru is for killing. The unstoppable tank thing is secondary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T12:59:22-07:00","id":126886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126879#post126879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, especially with the priorities - killing machine first, tank second. Gauru is about doing damage primarily; as Stew himself said in the preview, Gauru is for killing. The unstoppable tank thing is secondary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should note. I <b>do</b> want Gauru to be able to Tank. Especially if it's going to be getting into the rough and really dish out damage the form should be expected to take quite a few hits. I just think that <b>all</b> lethal goes a step beyond tanking and enters the realm of boring. A reduced, but still extreme rate accomplishes the same goal 90% of the time while also adding a little bit of excitement and some potential sense of progress for attackers.<br /> <br /> Basically, attempting to fight a rapid regeneration with a steady stream of damage, exciting. Having a hard 'damage point' which must be hit every turn for any progress to be made, less exciting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T13:19:05-07:00","id":126904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126886#post126886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should note. I <b>do</b> want Gauru to be able to Tank. Especially if it's going to be getting into the rough and really dish out damage the form should be expected to take quite a few hits. I just think that <b>all</b> lethal goes a step beyond tanking and enters the realm of boring. A reduced, but still extreme rate accomplishes the same goal 90% of the time while also adding a little bit of excitement and some potential sense of progress for attackers.<br /> <br /> Basically, attempting to fight a rapid regeneration with a steady stream of damage, exciting. Having a hard 'damage point' which must be hit every turn for any progress to be made, less exciting.</div> </div> </div> </div>At a certain point, though, that distinction becomes pretty meaningless (All vs. Stamina+PU). The Werewolf character I play in Classic nWOD would be healing 11-13 Boxes or so per round (Garou/Primal Form - a far cry from the PU Healing he has currently, which is 4). THAT is a SIGNIFICANT difference, and quite robust, regardless of which rule is active at that point. Is that less than the Health Boxes he has? Of course (he has 20/22 in Garou/Primal Form) but that distinction is pretty meaningless in the long run since I can't remember the last time he TOOK 13+ boxes of health damage in a single round. At some point, they become the same in effect, even if they are not the same in theory.<br /> <br /> That said - I tend to take more Aggravated damage from primary opponents (Vampires mostly) these days, sadly, which is not healed by regeneration at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T13:42:30-07:00","id":126925,"title":"","content":"See I'm fine with characters growing into that level of resilience. Because it means experience has been invested and growth achieved. Got lots of stamina and high PU? Congrats, you are rewarded with greater durability than a Werewolf 30xp your younger. Again, this was about baselines. Experienced wolves being that durable doesn't bother me as much, they earned it. (Though even then it'll be noticable for a while, healing 10 damage is a lot, but still significantly less than 14)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T13:46:57-07:00","id":126930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126904#post126904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At a certain point, though, that distinction becomes pretty meaningless (All vs. Stamina+PU).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the point. At the point you've got 5+6 or more, you're not just an 'ordinary' werewolf, and you're pushing into the...well, there was no real word for it in Werewolf the Forsaken, but 'really powerful' might fit. I suppose a vampire comparison might be the elder, at 150+ years. That's when the game changes. Mages have double masteries, maybe move to archmage or past 5 dots in an arcana, changelings get their bedlams, vampires have to feed on other vampires. The game changes. In Forsaken, it meant you started bleeding essence.<br /> <br /> It's good that it's linked to Primal Urge, too. Cause, going by the teaser, the werewolf who just had their first change, and the most powerful werewolf in the world both work off the same system, and the thing that's going to determine who wins in a fight is their strength+brawl. Which, as I stated before, I'd also like to change. Placing more emphasis on the werewolf form, by giving the gauru form more damage, and on the werewolf condition, by giving an advantage to primal urge (though admittedly we haven't seen much in the way of that stat before). Sure, the first change werewolf is tough, and scary, but a hunter is going to be able to, conceivably, rally up a posse and take them out. Whereas they'll have more trouble when Terribus the Thirdborn comes into town and pushes through hails of gunfire with ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T13:49:34-07:00","id":126934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126904#post126904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At a certain point, though, that distinction becomes pretty meaningless (All vs. Stamina+PU). The Werewolf character I play in Classic nWOD would be healing 11-13 Boxes or so per round (Garou/Primal Form - a far cry from the PU Healing he has currently, which is 4). THAT is a SIGNIFICANT difference, and quite robust, regardless of which rule is active at that point. Is that less than the Health Boxes he has? Of course (he has 20/22 in Garou/Primal Form) but that distinction is pretty meaningless in the long run since I can't remember the last time he TOOK 13+ boxes of health damage in a single round. At some point, they become the same in effect, even if they are not the same in theory.<br /> <br /> That said - I tend to take more Aggravated damage from primary opponents (Vampires mostly) these days, sadly, which is not healed by regeneration at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's the point, I think. Working for near invulnerability instead of having it by virtue of form.<br /> <br /> I also agree that this current setup is <b>boring</b>. Some of the best scenes I've had involved actual fear of character loss. And those got me thinking creatively as you wouldn't believe.<br /> <br /> Ithaeur HiD from my previous anecdote, being chase by 7 materialized spirit hounds thru the dilapidated streets of Detroit. The chase isn't going well, so I take to the roofs. I managed to determinate the hounds bans with Read Spirit. They cannot give up the hunt. So I go up and up. Then I confront them, on a ledge, and, as they circle me, thinking I have no escape, I ask my ST if I can fully dodge (everything put into that action) and if they fail their attacks, if they would fall off the building. They all attack, they all fail, they all plummet into discorporation.<br /> <br /> My character was rank 3; these were rank 2. In the current system, I only would have needed to take Gauru, down and dirty and discorporate them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:00:59-07:00","id":126940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126875#post126875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the context of a thread discussing shapeshifting, I find that gifts (that only a certain percentage of the werewolf population buy) or merits, and especially fetishes, which you have to own to use, are entirely irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be entirely irrelevant if it where not for the fact that most of this white rooming is pitting a naked, unarmed, unGifted, unMerited Werewolf against a Vampire Elder who has complete access to his full template arsenal. It's a Werewolf with 25% of his power vs. a Vampire with 100% of his own. It seems hardly fair to judge the Gauru form based solely on inborn template traits alone, but thankfully, Pendragon just explained to me what the whole point was. So, not really a big deal for me now. Thanks Pendragon. I mean it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126875#post126875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course not. It wouldn't be thematic or sensible to do so. Different forms serve different purposes. Gauru is for killing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Gauru form is for killing. But I don't see why that has to mean the form is useless in other situations. Urhan is for chasing down and harrying prey. I don't see any resriction saying &quot;this form can only be assumed for the purpose of Foot Chases. If assumed outside of a Foot Chase, it always leads to Kuruth&quot; or &quot;this form can only be maintained during a Foot Chase&quot;. The forms have there purpose, yes, but I don't see why this has to handicap the Gauru form. Urhan is still usable for things outside of Foot Chases. It's just better suited for it. Why can't I assume Gauru form to break down a wall or what in ambush for my pack mates to lead our prey to my waiting jaws? Granted, we don't know how Kuruth works now, so maybe I'm wrong about the whole Urhan thing. I certainly hope not.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:09:27-07:00","id":126951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126940#post126940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be entirely irrelevant if it where not for the fact that most of this white rooming is pitting a naked, unarmed, unGifted, unMerited Werewolf against a Vampire Elder who has complete access to his full template arsenal. It's a Werewolf with 25% of his power vs. a Vampire with 100% of his own. It seems hardly fair to judge the Gauru form based solely on inborn template traits alone, but thankfully, Pendragon just explained to me what the whole point was. So, not really a big deal for me now. Thanks Pendragon. I mean it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The takeaway from that test was the fact that, even at 25% power, Gauru was still nearly impossible to kill. Even for an absolute beast of a vampire, far and beyond anything you'd expect to run across in game (seriously, 30 dice on an attack is madness in GMC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:20:31-07:00","id":126966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126951#post126951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The takeaway from that test was the fact that, even at 25% power, Gauru was still nearly impossible to kill. Even for an absolute beast of a vampire, far and beyond anything you'd expect to run across in game (seriously, 30 dice on an attack is madness in GMC).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll say.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> FWIW, I do agree that the Gauru form's Lethal healing should be a bit less. Your idea was better than mine, I think. Mine was going to be &quot;all Bashing/ PU Lethal per turn&quot;. Adding Stamina to that definitly makes them scarier for sure without making the fight irritating. As far as increasing the baseline weapon damage on claws and bites, I still say wait to see the Strength and/or Rage Facets. Their's a good chance one of those will do the job. If not, your idea it very sound and I'll most likely go with that if there isn't such a Facet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:38:31-07:00","id":126987,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, I've rarely been impressed by the fanfixes I've seen, but I like how this thread has turned out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:45:27-07:00","id":126992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126934#post126934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's the point, I think. Working for near invulnerability instead of having it by virtue of form.<br /> <br /> I also agree that this current setup is <b>boring</b>. Some of the best scenes I've had involved actual fear of character loss. And those got me thinking creatively as you wouldn't believe.<br /> <br /> Ithaeur HiD from my previous anecdote, being chase by 7 materialized spirit hounds thru the dilapidated streets of Detroit. The chase isn't going well, so I take to the roofs. I managed to determinate the hounds bans with Read Spirit. They cannot give up the hunt. So I go up and up. Then I confront them, on a ledge, and, as they circle me, thinking I have no escape, I ask my ST if I can fully dodge (everything put into that action) and if they fail their attacks, if they would fall off the building. They all attack, they all fail, they all plummet into discorporation.<br /> <br /> My character was rank 3; these were rank 2. In the current system, I only would have needed to take Gauru, down and dirty and discorporate them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Believe me, I understand that... Being hounded by Spirits really, really sucks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Even my Cahalith was harried from time to time by Spirits. No matter how bad ass you were/are in Forsaken Base, Numbers mattered. I agree that the new system is leading down a road that I am unlikely to follow. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 05-06-2014, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:49:35-07:00","id":126995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahuman101</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126966#post126966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I'll say.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> FWIW, I do agree that the Gauru form's Lethal healing should be a bit less. Your idea was better than mine, I think. Mine was going to be &quot;all Bashing/ PU Lethal per turn&quot;. Adding Stamina to that definitly makes them scarier for sure without making the fight irritating. As far as increasing the baseline weapon damage on claws and bites, I still say wait to see the Strength and/or Rage Facets. Their's a good chance one of those will do the job. If not, your idea it very sound and I'll most likely go with that if there isn't such a Facet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, it should be all bashing and Primal Urge Lethal per turn with one essence change that to (Stamina + PU) lethal. At Stamina 3 and Pu 2 that's over half your Health levels per turn for free otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T14:59:32-07:00","id":127005,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind we're just talking about in one form that has a limited duration, as well as the chance to go into Death Rage. Some power is to be expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T15:05:18-07:00","id":127008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=127005#post127005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind we're just talking about in one form that has a limited duration, as well as the chance to go into Death Rage. Some power is to be expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As suggested Gauru would start out recovering ~50% of it's lethal every turn. A number that would only go up as Stamina &amp; Primal Urge improve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T15:20:24-07:00","id":127016,"title":"","content":"I just really like the increased damage. It makes sense, it's not that unfair (you get damage comparable to a fire ax, instead of a crowbar, which seems more appropriate), and theoretically you could demote the 'supernatural damage, bypassing vampires' to a merit. I like the damage to vampire thing, but I understand some don't and a base increase in damage may help alleviate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T16:27:18-07:00","id":127063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=127005#post127005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind we're just talking about in one form that has a limited duration, as well as the chance to go into Death Rage. Some power is to be expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see a lot of fights last longer than Gauru form currently can. Especially if you focus on stamina and renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T18:51:07-07:00","id":127154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126698#post126698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the record, my opinion is that Tilts should be brought in and something sacrificed in order to make word count for them. But that's mostly because I have absolutely no idea what might get sacrificed, which makes it really easy to say that.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I've looked at, I'm not sure what we'd cut, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T18:54:00-07:00","id":127156,"title":"","content":"You know, it's funny? I don't know if tilts are in Blood and Smoke.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that randomly, I'm saying there might be a little bit of a point if it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T18:54:16-07:00","id":127157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=127154#post127154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've looked at, I'm not sure what we'd cut, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple fix. Reduce all fonts by one point, then ship the book with a magnifying monocle! Class and convenience in one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T19:18:33-07:00","id":127168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=126869#post126869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that gets me is that I'm pretty sure the time in Gauru is expanded-wasn't it just Stamina+PU before, where now it's Stamina+PU+Auspice Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't see a response to this. Yes, originally it's Stam+PU except on nights of your Auspice, then you get to add your Auspice Renown. You also shapeshift as a reflexive action for free if your moon is out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T19:18:36-07:00","id":127169,"title":"","content":"The tilt rules are available for free with the GMC mechanics, not having them in isn't that big of a deal.<br /> <br /> Blood and Smoke has a limited tilt section, only referring to the results of called shots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T19:38:52-07:00","id":127176,"title":"","content":"I'd like to take a moment to make something clear about all previous tests and comments, as there has been some confusion about their purpose/conclusion.<br /> <br /> The tests are not remotely intended to nay say or detract from the work of the writers, nor at they intended to cast any light on how the Idigam modifications will play out in their complete form (with Gifts and Merits). I am well aware, as others should be, that when it comes to the table the number of additional factors present in the game can grossly throw off any &quot;expected&quot; outcomes. Just at my table I've seen an immensely powerful Rahu Gauru 'defeated' in numerous ways, from well placed illusion to telekinetic suspension twenty feet off the ground. Even if the form was totally invulnerable, it would still be possible render it helpless.<br /> <br /> What I intend to offer, all I can offer, is a narrow insight into specific scenarios and some ideas on how to modify those scenarios for greater excitement (again, my opinion of it). The value of this is exclusively derived from the reader and whether or not they believe that, within that scenario, the end result was acceptable for their expectations. If in the light of other factors the suggestions help. Good. If they don't, well we'll all see exactly why when the book hits the digital press and then we're all the happier.<br /> <br /> Idigam is great, all the spoilers have been inspired, and what little quibbles I have amount to little more than a dump of ideas based on the current data. My option is simply between providing no feedback, and doing what I can to provide something constructive. If that offends, please know that it was never intended to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T20:53:24-07:00","id":127227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=127169#post127169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tilt rules are available for free with the GMC mechanics, not having them in isn't that big of a deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that I want the tilt rules for reference; it's that I want the tilt rules available for being used by all the other rules. As has been pointed out, the Urshul thing makes sense as a Tilt, but it can't be one because word count. Anyways. I'm not hung up on it; I just wanted to put the opinion up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T02:55:54-07:00","id":127339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=127176#post127176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If that offends, please know that it was never intended to.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, it's not offending me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T09:37:30-07:00","id":128316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=127227#post127227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not that I want the tilt rules for reference; it's that I want the tilt rules available for being used by all the other rules. As has been pointed out, the Urshul thing makes sense as a Tilt, but it can't be one because word count. Anyways. I'm not hung up on it; I just wanted to put the opinion up there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, personally I feel like leaving out the tilt mechanics (as opposed to leaving out certain specific tilts) is a little bit like leaving out extended action mechanics. It's a part of how the system works, if you leave it out you don't make the book more standalone, you make it incomplete. Don't get me wrong, I'm not upset they're not making if in, since I have two other books with those rules in them and I am not much bothered whether IC stands alone or not. I just think its a strange choice of where to cut word count. (Though I trust the writers and developers judgment and assume I would feel differently if I saw the full product).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T00:33:42-07:00","id":128797,"title":"","content":"Am I to believe that the current rules for fighting style application across the forms will be retained into the new system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T01:01:49-07:00","id":128803,"title":"","content":"We don't know. Though it seems likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T03:10:26-07:00","id":128842,"title":"","content":"Can't wait to see Dath Rage spoiler now! <img 