but that's a lot on anyone's plate, I'd suspect.<br /> <br /> Still, there are a few of us who do try to comment as much as we can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T15:02:10-07:00","id":129284,"title":"","content":"The nerve of those people, throwing money at W20 and slowing down our Idigam Chronicles updates.<br /> <br /> *nudges his leatherbound copy out of sight*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T15:07:57-07:00","id":129286,"title":"","content":"We love ya Strider, its just worrying since he's the one that posts the blogs!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T15:21:30-07:00","id":129297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=129284#post129284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nerve of those people, throwing money at W20 and slowing down our Idigam Chronicles updates.<br /> <br /> *nudges his leatherbound copy out of sight*</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I wanted to throw money at that, I just didn't have the money. I mean, not that I play Apocalypse - or, really, any cWoD stuff - these days, but it would have been nice to have it on the shelf next to my V20...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T17:51:39-07:00","id":129441,"title":"","content":"I know. I never got into old World of Darkness, heard about it but at the time it wasn't something to interest me. So new World of Darkness was my first step into things.<br /> I've looked at the old stuff every once and awhile, but never really thought it was worth picking up anything for until the 20th anniversary books. I hate to sound like a commercial but they're really solidly made and they do look nice on the shelf with the other stuff.<br /> <br /> The Mage is the only kickstarter I threw into, though. I think my players will appreciate the super science of the conventions more than the traditions, but fun is fun. I incorporate aspects of both v20 and w20 into my current game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T17:57:19-07:00","id":129445,"title":"","content":"I like a lot of the Old World stuff, but I don't know it as well, and most of my resources are on a computer, which hinders my groups more than it should. Contrast that with nWoD where I know a shit ton(although not as much as others do) of the lore and pretty much all of the mechanics(loosely) and have them in hard copy, and it's easy to see why I'm an nWoD child.<br /> <br /> Asides from, you know, coming in between Created and Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:13:50-07:00","id":129510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=128803#post128803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't know. Though it seems likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mention it because the main detriment in my opinion to Gauru form in the current Forsaken is its lack of access to fighting styles. <br /> <br /> With those being the main go-to for multiple-attack actions, it quickly becomes apparent that Gauru is by far the weakest of the forms. Unless you've discovered a way to get an obscenely large dice pool that's only available in your war-form, making 2+ attacks per turn is going to trump anything you dish out in a practical fighting scenario.<br /> <br /> Now so far it seems like they've done a good job keeping multiple-attacks out of the new system. I haven't seen it in any of the fighting-styles in GMC and nothing either Demon or Vampire seems to allow it barring Celerity's pre-empt ability but if I read that right it doesn't actually give extra actions. If it does I need very much to reread it.<br /> <br /> If both remain true into the future, that Gauru can't use fighting-styles and multiple-attack actions are left out of the system entirely, then things should probably be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:29:06-07:00","id":129527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=129510#post129510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mention it because the main detriment in my opinion to Gauru form in the current Forsaken is its lack of access to fighting styles.<br /> <br /> With those being the main go-to for multiple-attack actions, it quickly becomes apparent that Gauru is by far the weakest of the forms. Unless you've discovered a way to get an obscenely large dice pool that's only available in your war-form, making 2+ attacks per turn is going to trump anything you dish out in a practical fighting scenario.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple attacks are gone completely now, even from fighting styles,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T19:47:58-07:00","id":129540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=129527#post129527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Multiple attacks are gone completely now, even from fighting styles,</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thank you for confirmation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T21:08:53-07:00","id":129589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=129540#post129540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome, thank you for confirmation.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've said that was a big thing. And the Celerity Pre-empt uses up your action for the turn. Its basically a reactive initiative adjustment, that doesn't allow the defender to change their action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T00:53:57-07:00","id":129705,"title":"","content":"On top of that, it is worth noting that the GMC era updates greatly increased Defense relative to attack dice pools (not including firearms) and made armor much more potent.<br /> <br /> Even if you did have Whirlwind Strike from the pre-GMC rules in the new rules, it would be incredibly stupid to use. The brokeness of the pre-GMC multiple action Merits was strongly linked to the disparity in access to large offensive pools to large Defense totals. In the pre-GMC rules have 4-6 dice after Defense even on a Brawl attack was very easy; so when multiplied you could easily dish out more damage than a target could hope to take. In the GMC rules have an attack pool of 3+ after Defense represents a large imbalance between offensive investment vs. defensive investment (aka the defender is way weaker than the attacker; though again not counting guns, though in the new form rules Gauru applies full Defense against guns anyway). Having 1-2 dice per attack and then running into Armor on top of that, while sacrificing your Defense is far from the reliable KO route of the old rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T14:02:00-07:00","id":130151,"title":"","content":"There was the Silver Road option; if a Rahu took the Silver Road (War Against the Pure), their benefit was access to Fighting Styles in Gauru form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T22:18:26-07:00","id":131631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=129589#post129589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've said that was a big thing. And the Celerity Pre-empt uses up your action for the turn. Its basically a reactive initiative adjustment, that doesn't allow the defender to change their action.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't use up your action you just can't attack twice in a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T22:31:43-07:00","id":131643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=131631#post131631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It doesn't use up your action you just can't attack twice in a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div> You can't take any more than one instant action in a turn, doesn't matter if the action is an attack or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T06:47:16-07:00","id":132127,"title":"","content":"With the discussion of whether or not vampires downgrade tooth and claw to bashing damage going on in the Requiem forum I figured I'd post a vote here in the shape-shifting thread to keep those attacks as lethal damage. If it isn't then I hope to see a merit or facet that upgrades the type of damage an Uratha causes (which seems like a reasonable compromise to me.) I'd definitely like to see the issue officially addressed in the IC book, one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:04:45-07:00","id":132150,"title":"","content":"I'll agree that it should point out that a Werewolf's natural weapons in the intermediary forms are supernatural, but I would prefer it not specifically say that means lethal damage to vampires. Supernal already implies lethal to vampires, no need to call it out, especially since vampires may or may not even exist in a given game and may or may not follow the same rules as Requiem's vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:18:03-07:00","id":132162,"title":"","content":"As I've said previously, I prefer that these things are just stated outright in order to avoid rules arguments at the game table. Vampire itself has left the issue of whether or not it would do anything vague enough to cause that shit storm in the vampire section, so I'd prefer just giving a hard answer one way or the other. Personally I don't see a problem with it, and in fact would prefer it to pierce all downgrading effects, regardless of source. I'll admit that that might be going a bit too far but I do find it fittingly monstrous/powerful for a werewolves natural weaponry to be efficient in almost all situations and against almost all opposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:28:33-07:00","id":132203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=131631#post131631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't use up your action you just can't attack twice in a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever you do for your interrupt is your action, celerity itself doesn't stop their action, basically it moves your action up and lets you react to what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Also I vote for lethal being a merit rather than an innate facet of the intermediate forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T07:43:51-07:00","id":132250,"title":"","content":"I sicerely don't care anymore one way or another. If it is explicetely said it does Lethal to vampires, I expect an explanation as to why, besides &quot;it's supernatural&quot;. That's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:10:59-07:00","id":132280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132250#post132250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sicerely don't care anymore one way or another. If it is explicetely said it does Lethal to vampires, I expect an explanation as to why, besides &quot;it's supernatural&quot;. That's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Unnatural Aspect gets away with it without any explanation. Make up your own like you did with it. That's the deal with supernatural stuff, you fill in the gaps, because it can't be explained otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:27:39-07:00","id":132303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132280#post132280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why? Unnatural Aspect gets away with it without any explanation. Make up your own like you did with it. That's the deal with supernatural stuff, you fill in the gaps, because it can't be explained otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm with Thorbes on this, but I do think a fan explanation is just as good as an &quot;official&quot; one, and Ahenrogue pointed out a good one over in the vampire thread. The popular fan justification for Protean 4 doing lethal is that they're an extension of the vampire's Beast and beast-on-beast contact is bad for vampires. In the Predatory Aura section in B&amp;S there's a sidebar that says vampires Beasts have a similar reaction to other supernaturals' auras, and werewolves' are mentioned specifically. So in the hybrid forms their claws should have the same beast-harming effect Protean 4 claws do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:31:34-07:00","id":132304,"title":"","content":"Well, it is a vampire power, you may find it silly, but it is easier for me to accept it. Plus it is a carry over from when the Protean claws did Aggravated.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the explanation provided by Ashenrogue in the thread in the Vampire forum works for me, and does it for both Uratha and Protean claws, so bonus!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:36:35-07:00","id":132308,"title":"","content":"Eh to me its a gamebreaking issue. I'm heavily invested in crossover and I really don't like the concept of innate abilities ignoring the innate abilities of other gamelines, especially those that didn't have the benefit of a later release. I feel its going to lead to an increasingly downward trend in later lines.<br /> <br /> Mages generally don't have substantial innate abilities, most of their power comes from spells, with a few other capabilities. I'm fine with that. I'd be fine with non-Gauru claws dealing lethal if it required some experience investment, even if its a merit similar to Unnatural Affinity (With options to do damage to different major gamelines/1 dot per oddity).<br /> <br /> Werewolves already have what amounts to facets of several disciplines and devotions innately, and I don't mind that. I don't mind the defense against firearms or the Interrupt capability, they don't cancel out another group's innate feature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T08:50:11-07:00","id":132311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132308#post132308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh to me its a gamebreaking issue. I'm heavily invested in crossover and I really don't like the concept of innate abilities ignoring the innate abilities of other gamelines, especially those that didn't have the benefit of a later release. I feel its going to lead to an increasingly downward trend in later lines.<br /> <br /> Mages generally don't have substantial innate abilities, most of their power comes from spells, with a few other capabilities. I'm fine with that. I'd be fine with non-Gauru claws dealing lethal if it required some experience investment, even if its a merit similar to Unnatural Affinity (With options to do damage to different major gamelines/1 dot per oddity).<br /> <br /> Werewolves already have what amounts to facets of several disciplines and devotions innately, and I don't mind that. I don't mind the defense against firearms or the Interrupt capability, they don't cancel out another group's innate feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>My biggest issue with this reasoning is that it's a double standard. By your reasoning it is ok for vampires to be able to innately downgrade a werewolves innate ability to do lethal with their teeth and claws in intermediary forms. Why is that not a gamebreaking issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:40:37-07:00","id":132338,"title":"","content":"Oh, one thing I just realized about Gauru form healing all bashing and all lethal every turn allows it to be used as a mid-combat reset button. During a long combat as you get steadily worn down, accumulating more and more lethal damage, once your health track gets a little too close to full, you can just shift to Gauru form for one turn and suddenly you're good as new. I'm not sure if I like that or not. I'll have to see it play out, but it feels like it creates a weird incentive to use Gauru as the healing form rather than the killing form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:43:53-07:00","id":132342,"title":"","content":"Especially combined with the limited duration, it seems like I wouldn't want to &quot;waste&quot; my Gauru turns on &quot;just&quot; attacking something before my health track is close to full of lethal. I guess I'll have to wait and see how regeneration world in the other forms to get the full picture though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:55:52-07:00","id":132349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132308#post132308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh to me its a gamebreaking issue. I'm heavily invested in crossover and I really don't like the concept of innate abilities ignoring the innate abilities of other gamelines, especially those that didn't have the benefit of a later release. I feel its going to lead to an increasingly downward trend in later lines.<br /> <br /> Mages generally don't have substantial innate abilities, most of their power comes from spells, with a few other capabilities. I'm fine with that. I'd be fine with non-Gauru claws dealing lethal if it required some experience investment, even if its a merit similar to Unnatural Affinity (With options to do damage to different major gamelines/1 dot per oddity).<br /> <br /> Werewolves already have what amounts to facets of several disciplines and devotions innately, and I don't mind that. I don't mind the defense against firearms or the Interrupt capability, they don't cancel out another group's innate feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves still dealt Lethal prior to B&amp;S, even in Urhan. It wasn't game-breaking.<br /> <br /> Uratha don't get the benefits of Prey's Blood with them. It isn't game-breaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:06:40-07:00","id":132360,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's game-breaking at all. The idea is laughable, considering you could throw out the rule without a pause. But, thematically, I think it'd make more sense for gauru (who are designed to kill) and urhan (the wolf form), because it's supposed to be representative of Father Wolf, who would certainly give vampires lethal damage.<br /> <br /> I'm torn on urshul, simply because it's not designed to kill.<br /> <br /> However, I do think it's weird that dalu would be able to do lethal damage to vampires with their claws and teeth, unless the form is being changed from slightly larger, feral man to big bear claws and teeth.<br /> <br /> I think having it all available via a merit or facet would be a fine compromise, though it'd have to have some effect more than 'do lethal to vampires,' since that seems to be the kind of ultra-focused option we're trying to get away from in GMC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:17:25-07:00","id":132366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132360#post132360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm torn on urshul, simply because it's not designed to kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? The shape that can bring down a moose on it's own isn't designed to kill? The preferred stalking shape of the Predator Kings, the form of Dire Wolf isn't designed to kill? I'd think otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:22:21-07:00","id":132372,"title":"","content":"I think nofather mixed up the form names like I did earlier in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:41:11-07:00","id":132412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132338#post132338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, one thing I just realized about Gauru form healing all bashing and all lethal every turn allows it to be used as a mid-combat reset button. During a long combat as you get steadily worn down, accumulating more and more lethal damage, once your health track gets a little too close to full, you can just shift to Gauru form for one turn and suddenly you're good as new. I'm not sure if I like that or not. I'll have to see it play out, but it feels like it creates a weird incentive to use Gauru as the healing form rather than the killing form.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a sticking point for me, too - I kind of feel that going Gauru should be an all-or-nothing affair - you use it at the rightmoment to get the kill, rather than heal your wounds. At the moment it seems <i>too</i> durable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T10:57:10-07:00","id":132433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132412#post132412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is a bit of a sticking point for me, too - I kind of feel that going Gauru should be an all-or-nothing affair - you use it at the rightmoment to get the kill, rather than heal your wounds. At the moment it seems <i>too</i> durable.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think you hit a key point with using it at the right moment. In my opinion, the right moment to use it should be the for the killing blow - after you've successfully harried your prey, maneuvered them into a corner, or pressured them into leaving an opening in their guard. But right now, the right moment is when you've got lethal damage marked in all but your last health box. Mechanically speaking, that's when you benefit from it the most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T12:10:47-07:00","id":132605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132366#post132366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? The shape that can bring down a moose on it's own isn't designed to kill? The preferred stalking shape of the Predator Kings, the form of Dire Wolf isn't designed to kill? I'd think otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for sarcasm, and no I didn't get the names wrong.<br /> <br /> As Stew said in the blog, each form has a different part to play in the hunt.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Changing Man &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-changing-man/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hishu (Human)<br /> Used to walk unseen in the world of humans, even on the hunt.<br /> <br /> Dalu (near-human)<br /> Used to isolate and chase foes among humans, where Urhan and Urshul would invite too much attention.<br /> <br /> Gauru (war form)<br /> Used to kill prey as quickly and efficiently as possible. This is for killing, see.<br /> <br /> Urshul (near wolf)<br /> Used to weaken and harry the prey near the end of the hunt. This is not a form only designed for killing. Yes, it -can- kill, but it's not there just for that, or you might as well have dalu and hishu do lethal to vampires because they can kill by using guns. But it is a big hulking wolf. Thus I am torn.<br /> <br /> Urhan (wolf)<br /> Used to chase down prey over long distances, or to harry where Urshul would be noticed. Stew later said, 'Urhan is the form of Father Wolf and the Firstborn, it is the purity of wolf untouched by Luna\u2019s changing energies.' So I figure it could fit with lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-11-2014, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T12:31:47-07:00","id":132620,"title":"","content":"A cornered rat fights much harder than one still on the run. I'd imagine you've harried and cornered your prey, you try to bring it down but it turns out you can't quite handle the desperation-born attacks, so you Gauru, heal up, and finish him off. The Gauru is an unstoppable force, not an assassin. A tank, not a sniper rifle. The efficiency is in the damage output versus damage taken ratio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T12:40:57-07:00","id":132625,"title":"","content":"As some of us stated in opinion form earlier in the thread (I know, who wants to read a dozen+ pages just to reply to a thread), the gauru should not be a tank, it should be a killer, as that's the intent to begin with.<br /> <br /> The mechanics are built for tanking, rather than killing efficiently or quickly, outside of the Quick and Dirty fight rule. But some think it would be improved by a fix to those mechanics, and since the game is in its first draft it's likely they'll change, though we can only hope it does the way we want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-11-2014, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T13:27:09-07:00","id":132729,"title":"","content":"The problem is that while in gamer parlance we use &quot;tank&quot; to mean &quot;low DPS, high aggro management, high survivability,&quot; in the actual function of a tank as a military weapon is to be a fast moving, high powered weapon that's got so much armor on it you need highly specialized weapons and/or tactics to avoid it leveling your forces.<br /> <br /> The Gauru form, as it stands, is a tank in the military sense. Having a lot of survivability aids in being a front-line offensive weapon because you can fire more than once before return fire reduces your ability to apply your offensive weapons (snipers, mortars, unarmored artillery).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T14:10:10-07:00","id":132778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132620#post132620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cornered rat fights much harder than one still on the run. I'd imagine you've harried and cornered your prey, you try to bring it down but it turns out you can't quite handle the desperation-born attacks, so you Gauru, heal up, and finish him off. The Gauru is an unstoppable force, not an assassin. A tank, not a sniper rifle. The efficiency is in the damage output versus damage taken ratio.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as it stands your best tactic to to go in Gauru as early as possibly and not stop until whatever you fight is dead. Urshal should be the form for getting them in position, wearing them down, and the Gauru goes for the throat - that's the quintessential moment as both wolf and werewolf, the kill, crushing the life out of your opponent in a single vicious lunge after you and your pack have harried them, It should be a moment of exaltation but it should also be a moment of danger, the high drama climax of the hunt. Having most of the damage you're likely to take in that final moment disappear detracts from that drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T14:11:59-07:00","id":132781,"title":"","content":"Even in a military sense, the gauru form isn't that offensively imposing the way it exists right now. Most of the danger is going to depend on your brawl ability, instead of your form. The form only gives you survivability, but with a time limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T14:24:57-07:00","id":132788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132311#post132311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest issue with this reasoning is that it's a double standard. By your reasoning it is ok for vampires to be able to innately downgrade a werewolves innate ability to do lethal with their teeth and claws in intermediary forms. Why is that not a gamebreaking issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Having claws doesn't mean it innately deals damage to everything the same. Why should ANY gameline be able to go and be like &quot;Oh we ignore this part of another&quot; by default without any investiture. Lethal damage from claws would be lethal regardless of magic or not, why do they have to be lethal to something that is unliving and specifically is less effected by physical damage?<br /> <br /> One ignoring another is the problem, your presenting the double standard not me. Its okay for werewolves to IGNORE the innate abilities one group has but god forbid something stopped werewolves from healing. I the entire werewolf forum would be up in arms if Prometheans disquiet shut down regeneration.<br /> <br /> There is no double standard of not wanting something ignored by something that is still in development. Why should claws be treated as anything but claws? Thats my point.<br /> <br /> Again if there is an experience investiture, I don't mind. I just don't think that its a good trend to set to have one group having innate abilities that ignore anothers. A claw is a claw, its going to be a weapon even against a vampire, that doesn't mean it effects vampires in the same way. A vampire not needing its internal organs and not being at risk of bleeding out doesn't mean that the damage to the body isn't the same, it just means its not as severe because the thing is already dead.<br /> <br /> It isn't a matter of a double standard as much as its a concern over what I consider a very poor design choice in the outlook of crossover.<br /> <br /> And for those pushing &quot;Oh you can houserule it&quot;, again I and many others don't like houserules. I for the most part go as close to the book as possible. My only exception I make is the wonkery with blood sorcery's improvised vs learned rituals.<br /> <br /> But with Rose's point on Vinculum, I'm not as worried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 05-11-2014, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T14:29:09-07:00","id":132790,"title":"","content":"If we are discussing where a werewolf should stand when compared to a vampire, I guess I might as well throw in my opinion. I think the average werewolf should have a dot or two more in combat skills than an average vampire of similar experience. Now for forms, I think the near-human should be comparable to a neonate vampire. The war form and near wolf should be on par with a combat specialized vampire. I think an elder vampire should be able to kill a single average werewolf without much trouble. As far as white rooms go, I think it should be considered as the two meet without any preparation. My idea of balance is the fight could go either way so the smarter fighter usually wins. I like the idea of vampires preferring to flee rather than fight werewolves, unless it is Bruce Leepire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Obviously, Elders and combat junkies should only be afraid of a whole pack. I'm not even sure an Elder should even be afraid of a pack if it is full of noobs. If suggestions are being taken, that is what I would want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T14:55:55-07:00","id":132806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132781#post132781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in a military sense, the gauru form isn't that offensively imposing the way it exists right now. Most of the danger is going to depend on your brawl ability, instead of your form. The form only gives you survivability, but with a time limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're sorely underestimating how important survivability is in actually killing things. There's a reason that the scariest weapons we have are measured in terms of range rather than sheer damage output: if the other person can't hit back, then failing to kill them in the first shot means that you can hit them again. And again. And again. Something as simple as a machine gun is more about suppressing return fire than actually killing. The Gauru declines to be suppressed: it just walks through it.<br /> <br /> If you don't have that survivability, then the other person can rock you back onto the defense. When you're invincible, that's no longer an option. The other person can only run away. If you did the rest of the hunt right, they were cornered already and they are out of options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132778#post132778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as it stands your best tactic to to go in Gauru as early as possibly and not stop until whatever you fight is dead. Urshal should be the form for getting them in position, wearing them down, and the Gauru goes for the throat - that's the quintessential moment as both wolf and werewolf, the kill, crushing the life out of your opponent in a single vicious lunge after you and your pack have harried them, It should be a moment of exaltation but it should also be a moment of danger, the high drama climax of the hunt. Having most of the damage you're likely to take in that final moment disappear detracts from that drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree. Going Gauru early means they can run away, or they still have tricks to pull out. You should be drawing out their desperation tactics during the hunt and burning through their ability to fight back. Going Gauru is a response to their &quot;nothing else matters; I have to win NOW&quot; card... and then you heal it all and hit them in the face. They throw away everything to kill you and you hit them again without blinking.<br /> <br /> I feel that if you go Gauru early, you play your hand too soon. Crossing the finish line isn't a moment of danger; it's a moment of victory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T15:03:44-07:00","id":132813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132790#post132790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are discussing where a werewolf should stand when compared to a vampire, I guess I might as well throw in my opinion. I think the average werewolf should have a dot or two more in combat skills than an average vampire of similar experience. Now for forms, I think the near-human should be comparable to a neonate vampire. The war form and near wolf should be on par with a combat specialized vampire. I think an elder vampire should be able to kill a single average werewolf without much trouble. As far as white rooms go, I think it should be considered as the two meet without any preparation. My idea of balance is the fight could go either way so the smarter fighter usually wins. I like the idea of vampires preferring to flee rather than fight werewolves, unless it is Bruce Leepire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Obviously, Elders and combat junkies should only be afraid of a whole pack. I'm not even sure an Elder should even be afraid of a pack if it is full of noobs. If suggestions are being taken, that is what I would want.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that game balance is a myth. I personally hold to the motto that games should be balanced around themselves, not against others. Now obviously if they are good, they will at least consider the others, but not make it the primary factor. Fact of the matter is Vampires and Werewolves are both apex predators and would only come to blows if their issues overlap in a forceful way. Most of the time, they leave each other alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T15:11:36-07:00","id":132823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132788#post132788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having claws doesn't mean it innately deals damage to everything the same. Why should ANY gameline be able to go and be like &quot;Oh we ignore this part of another&quot; by default without any investiture. Lethal damage from claws would be lethal regardless of magic or not, why do they have to be lethal to something that is unliving and specifically is less effected by physical damage?<br /> <br /> One ignoring another is the problem, your presenting the double standard not me. Its okay for werewolves to IGNORE the innate abilities one group has but god forbid something stopped werewolves from healing. I the entire werewolf forum would be up in arms if Prometheans disquiet shut down regeneration.<br /> <br /> There is no double standard of not wanting something ignored by something that is still in development. Why should claws be treated as anything but claws? Thats my point.<br /> <br /> Again if there is an experience investiture, I don't mind. I just don't think that its a good trend to set to have one group having innate abilities that ignore anothers. A claw is a claw, its going to be a weapon even against a vampire, that doesn't mean it effects vampires in the same way. A vampire not needing its internal organs and not being at risk of bleeding out doesn't mean that the damage to the body isn't the same, it just means its not as severe because the thing is already dead.<br /> <br /> It isn't a matter of a double standard as much as its a concern over what I consider a very poor design choice in the outlook of crossover.<br /> <br /> And for those pushing &quot;Oh you can houserule it&quot;, again I and many others don't like houserules. I for the most part go as close to the book as possible. My only exception I make is the wonkery with blood sorcery's improvised vs learned rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf claws innately deal lethal just like vampire bodies innately downgrades lethal. However you want to spin it, by design werewolf claws deal lethal damage (not bashing), that is a part of how they work. You are saying it is ok for vampires to force werewolves to deal bashing, downgrading the intended aspect of werewolves innate shapeshifting abilities but it's not ok for their innate shapeshifting abilities to allow them to continue to do lethal on vampires.<br /> <br /> I've actually not presented a double standard, because while I prefer one way over another it's that I feel one is more appropriate, not because it's unfair for one side to do something and it not apply the other way around like you are specifically stating. You're also trying to change the subject by bringing up something completely irrelevant to the argument at hand, and stating false claims about issues that no one else is arguing (werewolf regeneration). We'll come back to that point later, but right now, we aren't talking about either sides self healing, so stop trying to straw man me bro.<br /> <br /> Because those claws belong to supernatural half spirit beasts and the devs seemed to think they should (because while they might change their mind because of the fuss a portion of the vampire forum is kicking up and change it due to the reaction of certain people they obviously thought it was a decent enough idea when the first posted about it. Even now they're testing the waters with a poll instead of just going with what they feel is appropriate.). Why is it ok for vampire damage downgrade to reduce the stated damage type of a werewolves innate natural weaponry? My answer would be that neither is more ok than the other, what matters is what feels most appropriate, and if the werewolf devs feel that werewolf claws bypassing damage mitigation is suitably appropriate for apex predators and master hunters like werewolves then I'd agree with them.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't have to pay experience to downgrade werewolf claw damage why do werewolves need a merit to do the damage their supernatural weaponry states they do? And if a claw was a claw then protean 4 wouldn't deal lethal. Regardless of whether or not you spend xp for it, it's still just a claw attack. There's nothing spiritual about it, it's still tearing through dead flesh just as werewolves claws do. By your logic that should also deal bashing, since no matter what they cut they're still cutting dead flesh which vampires don't need.<br /> <br /> Your reasoning is a matter of double standards, though why you cling to it is because you prefer one game design option over the other, you just happen to favor the vampire side of this issue.. Which is fine, you have your preferences, as does everyone. But you should just say that it's your preference instead of trying to act like it's something else. It's no more or less improper or unfair for vampires to downgrade other splats supernatural ways of dealing damage than it is for them to be able to bypass it. The only thing that matters is how appropriate people feel it is. You feel it is inappropriate, I do not. The decision will be made based off of how appropriate most parties see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-11-2014, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T16:18:54-07:00","id":132856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132823#post132823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf claws innately deal lethal just like vampire bodies innately downgrades lethal. However you want to spin it, by design werewolf claws deal lethal damage (not bashing), that is a part of how they work. You are saying it is ok for vampires to force werewolves to deal bashing, downgrading the intended aspect of werewolves innate shapeshifting abilities but it's not ok for their innate shapeshifting abilities to allow them to continue to do lethal on vampires.<br /> <br /> I've actually not presented a double standard, because while I prefer one way over another it's that I feel one is more appropriate, not because it's unfair for one side to do something and it not apply the other way around like you are specifically stating. You're also trying to change the subject by bringing up something completely irrelevant to the argument at hand, and stating false claims about issues that no one else is arguing (werewolf regeneration). We'll come back to that point later, but right now, we aren't talking about either sides self healing, so stop trying to straw man me bro.<br /> <br /> Because those claws belong to supernatural half spirit beasts and the devs seemed to think they should (because while they might change their mind because of the fuss a portion of the vampire forum is kicking up and change it due to the reaction of certain people they obviously thought it was a decent enough idea when the first posted about it. Even now they're testing the waters with a poll instead of just going with what they feel is appropriate.). Why is it ok for vampire damage downgrade to reduce the stated damage type of a werewolves innate natural weaponry? My answer would be that neither is more ok than the other, what matters is what feels most appropriate, and if the werewolf devs feel that werewolf claws bypassing damage mitigation is suitably appropriate for apex predators and master hunters like werewolves then I'd agree with them.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't have to pay experience to downgrade werewolf claw damage why do werewolves need a merit to do the damage their supernatural weaponry states they do? And if a claw was a claw then protean 4 wouldn't deal lethal. Regardless of whether or not you spend xp for it, it's still just a claw attack. There's nothing spiritual about it, it's still tearing through dead flesh just as werewolves claws do. By your logic that should also deal bashing, since no matter what they cut they're still cutting dead flesh which vampires don't need.<br /> <br /> Your reasoning is a matter of double standards, though why you cling to it is because you prefer one game design option over the other, you just happen to favor the vampire side of this issue.. Which is fine, you have your preferences, as does everyone. But you should just say that it's your preference instead of trying to act like it's something else. It's no more or less improper or unfair for vampires to downgrade other splats supernatural ways of dealing damage than it is for them to be able to bypass it. The only thing that matters is how appropriate people feel it is. You feel it is inappropriate, I do not. The decision will be made based off of how appropriate most parties see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire's aren't downgrading the claws. Vampires are simply not affected in the same way that living things would be.<br /> <br /> That is the difference. They aren't doing anything. They just are. The only thing it effects is how a vampire heals the damage. It is the only thing being ignored. Werewolves doing lethal damage to things within werewolf's overall purview is one thing, but its an entirely different concept when it starts applying to others.<br /> <br /> It isn't a double standard. Its simply a position that one group shouldn't innately bypass innate abilities of others. Whether they be vampire, werewolf or prometheans.<br /> <br /> Again, how would you think if Disquiet made werewolves unable to regenerate without essence?<br /> <br /> I think its a bad design to make features that distinctively have impacts on the features of other groups. A vampire's undead body has no effect on whether a werewolf can kill a spirit, human, or anything else. However a werewolves innate ability to ignore a vampire's innate ability is the only one being ignored.<br /> <br /> If a werewolf doesn't innately do that, then no innate ability is being ignored, the damage is still the same regardless, how a vampire's body holds up is what is in question. You keep pushing this, and its a clear bias, because I'm not talking just about werewolf. I think it should apply across all lines that innate abilities do not cancel out innate abilities of others. One should not be made that automatically ignores this. I don't think They should begin this trend with werewolf and end up with werewolf getting shafted by other lines either. It doesn't mean anything to werewolf's other capabilities, it just impacts whether other major gamelines just get shit on by the next one released.<br /> <br /> Its a bad precedent, and has impact on the enjoyment others have. You're falsely calling it a double standard when you've not got all of the features. Werewolves are apparently getting a gift that is highly effective against vampires, I have no issue with that. My issue is the precedent set by this situation of next line has to be better than last. I think ignoring innate abilities in the design of new innate abilities is a bad way to go about it.<br /> <br /> A vampire doesn't innately make you lose the claws, you still have the claws, you can do any number of things with the claws you couldn't before, including making attacks that wouldn't be possible with unarmed damage (tilts and things that require tissue loss) etc. The damage is still done, its simply a matter of how vampires should react to it.<br /> <br /> If you were saying I'm pushing a double standard, I'd be saying werewolves lose claws completely, and this isn't the case. Called shots with claws would still be worse than called shots with fists. There's a major difference there.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T16:40:13-07:00","id":132871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132778#post132778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But as it stands your best tactic to to go in Gauru as early as possibly and not stop until whatever you fight is dead. Urshal should be the form for getting them in position, wearing them down, and the Gauru goes for the throat - that's the quintessential moment as both wolf and werewolf, the kill, crushing the life out of your opponent in a single vicious lunge after you and your pack have harried them, It should be a moment of exaltation but it should also be a moment of danger, the high drama climax of the hunt. Having most of the damage you're likely to take in that final moment disappear detracts from that drama.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. Due to the limited time and full healing, the best tactic is to save it until your health track is almost full, then use it to instantly clear it all back out again. If you use it that way it's like having double your normal amount of health in addition to your healing. I have no problem with the high durability, in fact I think it's very appropriate for the form. But since it heals all bashing and lethal, the more damage you've taken the more you benefit from the healing. That, combined with the limited time in the form discouraging you from blowing it too early, strongly incentivizes using the form as a healing tool instead of a damage dealing tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:13:28-07:00","id":132906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132856#post132856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire's aren't downgrading the claws. Vampires are simply not affected in the same way that living things would be.<br /> <br /> That is the difference. They aren't doing anything. They just are. The only thing it effects is how a vampire heals the damage. It is the only thing being ignored. Werewolves doing lethal damage to things within werewolf's overall purview is one thing, but its an entirely different concept when it starts applying to others.<br /> <br /> It isn't a double standard. Its simply a position that one group shouldn't innately bypass innate abilities of others. Whether they be vampire, werewolf or prometheans.<br /> <br /> Again, how would you think if Disquiet made werewolves unable to regenerate without essence?<br /> <br /> I think its a bad design to make features that distinctively have impacts on the features of other groups. A vampire's undead body has no effect on whether a werewolf can kill a spirit, human, or anything else. However a werewolves innate ability to ignore a vampire's innate ability is the only one being ignored.<br /> <br /> If a werewolf doesn't innately do that, then no innate ability is being ignored, the damage is still the same regardless, how a vampire's body holds up is what is in question. You keep pushing this, and its a clear bias, because I'm not talking just about werewolf. I think it should apply across all lines that innate abilities do not cancel out innate abilities of others. One should not be made that automatically ignores this. I don't think They should begin this trend with werewolf and end up with werewolf getting shafted by other lines either. It doesn't mean anything to werewolf's other capabilities, it just impacts whether other major gamelines just get shit on by the next one released.<br /> <br /> Its a bad precedent, and has impact on the enjoyment others have. You're falsely calling it a double standard when you've not got all of the features. Werewolves are apparently getting a gift that is highly effective against vampires, I have no issue with that. My issue is the precedent set by this situation of next line has to be better than last. I think ignoring innate abilities in the design of new innate abilities is a bad way to go about it.<br /> <br /> A vampire doesn't innately make you lose the claws, you still have the claws, you can do any number of things with the claws you couldn't before, including making attacks that wouldn't be possible with unarmed damage (tilts and things that require tissue loss) etc. The damage is still done, its simply a matter of how vampires should react to it.<br /> <br /> If you were saying I'm pushing a double standard, I'd be saying werewolves lose claws completely, and this isn't the case. Called shots with claws would still be worse than called shots with fists. There's a major difference there.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>By that logic, werewolf claws aren't doing anything either. The section that talks about the damage reduction says they take downgraded damage from many sources that would deal lethal to humans, specifying most non-supernatural weapons. All the werewolf line is doing is stating that werewolf teeth and claws count as supernatural weapons. So by that logic, werewolves also aren't doing anything, that's just how 'they are', as you put it. You are still using that same double standard. Why are werewolves restricted to things within their purview and not vampires? Spirit tempered claws aren't under a vampires purview, so how can you arguing that they get to affect the damage type those claws deal?<br /> <br /> But it <i>is</i> a double standard when you allow such things for vampires using weak excuses like 'it's just how they are', yet complain when the reverse happens.<br /> <br /> I would first question why, because those two things are so hilariously far removed from each other that I can't see how one relates to the other. Claws and dead flesh to be clawed are related, regeneration and an aura that makes you hate someone aren't even in the same ballpark. That said, if you gave me a semi-good reason why it would, sure, why not?<br /> <br /> The claws of werewolves have no effect on how vampires downgrade damage caused by swords, guns, clubs, fists, cars, or anything else they are resistant to. Currently, a vampires innate damage downgrade ignores the proper damage type dealt by werewolf claws, where's your issue with that? Their innate ability directly modifies that of another splat in which they should have no bearing on. It is literally the same damn thing. Yet you're fine with it working one way but say for it to work the other way is gamebreaking. That's called a double standard.<br /> <br /> I could say the same for vampire damage downgrade. I can imagine having their innate supernatural weaponry reduced to dealing bashing would have an impact on werewolf players. And again, it's not like this wasn't set up in B&amp;S anyways. The fact that they completely left out supernatural weaponry sources in the book, seemingly intentionally, is the cause of this. when talking about lethal damage being reduced to bashing they only mention that most non-supernatural sources are reduced, implying that supernatural sources (probably with some exceptions) bypass the effect. So it's not even ignoring the effect, it is simply specifying that it belongs in the category in which the book itself has no mention of being able to reduce.<br /> <br /> A werewolf doesn't innately make your body alive. You are still undead, you can resist any number of things that you couldn't before, including attacks that would formally be lethal (numina immediately comes to mind).<br /> <br /> No, you are saying it isn't fine for one splay to disregard the stated mechanics of another, yet you are promoting just that, while vehemently denying a reversal of the situation. Werewolf claws innately deal lethal damage, and you are promoting a mechanic that alters that. Yes or no, innate werewolf claws deal lethal? Yes or no, you want to allow an innate vampire feature to alter the damage that innate werewolf feature deals, for all intents and purposes removing the claws and making them count as a punch with a +1 weapon damage. Yes or no, you don't want innate features of one splat to overrule the innate features of another. If you answer yes to these then you are contradicting yourself, and proposing a double standard. If you answer no to the first then you need to go recheck the damage types. If you answer no to the second then we don't have a problem. If you answer no to the third then what is the basis of your argument?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-11-2014, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:19:51-07:00","id":132910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132806#post132806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're sorely underestimating how important survivability is in actually killing things. There's a reason that the scariest weapons we have are measured in terms of range rather than sheer damage output: if the other person can't hit back, then failing to kill them in the first shot means that you can hit them again. And again. And again. Something as simple as a machine gun is more about suppressing return fire than actually killing. The Gauru declines to be suppressed: it just walks through it.<br /> <br /> If you don't have that survivability, then the other person can rock you back onto the defense. When you're invincible, that's no longer an option. The other person can only run away. If you did the rest of the hunt right, they were cornered already and they are out of options.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually part of my point. Going into gauru is probably a worse idea than simply staying out of range and shooting. A rifle or shotgun will do more damage, with reflexive shifting you can likely stay out of range with the increased speed of wolf-form. Because when you're in gauru all something has to do is tie you up for a bit, by grappling or whomping on the head for a stun or simply moving out of the range before it can hit you. In that last case it may even attack one of its allies, since they may end up close than you, it's just wasting its time in gauru since it doesn't have the damage to quickly kill something that can kill.<br /> <br /> The whole point of the form is killing things quickly and efficiently, but beyond the Down and Dirty combat, the mechanics do not support this. No one's saying being able to full heal isn't great, but survivability does not equate to quick and efficient killing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:29:48-07:00","id":132927,"title":"","content":"I don't want to be a conversation killer, but can we pick one thread to argue about vampire damage reduction in? Going back and forth between the two is a little tedious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:36:28-07:00","id":132935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132910#post132910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is actually part of my point. Going into gauru is probably a worse idea than simply staying out of range and shooting. A rifle or shotgun will do more damage, with reflexive shifting you can likely stay out of range with the increased speed of wolf-form. Because when you're in gauru all something has to do is tie you up for a bit, by grappling or whomping on the head for a stun or simply moving out of the range before it can hit you. In that last case it may even attack one of its allies, since they may end up close than you, it's just wasting its time in gauru since it doesn't have the damage to quickly kill something that can kill. The whole point of the form is killing things quickly and efficiently, but beyond the Down and Dirty combat, the mechanics do not support this. No one's saying being able to full heal isn't great, but survivability does not equate to quick and efficient killing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I am actually saying the full heal isn't great lol. I mean, I love the awesome amount of survivability, but I'm worried this particular way of achieving it encourages using the form as a means of resetting your health instead of a means of killing stuff. Though, making the form more lethal may fix that without having to change the healing, which would be preferable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:46:46-07:00","id":132939,"title":"","content":"If your players want to run it that way it is a perfectly viable tactic. me being a cahalith I intend to full well war form and smash into the side of someones moving semi truck to make their life an active nightmare. Hell let the damn truck hit me while in war form! I'll get up and rip the damn door off without being stopped and eat the poor bastard.<br /> <br /> Ya'll are thinking too hard about the form being possibly broken and ignoring the fun possibilities that comes with it.<br /> <br /> Also loving the complaints against werewolves doing lethal to vampires, when one of the complaints (again) is the warform being too weak. Jeez people pick your battles. You want it to have power and in the same breath complain because now characters you may never run into happen to take lethal to it now? Cause vampires don't have a way to heal lethal on their own anyway amirite?<br /> <br /> Edit: to add to my growing confusion on complaints, some of you act like the werewolf loses power going into warform. He doesn't. The base stats still increase, and there is still the drive for pack combat. Just because the more human forms can add weaponry damage does not make them stronger then the warform. It makes them adaptable, which is what humans are anyway. It would be like saying the Primal Form is acctually weaker then the near man form because it doesn't deal range damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 05-11-2014, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:54:00-07:00","id":132943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132927#post132927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to be a conversation killer, but can we pick one thread to argue about vampire damage reduction in? Going back and forth between the two is a little tedious.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're arguing mechanic legitimacy involving existing rules and the proposed rules for werewolf shapeshifting. I feel that it's best to deal with this sooner rather than lather, and we are providing insight into both sides of the issue, something the devs can take into consideration when making the call. <br /> <br /> Besides, I need to warm up for my keyboard crusade for when the Fallen World Chronicles is in open development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T17:57:48-07:00","id":132948,"title":"","content":"If you want a forsaken players standpoint on that debate Ashenrogue, it looks to me like the Vamp players are crying foul because now they cant outright nerf our main claw attacks by virtue of just being. It wouldn't make sense for me to not be able to do lethal in Garou form at least to vampires, given the emphasis on killing things, and the fact that the form itself is half spirit.<br /> <br /> Hell the wolfen forms are based on spirit wolves not real wolves, so the supernatural element in the claws should be innate. It isn't like the Uratha grow normal claws from a wolf, they grow spiritually imbued claws from being half spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:15:41-07:00","id":132957,"title":"","content":"I Myself thinks that Werewolf claw should deliver Lethal damage to vampire. They are considered supernatural now, and if vampire players fears the fact that a gauru is relatively stronger physicaly than the same experience character vampire... well, what to say ? It was like... always the case in the past. I play vampire and werewolf, and having your character vampire feeling some fear and acting carefully around the fury and angry apex predator of this world, is just normal in my eyes. Mage outshine vamps in power, and werewolf, outshine them physically. So what ? Vampire outshine both of them in plots, manipulation, and by carefull use of contacts and of their jack of all trades versatility...<br /> <br /> In any case, I also think that the gauru should heal faster. Gauru is the &quot;warform&quot; but also the raging form. Gauru in control is like... the vampire &quot;riding the wave&quot; in a sort of way. Having him deal more damage, and heal faster is the way to go. After all, if they heal quickly naturaly... what should they do in an &quot;overcloacked, orveride mode&quot; ? Then again, I do think that regenerating all their lethal, is far too much. Something based on their primal urge seems appropriate. I prefer the damage dealing werewolf to the imortal werewolf. Werewolf should be hard to kill... really hard to kill... but they are not immortal in battle. Harming a gauru should not be the main problem for an enemy... unless he uses bashing... wich is stupid. Surviving them should be the problem. The bestial, monstrous horror that they are, should put fear inside the spirit of almost anyone.<br /> <br /> However, I have a question ? Do we still use the 8 or 9 again rule ? They are not mentionned anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:21:32-07:00","id":132997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132943#post132943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We're arguing mechanic legitimacy involving existing rules and the proposed rules for werewolf shapeshifting. I feel that it's best to deal with this sooner rather than lather, and we are providing insight into both sides of the issue, something the devs can take into consideration when making the call. Besides, I need to warm up for my keyboard crusade for when the Fallen World Chronicles is in open development.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh don't get me wrong, I do think it's an important conversation to have. That's why I've been such an active participant in it myself. I just think it would be better to keep the discussion all in the same place so someone following it doesn't have to go back and forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:26:21-07:00","id":132998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132948#post132948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a forsaken players standpoint on that debate Ashenrogue, it looks to me like the Vamp players are crying foul because now they cant outright nerf our main claw attacks by virtue of just being. It wouldn't make sense for me to not be able to do lethal in Garou form at least to vampires, given the emphasis on killing things, and the fact that the form itself is half spirit. Hell the wolfen forms are based on spirit wolves not real wolves, so the supernatural element in the claws should be innate. It isn't like the Uratha grow normal claws from a wolf, they grow spiritually imbued claws from being half spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, I don't think its beneficial to divide people into &quot;werewolf players&quot; and &quot;vampire players&quot;. I think most of us play both games, and while we all have preferences and biases, labeling people based on them will only cause dissension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:29:32-07:00","id":133000,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Gauru healing, I'm also thinking it might be a tad too much, but I'm not quite sure how I'd change it. Since lethal is the standard damage type nowadays, because weapons no longer ever deal bashing, it has to be able to heal fairly large amounts of it every turn, but I'm wondering if healing all of it is going overboard. I might suggest changing it to passively healing lethal equal to your passive healing rate (or maybe your healing rate as if your primal urge was considered 1 or even 2 points higher, it depends on the exact numbers here tbh) and still being able to spend a point of essence to heal additional lethal equal to your natural normal regeneration rate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132997#post132997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh don't get me wrong, I do think it's an important conversation to have. That's why I've been such an active participant in it myself. I just think it would be better to keep the discussion all in the same place so someone following it doesn't have to go back and forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's reasonable enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-11-2014, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:31:55-07:00","id":133004,"title":"","content":"remember the form is usually around 20 seconds of usage though. And per what... story? Scene? It isn't like the characters can always take the warform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:38:19-07:00","id":133011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133004#post133004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">remember the form is usually around 20 seconds of usage though. And per what... story? Scene? It isn't like the characters can always take the warform.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another good point. How often will you be able to enter war form? I'd like to see it used more than once per gaming session, but I'm not sure if it's too powerful to be an every scene kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:38:44-07:00","id":133012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133004#post133004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">remember the form is usually around 20 seconds of usage though. And per what... story? Scene? It isn't like the characters can always take the warform.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's exactly why you're better off not taking it unless your damage track is full. Every health box not filled when you take the war form is a point of healing wasted. When you only get to use the form for precious few moments, you're going to want to get as much benefit out of the time you do get as possible. Which means the most efficient use of it is not when you want to kill something, but when you're close to death and want to get a fresh start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:40:33-07:00","id":133013,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd really just want clarification as to what counts as a supernatural source of damage for the purposes of overcoming a Vampire's inherent resilience since it's going to come up a lot as more books come out. As long as Klaives qualify though, I don't really mind if the inherent weapons of the intermittent forms don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:44:40-07:00","id":133030,"title":"","content":"At the moment it is. With the limitation of the form the healing bonus isnt that big of a deal. It IS for the cahalith to be the nightmare. For the Rahu to be the siege tank. For the Irraka to be the unstoppable assassin. We use it only when the moment is right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:52:15-07:00","id":133032,"title":"","content":"Still, the fact that it is tank form instead of wreck form is slightly disappointing regardless of how effective it is. I for one would be happier with half of the healing capability with an additional quarter damage. If already people are reading it as a damage soak and heal instead of ripping something to shreds, it seems to go against the intended purpose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T18:52:39-07:00","id":133033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133030#post133030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment it is. With the limitation of the form the healing bonus isnt that big of a deal. It IS for the cahalith to be the nightmare. For the Rahu to be the siege tank. For the Irraka to be the unstoppable assassin. We use it only when the moment is right.</div> </div> </div> </div> We must be misunderstanding each other. The limitation of the form is, in my opinion, the very reason the healing bonus is a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T19:08:46-07:00","id":133042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133032#post133032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still, the fact that it is tank form instead of wreck form is slightly disappointing regardless of how effective it is. I for one would be happier with half of the healing capability with an additional quarter damage. If already people are reading it as a damage soak and heal instead of ripping something to shreds, it seems to go against the intended purpose</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly confused as to how people can be given a white room scenario of a newbie werewolf taking down a vampire elder and consider that &quot;against the intended purpose&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T19:25:41-07:00","id":133052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133042#post133042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm honestly confused as to how people can be given a white room scenario of a newbie werewolf taking down a vampire elder and consider that &amp;quot;against the intended purpose&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because white rooms don't really mean much. That scenario was specifically designed to test the survivability of the form, and it took way longer than you could reasonably expect to be in the form, and didn't take the death rage mechanics into account (mainly because we don't know them yet, but that doesn't change the fact that it's a very important factor not taken into account). The main thing the form actually does is heal itself. But the fluff presents it as the form that delivers swift and brutal death, not the form that survives anything and kills the enemy by winning an attrition war. Obviously there is a disconnect between the forms stated purpose and what it actually does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T19:29:34-07:00","id":133055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=132948#post132948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a forsaken players standpoint on that debate Ashenrogue, it looks to me like the Vamp players are crying foul because now they cant outright nerf our main claw attacks by virtue of just being. It wouldn't make sense for me to not be able to do lethal in Garou form at least to vampires, given the emphasis on killing things, and the fact that the form itself is half spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone has been fine with Gauru form doing lethal, I don't think anyone has said anything about Gauru form, only the two others of the three. That is my problem with it. And it isn't cancelling an innate power that isn't even out yet, at this point its hope for design not to go in the direction of ignoring things already out and established. Undead flesh and downgrading is the vampire equivalent of natural healing for werewolf, sure a vampire can spend vitae for lethal, just as a werewolf can (But apparently werewolves heal more efficiently as their PU goes up), but its essentially the same situation and equivalent.<br /> <br /> The issue is whether a game that is in development should be able to just handwave another group's innate capabilities. Werewolves as of Forsaken until Idigam Chronicles comes out don't have anything that says they innately bypass it in all 3 forms because it was obviously written before. And B&amp;S is basically suffering the same issue of getting its update first. Its upgrades that were great and necessary are of little consequence to a werewolf even without gifts or specialization.<br /> <br /> I don't think its right that werewolves can ignore a vampire's natural defenses while still retaining their own in the same situation. It isn't about one trumping the other as much as it is I'm worried about a precedent being set that future gamelines can just easily ignore basic features of others in crossover games.<br /> <br /> Some games are run as crossovers where more than one gameline is represented by PC's. It happens, almost every game I've played in and every game I've run have been this way. It isn't about NPC's from one line or the other but how PC's of both groups react in such situations.<br /> <br /> I would be fine with increasing the weapon modifier of claws and teeth in Gauru, as well as its attribute bonuses and even armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T20:00:04-07:00","id":133102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133055#post133055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone has been fine with Gauru form doing lethal, I don't think anyone has said anything about Gauru form, only the two others of the three. That is my problem with it. And it isn't cancelling an innate power that isn't even out yet, at this point its hope for design not to go in the direction of ignoring things already out and established. Undead flesh and downgrading is the vampire equivalent of natural healing for werewolf, sure a vampire can spend vitae for lethal, just as a werewolf can (But apparently werewolves heal more efficiently as their PU goes up), but its essentially the same situation and equivalent.<br /> <br /> The issue is whether a game that is in development should be able to just handwave another group's innate capabilities. Werewolves as of Forsaken until Idigam Chronicles comes out don't have anything that says they innately bypass it in all 3 forms because it was obviously written before. And B&amp;S is basically suffering the same issue of getting its update first. Its upgrades that were great and necessary are of little consequence to a werewolf even without gifts or specialization.<br /> <br /> I don't think its right that werewolves can ignore a vampire's natural defenses while still retaining their own in the same situation. It isn't about one trumping the other as much as it is I'm worried about a precedent being set that future gamelines can just easily ignore basic features of others in crossover games.<br /> <br /> Some games are run as crossovers where more than one gameline is represented by PC's. It happens, almost every game I've played in and every game I've run have been this way. It isn't about NPC's from one line or the other but how PC's of both groups react in such situations.<br /> <br /> I would be fine with increasing the weapon modifier of claws and teeth in Gauru, as well as its attribute bonuses and even armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, are we continuing this argument here because I'm not sure if I should dissect this here or elsewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T20:02:44-07:00","id":133127,"title":"","content":"I think people are going to continue the discussion wherever it pops up, so may as well. At least it's on topic here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T20:18:02-07:00","id":133130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133127#post133127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people are going to continue the discussion wherever it pops up, so may as well. At least it's on topic here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'm kinda bored of it now tbh. Regardless, we've both cast our votes. I vote to keep it, Rani votes to get rid of it. We'll see how the rest of the voting turns out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T01:39:54-07:00","id":133371,"title":"","content":"Here's a nifty solution that I have ported from the other forum, as the discussion seems split over two places.<br /> <br /> Keep all the wolf stats the same: the vamps downgrade also the same lathal damage to bashing. But add:<br /> <br /> *Rend and Maul: In a grapple, Gauru form jaws act as +2 Agg weapons, as the wolf beast tears flesh and bone apart in gobfuls.<br /> <br /> Vamps would downgrade this to lethal - retaining their downgrade ability, but still victim to the wolf if they let themselves get caught. Suddenly, Gauru vs Gauru fights have meaning, rather the prolonged pointless roll-fests. The deadliness of Gauru form is raised without having to alter their heal - which for me is a major new selling point.<br /> <br /> As long as Kuruth has significant downsides so it isn't just seen as a reliable get-out-of-jail free card (which I am sure it isn't, and we will find out today) there is no problem. This could be tweaked: the Agg upgrade could always be on, or could cost essence per turn etc. My problem was that, with no further expense - Gauru seemed to bypass an ability that cost vamps significant xp expenditure to byspass the same (Protean 4): but this doesn't do that. The vamps are still better off vs this bite than a human - and a vamp should be better off at surviving a werewolf bite than a hedge-fund manager. But the werewolves have a meaningful threat to bring to bear vs all prey - and the form is made for killing. And tanking.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","user":"hoodedclaw","date":". 05-12-2014, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T02:25:46-07:00","id":133399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133371#post133371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a nifty solution that I have ported from the other forum, as the discussion seems split over two places.<br /> <br /> Keep all the wolf states the same: the vamps downgrade also the same. But add:<br /> <br /> *Rend and Maul: In a grapple, Gauru form jaws act as +2 Agg weapons, as the wolf beast tears flesh and bone apart in gobfuls.<br /> <br /> Vamps would downgrade this to lethal - retaining their downgrade ability, but still victim to the wolf if they let themselves get caught. Suddenly, Gauru vs Gauru fights have meaning, rather the prolonged pointless roll-fests. The deadliness of Gauru form is raised without having to alter their heal - which for me is a major new selling point.<br /> <br /> As long as Kuruth has significant downsides so it isn't just seen as a reliable get-out-of-jail free card (which I am sure it isn't, and we will find out today) there is no problem. This could be tweaked: the Agg upgrade could always be on, or could cost essence per turn etc. My problem was that, with no further expense - Gauru seemed to bypass an ability that cost vamps significant xp expenditure: but this doesn't do that. The vamps are still better off vs this than a human - and a vamp should be better off at surviving a werewolf bight than a hedge-fund manager. But the werewolves have a meaningful threat to bring to bear vs all prey - and the form is made for killing. And tanking.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a good solution to the current issue in any way. Agg in general seems to be becoming much rarer as a damage type in general and I feel it's extremely out of place to add it here. Besides, as has been stated, no one has a problem with Gauru dealing lethal to vampires anyways. This still doesn't solve the actual problem, which is the unclear wording used in the damage downgrade section of vampire. The fact that they state that most non-supernatural weapons, heavily implying fully supernatural weapons are exempt to this rule, are downgraded. That is what is causing the problem. This is a crossover issue that deals with the fact that by it's wording, all (or at least most) explicitly supernatural powers that deal lethal bypass the alteration. People complained and MachineIV gave his own ruling of it that could be taken two ways. The first interpretation kept it mostly the same, while the second requires any effect that would bypass it, regardless of which line said effect came from, to have to explicitly call out vampires in order to have it working as intended. We've seen the kind of keyboard crusades people waged this time when another line specifically mentions something bypasses it, so to have every line be forced to specifically call it out time and time again will cause no end to the bellyaching.<br /> <br /> As for werewolves bypassing an ability that vampires have to spend xp on, that is false. We're talking about nothing but innate abilities here. And a vampire is better off taking this than a funds manager, because they have the ability to heal it off with relatively little effort. So again, we aren't even arguing over the war form, it is fine as is (if not a little too intensive in the healing department).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-12-2014, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T05:15:30-07:00","id":133516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133055#post133055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone has been fine with Gauru form doing lethal, I don't think anyone has said anything about Gauru form, only the two others of the three. That is my problem with it. And it isn't cancelling an innate power that isn't even out yet, at this point its hope for design not to go in the direction of ignoring things already out and established. Undead flesh and downgrading is the vampire equivalent of natural healing for werewolf, sure a vampire can spend vitae for lethal, just as a werewolf can (But apparently werewolves heal more efficiently as their PU goes up), but its essentially the same situation and equivalent.<br /> <br /> The issue is whether a game that is in development should be able to just handwave another group's innate capabilities. Werewolves as of Forsaken until Idigam Chronicles comes out don't have anything that says they innately bypass it in all 3 forms because it was obviously written before. And B&amp;S is basically suffering the same issue of getting its update first. Its upgrades that were great and necessary are of little consequence to a werewolf even without gifts or specialization.<br /> <br /> I don't think its right that werewolves can ignore a vampire's natural defenses while still retaining their own in the same situation. It isn't about one trumping the other as much as it is I'm worried about a precedent being set that future gamelines can just easily ignore basic features of others in crossover games.<br /> <br /> Some games are run as crossovers where more than one gameline is represented by PC's. It happens, almost every game I've played in and every game I've run have been this way. It isn't about NPC's from one line or the other but how PC's of both groups react in such situations.<br /> <br /> I would be fine with increasing the weapon modifier of claws and teeth in Gauru, as well as its attribute bonuses and even armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with Werewolves not dealing Lethal to Vampires, if Vampires lose their innate ability to do Lethal to Vampires.<br /> <br /> Forcing Werewolves to deal Bashing against Vampires is a nerf aimed at Werewolves, and a stupid one, considering that Vampires by themselves have a weapon to do Lethal against each other, and they don't even have to change shape to do it, like the Werewolves do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T05:48:08-07:00","id":133557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133516#post133516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with Werewolves not dealing Lethal to Vampires, if Vampires lose their innate ability to do Lethal to Vampires.<br /> <br /> Forcing Werewolves to deal Bashing against Vampires is a nerf aimed at Werewolves, and a stupid one, considering that Vampires by themselves have a weapon to do Lethal against each other, and they don't even have to change shape to do it, like the Werewolves do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read again the rule about vampire lethal-to-bashing conversion , you will see that it does not work for all natural weapons . That means that exist normal weapons (non supernatural) who still do lethal to vampires , this also means that the lethal-to-bashing is not an ''always must use'' rule , is just a rule for what usually happens when a vampire gets hurt by <b>normal</b> weaponry . Gauru for instance is no normal at all , is supernatural Rage + Supernatural force + supernatural ''natural weaponry'' , it must do lethal to all supernaturals not only vampires. because this is what the form is created for . Dalu may should not be able do lethal to supernaturals , but from what I have read so far on anouncements around the project Dalu is a form that wolfblooded will be able to use as a special ability , so if it is a unique power for wolfblooded to do lethal in hand -to- hand situations against supernaturals , sthe same will work for the Uratha themselves .<br /> <br /> As for Urshul I don't know , this is also a form that wolf blooded will be able to use as a special power so it will fall under Dalu core role of supernaturality . thus doing lethal to supernaturals as well ,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","user":"Furry","date":". 05-12-2014, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T09:42:50-07:00","id":133907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133516#post133516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fine with Werewolves not dealing Lethal to Vampires, if Vampires lose their innate ability to do Lethal to Vampires.<br /> <br /> Forcing Werewolves to deal Bashing against Vampires is a nerf aimed at Werewolves, and a stupid one, considering that Vampires by themselves have a weapon to do Lethal against each other, and they don't even have to change shape to do it, like the Werewolves do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have to bite one another, which is a stupid thing for anyone to do. It requires a grapple, and basically costs a willpower to resist the first stage of the blood bond. Again, big drawbacks associated with it and one reason for the concern with claws.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't really care about biting, I just think the claws are an issue, and its a bad trend to set that the next major gameline out gets to ignore the innate abilities of another. Vampire book is already out, Werewolf is not. Werewolves aren't losing an innate ability if they don't even have it yet. I'm pushing for something that I see as a very bad precedent to set.<br /> <br /> @Seidmadr, My example I posted earlier, what if disquiet or wasteland cancelled werewolf free healing? What would you think then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T09:46:58-07:00","id":133909,"title":"","content":"What if Werewolf healing was negated by a type of element or Vampires had to fear something any joe blow could get from rubbing two sticks together?<br /> <br /> I'll be more blunt here. It's not that big of a deal. Weakness and advantages don't change the game much and if you don't like it run your way. This isn't an issue in the overall balance of Templates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T09:57:19-07:00","id":133922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133909#post133909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Werewolf healing was negated by a type of element or Vampires had to fear something any joe blow could get from rubbing two sticks together?<br /> <br /> I'll be more blunt here. It's not that big of a deal. Weakness and advantages don't change the game much and if you don't like it run your way. This isn't an issue in the overall balance of Templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its still a bad precedent to set, even if both have more effective means. I fear that it sets the stage to &quot;Lets just make the next group even better&quot; that ended up a problem in original NWoD. Werewolf and Vampire really got shafted (until Danse Macabre for Vampire, werewolf continued getting shafted however).<br /> <br /> Why does it have to be all 3 forms? Thats the issue. Nobody cares if Guaru is the 10 ft murder monster. Its supposed to be. Hell I think they should all receive larger stat buffs, I just don't think you should start giving innate abilities to bypass other innate abilities without drawbacks or exp investiture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T11:02:20-07:00","id":134053,"title":"","content":"Well, back in the thread about this on the vampire forum, Rose said that vampire damage reduction was written with the expectation that most if not all supernaturals would be dealing lethal damage to each other, which is why there's a provision that supernatural attacks get through it. So with that in mind, i would say vampires innate ability is to downgrade attacks from mortals (similar to Gauru Down and Dirty, it's meant to apply against lesser opponents, not equals), in which case werewolves doing lethal doesn't circumvent it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T13:12:34-07:00","id":134248,"title":"","content":"Where is new Idigam Chronicles spoiler? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T13:16:50-07:00","id":134255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134248#post134248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is new Idigam Chronicles spoiler? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I need my fix. Feeling like a junkie right now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T13:17:43-07:00","id":134257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=133907#post133907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires have to bite one another, which is a stupid thing for anyone to do. It requires a grapple, and basically costs a willpower to resist the first stage of the blood bond. Again, big drawbacks associated with it and one reason for the concern with claws.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't really care about biting, I just think the claws are an issue, and its a bad trend to set that the next major gameline out gets to ignore the innate abilities of another. Vampire book is already out, Werewolf is not. Werewolves aren't losing an innate ability if they don't even have it yet. I'm pushing for something that I see as a very bad precedent to set.<br /> <br /> @Seidmadr, My example I posted earlier, what if disquiet or wasteland cancelled werewolf free healing? What would you think then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they go Frenzy. And they don't have to grapple for it. And they gain their BP in bonus to attacks. And if you read up on vampire biology they don't shed blood unless willing, or forced to by another vampire drinking. I would NOT rule biting to drink the same as if someone bit and ripped a chunk out of someone.<br /> <br /> Doing Lethal to Vampires is an innate ability of Vampires, why shouldn't Werewolves have one, when it's stated that supernatural attacks don't deal Bashing?<br /> <br /> And yes, I think that'd be bullshit, pardon my French, just like this is. Vampires are explicitly stated to downgrade most mundane weapons to Bashing, while leaving supernatural ones to deal Lethal. Using their claws to rip stuff apart is an innate ability of Werewolves. And when Vampires are said not to downgrade supernatural attacks, it'd be shitting on the Werewolves to not let their supernatural shape-change be supernatural.<br /> <br /> I think it's weird that Protean 2 DOESN'T deal Lethal, because it should, but that's another point entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T14:16:23-07:00","id":134342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134257#post134257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's weird that Protean 2 DOESN'T deal Lethal, because it should, but that's another point entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason given there is simply while the change itself is supernatural, the claws themselves are not. This is unlike those produced by Protean 4, which supposedly have the essence of the Beast or some such in them. Likewise, werewolf claws could be argued to be infused with Spirit and therefore deal Lethal to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T14:21:43-07:00","id":134346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134342#post134342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason given there is simply while the change itself is supernatural, the claws themselves are not. This is unlike those produced by Protean 4, which supposedly have the essence of the Beast or some such in them. Likewise, werewolf claws could be argued to be infused with Spirit and therefore deal Lethal to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, makes sense I suppose. I haven't growled about it, due to balance issues, and if they dealt lethal, it'd almost force the 4 dot claws to do agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T15:33:05-07:00","id":134466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134255#post134255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I need my fix. Feeling like a junkie right now</div> </div> </div> </div>My refresh button is getting a lot of action as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T15:43:16-07:00","id":134502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134466#post134466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My refresh button is getting a lot of action as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally don't believe it will be coming out today. My money (hope) is that it will be released Friday with both topics from last week being covered. That way we get Idigam AND Kuruth!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:05:05-07:00","id":134562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134257#post134257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or they go Frenzy. And they don't have to grapple for it. And they gain their BP in bonus to attacks. And if you read up on vampire biology they don't shed blood unless willing, or forced to by another vampire drinking. I would NOT rule biting to drink the same as if someone bit and ripped a chunk out of someone.<br /> <br /> Doing Lethal to Vampires is an innate ability of Vampires, why shouldn't Werewolves have one, when it's stated that supernatural attacks don't deal Bashing?<br /> <br /> And yes, I think that'd be bullshit, pardon my French, just like this is. Vampires are explicitly stated to downgrade most mundane weapons to Bashing, while leaving supernatural ones to deal Lethal. Using their claws to rip stuff apart is an innate ability of Werewolves. And when Vampires are said not to downgrade supernatural attacks, it'd be shitting on the Werewolves to not let their supernatural shape-change be supernatural.<br /> <br /> I think it's weird that Protean 2 DOESN'T deal Lethal, because it should, but that's another point entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frenzy still requires a grapple, however it doesn't require two actions. And if you bite, vampires can bleed freely if they want, but they're not forced to bleed. Pretty sure anytime you bite a vampire they can have you risk vinculum reflexively, and it was discussed rather in depth in the vampire forum.<br /> <br /> I don't remember which post brought it up that fangs were w poor choice of weapon against other vampires, but when you bit one, you have to realize they have full control of their vitae within their bodies. Biting to damage doesn't necessarily mean removing flesh either. It could be as little as piercing the skin.<br /> <br /> I've been on these forums participating in discussions for a long time, since before B&amp;S was released, since the first day these opened. I had thousands of posts on old White Wolf forums. I'll see if I can't find the thread that discussed it and see what all was said and then direct you to it. Hopefully its not on the old forums because I'm not going to look through all that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>B&amp;S pg 94</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When feeding violently, a vampire\u2019s fangs act as 0L weapons<br /> that use the Brawl Skill. That is to say, on a successful attack,<br /> they cause lethal damage equal to their successes, even to<br /> Kindred. <b>As well, the attacker also takes one Vitae (which<br /> causes an additional point of lethal damage to mortals)</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The forum thread was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/69143-question-about-bite-damage\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 05-12-2014, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T16:59:04-07:00","id":134682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134502#post134502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally don't believe it will be coming out today. My money (hope) is that it will be released Friday with both topics from last week being covered. That way we get Idigam AND Kuruth!</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like there would have been an announcement by now if it was being pushed back further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T17:02:19-07:00","id":134683,"title":"","content":"From his twitter: Ah, fuck. Knew I'd forgotten something in the rush today. Tomorrow for sure.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T17:27:32-07:00","id":134707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134683#post134683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From his twitter: Ah, fuck. Knew I'd forgotten something in the rush today. Tomorrow for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there you have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T02:20:43-07:00","id":135149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=134562#post134562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frenzy still requires a grapple, however it doesn't require two actions. And if you bite, vampires can bleed freely if they want, but they're not forced to bleed. Pretty sure anytime you bite a vampire they can have you risk vinculum reflexively, and it was discussed rather in depth in the vampire forum.<br /> <br /> I don't remember which post brought it up that fangs were w poor choice of weapon against other vampires, but when you bit one, you have to realize they have full control of their vitae within their bodies. Biting to damage doesn't necessarily mean removing flesh either. It could be as little as piercing the skin.<br /> <br /> I've been on these forums participating in discussions for a long time, since before B&amp;S was released, since the first day these opened. I had thousands of posts on old White Wolf forums. I'll see if I can't find the thread that discussed it and see what all was said and then direct you to it. Hopefully its not on the old forums because I'm not going to look through all that too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The forum thread was <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/69143-question-about-bite-damage\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I'll be damned about the Vitae. Thought it took a deliberate action to drink blood. I concede defeat there.<br /> <br /> But my point is still thus: It says the vampires take bashing from mundane attacks. Werewolf natural weapons aren't mundane. I don't see any problem here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T08:34:08-07:00","id":135382,"title":"","content":"Soooo...with this week's update one of my favorite changes is Urshul form now being able to inflict appropriate Tilts on a damaging hit. Hishu getting scent is also nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T08:39:17-07:00","id":135386,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty happy about that as well. As iffy as I was about werewolves' teeth and claws doing lethal in the intermediate forms, it's now been changed to only teeth, and that makes even less sense to me. Stew said it would be explained in the book, I only hope the explanation actually makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T08:41:37-07:00","id":135387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>devil bunny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=135382#post135382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soooo...with this week's update one of my favorite changes is Urshul form now being able to inflict appropriate Tilts on a damaging hit. Hishu getting scent is also nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree with this - it really gives Urshul a better niche to fill and offers a far more interesting range of options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:16:34-07:00","id":135815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=135386#post135386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty happy about that as well. As iffy as I was about werewolves' teeth and claws doing lethal in the intermediate forms, it's now been changed to only teeth, and that makes even less sense to me. Stew said it would be explained in the book, I only hope the explanation actually makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this does not work only for the intermediate forms , but all form , yes that means urhan as well does lethal to vampires , probably hishu ? hmmmmm<br /> I hope there will be changes to this rule , for gauru to do lethal with claws as well and hishu not do lethal with bite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2194-furry","name":"Furry","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:24:45-07:00","id":135824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=135386#post135386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty happy about that as well. As iffy as I was about werewolves' teeth and claws doing lethal in the intermediate forms, it's now been changed to only teeth, and that makes even less sense to me. Stew said it would be explained in the book, I only hope the explanation actually makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would have left it as it was, though if I were to have to change it I would have made claws lethal in Dalu and Gauru, and fangs lethal in Urshul and Gauru. That or make both count as mundane in all forms then give them the ability to give both teeth and claws armor piercing and the ability to count as supernatural weaponry for the scene by spending a point of essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T15:47:10-07:00","id":135838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=135824#post135824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That or make both count as mundane in all forms then give them the ability to give both teeth and claws armor piercing and the ability to count as supernatural weaponry for the scene by spending a point of essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that option as well, but would have preferred Gauru Claws be lethal regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T19:08:27-07:00","id":136071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=135824#post135824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I would have left it as it was, though if I were to have to change it I would have made claws lethal in Dalu and Gauru, and fangs lethal in Urshul and Gauru. That or make both count as mundane in all forms then give them the ability to give both teeth and claws armor piercing and the ability to count as supernatural weaponry for the scene by spending a point of essence.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would rather have left it as it was than changed to just teeth. I like your suggestion of spending essence to add AP and supernatural for a scene even better. But honestly I'm past the point of caring now. I'm going to run it the way I want to regardless of what the official rule on the matter is, so whatever. I just hope that what they decide to go with has solid fluff behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T20:35:30-07:00","id":136155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=135824#post135824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would have left it as it was, though if I were to have to change it I would have made claws lethal in Dalu and Gauru, and fangs lethal in Urshul and Gauru. That or make both count as mundane in all forms then give them the ability to give both teeth and claws armor piercing and the ability to count as supernatural weaponry for the scene by spending a point of essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like something that should be a gift rather than an innate aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T21:14:58-07:00","id":136171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136155#post136155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds more like something that should be a gift rather than an innate aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find it powerful enough to be a gift, and the only real reason I would go with it being innate is because too many people are complaining about it being 0 cost, so I put as minor a cost on it as I could in order to somewhat try to compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:09:38-07:00","id":136264,"title":"","content":"Regardless of that change Garou form claws SHOULD be lethal. Why wouldn't they be? The war form should be capable of RENDING bodies, vampire or otherwise. If I remember my vampires in Requiem properly, dismemberment IS lethal...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T00:30:47-07:00","id":136380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136264#post136264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of that change Garou form claws SHOULD be lethal. Why wouldn't they be? The war form should be capable of RENDING bodies, vampire or otherwise. If I remember my vampires in Requiem properly, dismemberment IS lethal...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think straight up dismemberment from basic attacks should be the province of gifts. A starting vamp can bump up their strength well beyond the level of a werewolf in Gauru through Vigor and Augmentation. Hell, start a character wit Vigor 3, BP 3 and Strength 3 (hardly unreasonable), and they can be swinging a 6L weapon with an effective Strength of <i>10</i>, and they're still only doing bashing to other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T01:26:20-07:00","id":136401,"title":"","content":"I think the unreasonable part of that is BP 3, considering how many Merit points that eats up (and the lack of incentive via creation vs. XP disparity to pump BP at start).<br /> <br /> It's also worth nothing that +3 of the Strength and +3 of that Damage they way you have it (which means you're assuming a 3L base weapon) is all from Vigor alone. The reason it does bashing is because they're simply putting a lot of strength behind a mundane weapon. Comparing a strength focused (even if not maxed) vampire using all of their Merit and Discipline dots just to boost Strength isn't necessarily the most apt comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T05:18:33-07:00","id":136572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136401#post136401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the unreasonable part of that is BP 3, considering how many Merit points that eats up (and the lack of incentive via creation vs. XP disparity to pump BP at start).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen plent of characters walk into the game with BP3, personaly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136401#post136401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth nothing that +3 of the Strength and +3 of that Damage they way you have it (which means you're assuming a 3L base weapon) is all from Vigor alone. The reason it does bashing is because they're simply putting a lot of strength behind a mundane weapon. Comparing a strength focused (even if not maxed) vampire using all of their Merit and Discipline dots just to boost Strength isn't necessarily the most apt comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the thing is swinging an a or chainsaw with 2 or three times the strength and destructive damage is just as likely to dismember a body as a Gauru tearing in with teeth, and vastly more so than claws (the claws being relatively equivalent of a very large tiger's, in my estimation), yet the weapon still does only bashing, where the argument that Lyrics put forward is that claws are capable of &quot;RENDING bodies&quot;. My counterpoint is that the an axe with the same or greater level of strength and damage potential behind it does not do lethal to the vampire, and therefore the &quot;RENDING&quot; capabilities of the Gauru form are not sufficient to cause straight Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T07:33:58-07:00","id":136694,"title":"","content":"BP 3 is perfectly reasonable for a starting character; no, there's no Experience cost disparity to incentivize it, but it's still within the realm for a starting character with no additional Experiences granted at creation.<br /> <br /> It's not necessarily a good choice, because it means no other merits, but it is a possible choice, so is not unreasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:43:03-07:00","id":136771,"title":"","content":"BP 3 being possible, and occasionally appropriate, doesn't make it a reasonable example character.<br /> <br /> I've never seen it, mostly because Merits are generally important enough that you want at least a few of them to flush out your character.<br /> <br /> As for the, &quot;lots of strength behind a high damage weapon,&quot; thing:<br /> <br /> 1) IIRC Rose has clarified that the ST should rule that appropriately gruesome bodily harm can get around the downgrade.<br /> <br /> 2) It doesn't matter because the downgrade is magic, not logic. It is weak to other magic by design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:47:24-07:00","id":136776,"title":"","content":"Since a chainsaw was mentioned as a weapon, they don't do damage by being swung really hard like an axe, they do damage by tearing away pieces of the object they are cutting into. Otherwise loggers would be swinging them at trees, something only a fucking idiot would do. Do what you want, I will never let a vamp (or any other splat, barring the use of some kind of magical ability) downgrade chainsaw damage to bashing in any of my games. Sin Eaters using plasm to downgrade counts as magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:53:05-07:00","id":136783,"title":"","content":"Reslience would count as a magic ability for my purposes as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:21:54-07:00","id":136796,"title":"","content":"Let's take a moment and pretend that garou form claws are the only thing about it causing damage, and not the roughly 500 pound war beast using them. There's logic. The claws do the slashing, the garou form can use them to do the rending. You can talk about downgrading natural weapons all you want, and axe won't pull your ribs out for staring at it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:50:46-07:00","id":136822,"title":"","content":"There's also the spiritual aspect to it as well, my own internal logic dictates that those claws are doing damage on more than just the physical level, they are damaging the animating force of the target, whether that target be undead, Spirit, or something stranger. Not everyone will agree with that but it's what makes justifiable sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:53:33-07:00","id":136825,"title":"","content":"Prometheans, Demons and Angels are what I have in mind with &quot;something stranger&quot;. Can't edit posts with my phone browser for some reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:31:52-07:00","id":136869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136825#post136825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans, Demons and Angels are what I have in mind with &amp;quot;something stranger&amp;quot;. Can't edit posts with my phone browser for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div> If it's like mine you can't do line breaks either. This site interacts weirdly with mobile browsers for some readon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:32:32-07:00","id":136870,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about something a bit silly about all this:<br /> <br /> It only takes 3 Merit dots to deal lethal to vampires with mundane weapons. Yay Kindred Dueling.<br /> <br /> Considering simply knowing what you're fighting well enough to damage them more effectively (this is not stated as magic in the Merit) can get around the downgrade, I think that's more than enough to get past most of the complaints about how vampires take bashing from just chucking a lot of normal damage at them. A vampire with Kindred Dueling 3 and Vigor 3, with a 3L weapon going to lethal damage another vampire to shreds very easily. More effectively than BP 3 would allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:46:25-07:00","id":136877,"title":"","content":"The only problem I have with the &quot;Kindred Dueling lets you do lethal and it's not magic&quot; argument is that Kindred Dueling is a Fighting Style, meaning its a matter of the technique, not the weapon. If you know the technique, it doesn't matter what weapon you use, as long as it's bladed. Likewise, if you don't know the technique, it doesn't matter what weapon you use because you don't know how to use it that way without the Merit. And if &quot;rending weapons&quot; could do lethal without the proper technique, that should have been mentioned along with &quot;supernatural weapons&quot; as things that are not downgraded. That said, I'm starting to warm up to the idea of werewolf claws doing &quot;magic damage&quot; to vampires with some sort of spirit mojo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T11:59:45-07:00","id":136958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136822#post136822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the spiritual aspect to it as well, my own internal logic dictates that those claws are doing damage on more than just the physical level, they are damaging the animating force of the target, whether that target be undead, Spirit, or something stranger. Not everyone will agree with that but it's what makes justifiable sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I prefer the idea of teeth doing the damage, because it sets up a nice metaphysical idea with the wolvves feeding on spirits after the sacred hunt, gaining their essence through literal devouring. It's the teeth of the wolf that are the symbolic lynchpin of this, not the claws.<br /> <br /> Not that Im hugely bothered by Uratha causing lethal to vampires in general - I don't particularly care for it, but I can very easily take it away in my games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:20:15-07:00","id":136967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136958#post136958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I prefer the idea of teeth doing the damage, because it sets up a nice metaphysical idea with the wolvves feeding on spirits after the sacred hunt, gaining their essence through literal devouring. It's the teeth of the wolf that are the symbolic lynchpin of this, not the claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, y'know, that whole body of modern lycanthropic lore that says getting bitten by a werewolf is Bad News.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:26:47-07:00","id":137003,"title":"","content":"Same for scratches though. In fact that little bit if lore is gonna be a focus in teen wolf season 4. After they kill more of the cast I'm sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:30:13-07:00","id":137007,"title":"","content":"The scratch delivering the curse is in some werewolf stories and not in others. The bite, though, is pretty much universal in Werewolf lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:36:21-07:00","id":137012,"title":"","content":"Indeed but while were working with a game line focusing in folklore let's exemplify the out there crazy, ja? This story is true after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:39:27-07:00","id":137017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=137007#post137007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scratch delivering the curse is in some werewolf stories and not in others. The bite, though, is pretty much universal in Werewolf lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no universal there. Every myth I've seen is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T12:52:17-07:00","id":137052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=136877#post136877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem I have with the &quot;Kindred Dueling lets you do lethal and it's not magic&quot; argument is that Kindred Dueling is a Fighting Style, meaning its a matter of the technique, not the weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because that's not the point of the argument I'm making.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that it doesn't take supernatural powers to get around the vampire's damage reduction. Supernatural powers can get around it, as can technique. Basically that vampires reduce lethal to bashing because lethal usually isn't applied properly to vampires to cause full effect. Not because vampires have a magical field of downgrading damage. Anything the ST feels should apply lethal because it will effectively be applied correctly - either through skill, excessive force, or some other source - isn't &quot;violating&quot; the vampire's innate powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T14:57:33-07:00","id":137216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=137052#post137052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not really, because that's not the point of the argument I'm making. What I'm saying is that it doesn't take supernatural powers to get around the vampire's damage reduction. Supernatural powers can get around it, as can technique. Basically that vampires reduce lethal to bashing because lethal usually isn't applied properly to vampires to cause full effect. Not because vampires have a magical field of downgrading damage. Anything the ST feels should apply lethal because it will effectively be applied correctly - either through skill, excessive force, or some other source - isn't &amp;quot;violating&amp;quot; the vampire's innate powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry, I was not meaning your argument specifically, I've just seen Kindred Dueling brought up a lot in this discussion. Your post just happened to be TH proverbial straw that got me to express my issue with that as an example for why werewolf teeth/claws should be able to do lethal even if they're mundane . The comparison doesn't really work. But I agree with you, it does illustrate that sometimes mundane sources can be made to do Lethal, and it's pretty much am ST call most of the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T00:15:52-07:00","id":137853,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's magic&quot; is actually enough of an answer for me. I can run it how I want/need in my own games past that point; I don't need the books to be hyper-accurate literary straight-jackets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:05:48-07:00","id":138110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=137853#post137853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;It's magic&amp;quot; is actually enough of an answer for me. I can run it how I want/need in my own games past that point; I don't need the books to be hyper-accurate literary straight-jackets.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would be fine with just &quot;it's magic&quot; if it doesn't also say &quot;and that means it does lethal damage to vampires&quot;, (vampire already says that, and the ST can use their best judgement in crossover. If it does specifically say it does lethal damage to vampires, I would like a bit more of an explanation. It doesn't have to be hyper accurate or pseudoscientific or anything, I just want to know that there's a reason it does lethal besides &quot;a wizard did it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:50:43-07:00","id":138162,"title":"","content":"The cursed blood of a vampire creates the cursed claws and teeth which can strike harder and deeper at the cursed body.<br /> <br /> The Uratha don't share that curse, so it's not as effective.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, ass pull, but it works. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:20:25-07:00","id":138189,"title":"","content":"Why does there need to be an assumption that when it says, &quot;and that means it does lethal to vampires,&quot; it isn't just referencing the B&amp;S rules and instead is saying something more and then requiring more explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T10:42:36-07:00","id":138212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138189#post138189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does there need to be an assumption that when it says, &amp;quot;and that means it does lethal to vampires,&amp;quot; it isn't just referencing the B&amp;S rules and instead is saying something more and then requiring more explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because vampires are not assumed to exist in Forsaken, or to function by the same rules as the vampires in Requiem. If you're going to specifically state that X affects vampires in Y way, you are acknowledging that vampires exist in the setting, and should explain how they work within in your setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T11:47:56-07:00","id":138304,"title":"","content":"See that's flawed logic though because requiem exists side by side with forsaken. It isn't like dc vs marvel here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T12:04:59-07:00","id":138314,"title":"","content":"That's a fairly weak rationale. The nWOD books have repeatedly addressed crossover in their rules even when not in books that are specifically about it (even in part). Should IC not have a complimentary section to B&amp;S's Supernatural Conflict and Clash of Will section which address rules that apply to other supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:25:24-07:00","id":138361,"title":"","content":"Eh, I just think its a vampire rule, it doesn't need to be repeated in werewolf. And if it is, the reasoning should be clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:46:20-07:00","id":138372,"title":"","content":"It is just a vampire rule, but if werewolf doesn't address it the first question out of crossover fan's mouths will be 'how do werewolf teeth and claws apply to vampire damage reduction'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:48:31-07:00","id":138374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=124073#post124073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does mean that Uratha will be pretty horrendous opponents in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight edit, much as I dislike the whole &quot;Fixed that for you&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Uratha have all the cunning of humans, the ferocity of werewolves, the ability to take different forms depending on need and all of it backed by spirit-magic inherited from two of the greatest spirits to ever exist. Weapons forged and natural help them in the Hunt. They might not be holy warriors anymore, each a one-wolfman army, but even the &quot;average&quot; werewolf is among the deadliest creatures on land. If they let loose for a moment, allow the Rage within to boil up and escape their control, you get Gauru. The sheer savagery and killing instinct of Man and Wolf and Spirit all embodied in one monster; it is the hunter freed of the Hunt, the predatory need to kill laid bare of thought or reason.<br /> <br /> And facing one of those might be <i>merciful </i>compared to a pack of thinking werewolves using magic and tactics to run you to ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 05-15-2014, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:53:08-07:00","id":138377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138374#post138374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slight edit, much as I dislike the whole &quot;Fixed that for you&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Uratha have all the cunning of humans, the ferocity of werewolves, the ability to take different forms depending on need and all of it backed by spirit-magic inherited from two of the greatest spirits to ever exist. They might not be holy warriors anymore, each a one-wolfman army, but even the &quot;average&quot; werewolf is among the deadliest creatures on land. If they let loose for a moment, allow the Rage within to boil up and escape their control, you get Gauru. The sheer savagery and killing instinct of Man and Wolf and Spirit all embodied in one monster; it is the hunter freed of the Hunt, the predatory need to kill laid bare of thought or reason.<br /> <br /> And facing one of those might be <i>merciful </i>compared to a pack of thinking werewolf using magic and tactics to run you to ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I like that portrayal very much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1198-devil-bunny","name":"devil bunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:56:52-07:00","id":138380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138212#post138212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because vampires are not assumed to exist in Forsaken, or to function by the same rules as the vampires in Requiem. If you're going to specifically state that X affects vampires in Y way, you are acknowledging that vampires exist in the setting, and should explain how they work within in your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually? They are. This isn't cWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:19:02-07:00","id":138390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138212#post138212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because vampires are not assumed to exist in Forsaken, or to function by the same rules as the vampires in Requiem. If you're going to specifically state that X affects vampires in Y way, you are acknowledging that vampires exist in the setting, and should explain how they work within in your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then how about in Animalism 4: Feral Injection where it specifically calls out that it sends werewolves into frenzy? How about the section about predatory auras? There are multiple places all throughout the book that mentions these things, and maybe I just haven't scoured the forums hard enough, but I don't remember people complaining about those. Fact of the matter is, all book call out other splats multiple times as an example for multiple things. Vampire isn't a special little snowflake that should be exempt to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-15-2014, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T15:37:31-07:00","id":138488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138212#post138212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because vampires are not assumed to exist in Forsaken, or to function by the same rules as the vampires in Requiem. If you're going to specifically state that X affects vampires in Y way, you are acknowledging that vampires exist in the setting, and should explain how they work within in your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that would be an incorrect assumption, unless you are playing Hunter which specifically provides its own rules for the various supernatural creatures. The unified rules systems are there precisely because the various splats exist in a shared world and different abilities make callouts to other splats, unlike the CWoD where lupines specifically were not necessarily the same thing as Garou, and Mages were different from human magicians. They tried reconciling that for players and ST's with the release of Dark Alliance, Under a Blood Red Moon and Chaos Factor. Sam Haight was used as a unifying element and it really didn't end up working that well once put into practice (too much Deus Ex Machina for my players tastes at the time and I can't fault them for feeling that way).<br /> <br /> NWoD specifically addresses that particular flaw of the CWoD by creating a rule-set that allows you to seamlessly (more or less) integrate the game lines without needing to make a bunch of house rulings on the spot. What it doesn't nor claim to do is establish some kind of objective balance between the various splats, as that would be a fools errand. There isn't even &quot;balance&quot; between the various sub-splats (Clans, Tribes, Paths etc) within a given line. It's up to the individual ST to determine if they want to include a particular group of supernatural beings, nothing forces you to use them in your game, but the default assumption is they do have a shared world without arbitrarily forced animosity between the various groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:02:29-07:00","id":138635,"title":"","content":"I don't use the books under the assumption that they're closed-off entities that don't exist or interact with each other, so we're working from opposite ends on this. In fact I assume all the games do exist in the same world, since that's how they tend to be written.<br /> <br /> And, as mentioned, if it was a case of &quot;vampire rules should only be in vampire books&quot; then it breaks because the vampire books have already given rules about werewolves, shouldn't those only exist in the werewolf books?<br /> <br /> I don't see &quot;werewolf claws and teeth do lethal damage to vampires&quot; as game-breaking in any way for either game. There has to be some reasons why vampires are wary of &quot;lupines&quot; and not just in a &quot;the fluff says so&quot;, the mechanics need to back up the fluff text. (I hate the word &quot;fluff&quot; in regards to descriptive text, but it's a closer description to what we're talking about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T18:29:24-07:00","id":138696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138635#post138635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't use the books under the assumption that they're closed-off entities that don't exist or interact with each other, so we're working from opposite ends on this. In fact I assume all the games do exist in the same world, since that's how they tend to be written. And, as mentioned, if it was a case of &amp;quot;vampire rules should only be in vampire books&amp;quot; then it breaks because the vampire books have already given rules about werewolves, shouldn't those only exist in the werewolf books? I don't see &amp;quot;werewolf claws and teeth do lethal damage to vampires&amp;quot; as game-breaking in any way for either game. There has to be some reasons why vampires are wary of &amp;quot;lupines&amp;quot; and not just in a &amp;quot;the fluff says so&amp;quot;, the mechanics need to back up the fluff text. (I hate the word &amp;quot;fluff&amp;quot; in regards to descriptive text, but it's a closer description to what we're talking about.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I use them under the assumption that the various lines existence or lack of existence and their relationships with one another is up to the storyteller and varies from one chronicle to the next. I could run one game where werewolves are the only supernats that exist, and then later run another where everything is fair game except mummies and Prometheans (cause I haven't read those books yet ^^<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> so yeah we're just coming at it from different perspectives. And I think yours is perfectly valid, I would just like that where the lines cross over, the book making reference to something from another line should either let the line it's referencing handle the rules, or if it's important to mention in that book, give a brief explanation of what that means in the context of the setting. And once again, this has nothing to do with being game breaking for me. In fact, I do like the idea of werewolves doing lethal to vampires. But I would like it to either have some kind of description of what in the game world the mechanics are representing, or have it left as &quot;they're supernatural attacks, let that mean what it will in your games&quot;. Also, could you give me an example of a werewolf-specific rule in Blood and Smoke? The only one I can think of is the sidebar in the predatory aura section that basically amounts to &quot;other creatures might have similar auras. Werewolves in particular. They should probably affect vampires in a similar way&quot;. If that's all the werewolves doing lethal to vampires is, a sidebar saying &quot;there are some creatures in the world of darkness that are not easily affected by ordinary weapons. Vampires undead bodies, for example, can withstand most forms of physical damage. Werewolves' spiritual nature allows their natural weapons to harm such creatures as easily as they tear through mortal flesh&quot; or something to that effect, I would not bat an eyelash. What I don't want is for the rules on shapeshifting to directly state &quot;werewolf bites do lethal damage to vampires&quot; without some attempt at describing how or why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T18:49:13-07:00","id":138706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138390#post138390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then how about in Animalism 4: Feral Injection where it specifically calls out that it sends werewolves into frenzy? How about the section about predatory auras? There are multiple places all throughout the book that mentions these things, and maybe I just haven't scoured the forums hard enough, but I don't remember people complaining about those. Fact of the matter is, all book call out other splats multiple times as an example for multiple things. Vampire isn't a special little snowflake that should be exempt to that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, Animalism 4, thank you. So, yeah, like I said, this gives a lovely description of what happens in the narrative when this power is used. If werewolf has a similar description of what an attack that ignores the damage resistance of vampires (and what ever else might resist mundane weapons) looks like, I will be satisfied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T21:34:22-07:00","id":138904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138706#post138706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ah, Animalism 4, thank you. So, yeah, like I said, this gives a lovely description of what happens in the narrative when this power is used. If werewolf has a similar description of what an attack that ignores the damage resistance of vampires (and what ever else might resist mundane weapons) looks like, I will be satisfied.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which it almost certainly would, since almost all WoD powers do. But this more than proves that even vampire is written under the assumption that it exists in the same world/setting as werewolf, and sets out mechanics that effect them in specified ways. I can't see why one would be a problem while the other isn't. I don't really find &quot;Because it didn't come with half a page of fluff&quot; to be a valid argument seeing as how this is nothing but a brief blog post touching on some of the things they planned on including in the main book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:07:53-07:00","id":139066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=138904#post138904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which it almost certainly would, since almost all WoD powers do. But this more than proves that even vampire is written under the assumption that it exists in the same world/setting as werewolf, and sets out mechanics that effect them in specified ways. I can't see why one would be a problem while the other isn't. I don't really find &amp;quot;Because it didn't come with half a page of fluff&amp;quot; to be a valid argument seeing as how this is nothing but a brief blog post touching on some of the things they planned on including in the main book.</div> </div> </div> </div> I... Never said I expected that that from the blog post? ...seriously, I feel like people are assuming I'm freaking out about this when all I'm trying to say is that I will be totally fine with werewolves doing lethal to vampires as long as in the book there is a brief narrative of what the mechanics represent in-game, and/or leaves it at &quot;is supernatural&quot;. The latter would be my preference, but I am also totally ok with the former. And I concede I was mistaken about the assumptions the books make about the shared universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T00:51:29-07:00","id":139095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=139066#post139066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I... Never said I expected that that from the blog post? ...seriously, I feel like people are assuming I'm freaking out about this when all I'm trying to say is that I will be totally fine with werewolves doing lethal to vampires as long as in the book there is a brief narrative of what the mechanics represent in-game, and/or leaves it at &quot;is supernatural&quot;. The latter would be my preference, but I am also totally ok with the former. And I concede I was mistaken about the assumptions the books make about the shared universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that you keep bringing it up in response to statements talking about similarities in the way both books are handling how they present rules. That fact that you do makes it seem like you're trying to use that argument as defense for why you would or wouldn't accept the rule as it was previously stated. That said, sorry if I was taking your statement the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T05:07:12-07:00","id":139200,"title":"","content":"I'm fine with the writers leaving it up to individual ST's to come up with their own internal logic for why certain effects work the way they do. They aren't writing textbooks on metaphysics, just giving some infrastructure to help you tell the story you and your players want to tell. That being said I do want rules to be consistent from one product line to another, when those lines use the same basic infrastructure with some tweaking for the needs of their specific lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T13:51:32-07:00","id":139748,"title":"","content":"I can understand wanting &quot;rules for line X are in X books&quot; but that's already been broken with Blood &amp; Smoke. So, rules of how Y power/ability of Line Y affect X and Z will have to accept being in books about Line Y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T05:58:23-07:00","id":140457,"title":"","content":"Will &quot;using Defence against Firearms&quot; work against aimed spells of mages, like <i>Celestial Fire</i> or <i>Influence Electricity</i>? In normal rules they are treated like using Firearms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T07:08:12-07:00","id":140475,"title":"","content":"Probably. I mean if I can dodge bullets why can't I dodge some magical fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T08:11:11-07:00","id":140552,"title":"","content":"We'll have to see how the updated GMC Mage rules deal with aimed spells?<br /> <br /> It is kind of hard to say how a preliminary IC Werewolf rule is going to interact with a completely unpreviewed FWC Mage rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T08:17:56-07:00","id":140558,"title":"","content":"If we assume full defense against firearms makes it in to IC and aimed spells work the same way in FWC as they do now (which is a pretty big assumption), then I agree with ephsy. If you can dodge bullets, I can't see why you wouldn't be able to dodge a fireball. One is supersonic, the other is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T08:40:10-07:00","id":140572,"title":"","content":"People are also assuming the defense is due to dodging, rather than it being a simulation of physical toughness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T09:01:06-07:00","id":140600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140572#post140572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are also assuming the defense is due to dodging, rather than it being a simulation of physical toughness.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that is technically a good way to run with it, it would clearly raise the question why it involves Dexterity and Wits and not ...Stamina and Strength or whatever. That being said, switching Dexterity and Wits for Strength and Stamina while shape changed sounds like a decent idea, actually. You definitely do not need the higher of the two then, though, as it will probably be already quite high from the form bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T10:15:00-07:00","id":140696,"title":"","content":"*shows up*<br /> <br /> Still a crossover discussion?<br /> <br /> *vanishes*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T10:22:33-07:00","id":140700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140696#post140696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shows up*<br /> <br /> Still a crossover discussion?<br /> <br /> *vanishes*</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of it's about the intermediary forms gaining Defense against projectile attacks. Which, I think, is an interesting idea.<br /> <br /> What did you like about the article?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T10:24:38-07:00","id":140701,"title":"","content":"Not much, to be honest; but I've posted my concerns before, and I'd rather not repeat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T11:08:34-07:00","id":140740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140572#post140572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are also assuming the defense is due to dodging, rather than it being a simulation of physical toughness.</div> </div> </div> </div> Isn't that what Defense represents? Using cleverness and reflexes to avoid being hit by attacks? If it's toughness, why not represent that with additional health or armor? I'd be all for some natural ballistic armor in hybrid forms!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T11:34:56-07:00","id":140758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140572#post140572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are also assuming the defense is due to dodging, rather than it being a simulation of physical toughness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me think of Van Helsing werewolves dodging the bullets by jumping around and what not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T13:38:14-07:00","id":140898,"title":"","content":"Look at it like heightened instincts: reacting as soon as someone moves, a combination of fast-twitch and slow-twitch, sensing danger and so on. Though I wonder if the same reasoning should apply to Urhan form, but either way, I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T13:59:09-07:00","id":140914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140898#post140898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at it like heightened instincts: reacting as soon as someone moves, a combination of fast-twitch and slow-twitch, sensing danger and so on. Though I wonder if the same reasoning should apply to Urhan form, but either way, I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, I like it, and it doesn't really effect combat other than making all weapons of the same damage rating equal, whether they're firearms or fire axes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T14:25:34-07:00","id":140938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140600#post140600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While that is technically a good way to run with it, it would clearly raise the question why it involves Dexterity and Wits and not ...Stamina and Strength or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be the Athletics portion of the pool.<br /> <br /> Also, do remember what Defensive Combat: Weaponry represents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T14:45:55-07:00","id":140947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140572#post140572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are also assuming the defense is due to dodging, rather than it being a simulation of physical toughness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably because &quot;additional toughness&quot; would be better represented by additional health. Also, choosing not to use your Defense against an attack means they are more likely to hit you; if you were &quot;extra tough&quot; then they'd still hit you but it would hurt less when they did, which is more like armor in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T17:13:54-07:00","id":141063,"title":"","content":"I see it as them having the ability to expose the areas less vulnerable to harm, so yes dex and wits would apply. I can take a blow to my forearms that result in less damage than if I took it in my face for example. No need to represent that with additional health levels, which werewolves also get. It doesn't really matter how I envision it applying, I'm not describing what happens when you are playing, just relating how I'd describe it in my game. I can describe a shot as grazing without doing any damage, you may describe the same result as them leaping out of the way, twisting to avoid contact, etc. It's an abstract system, not simulationist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T17:18:59-07:00","id":141064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=140947#post140947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Probably because &amp;quot;additional toughness&amp;quot; would be better represented by additional health. Also, choosing not to use your Defense against an attack means they are more likely to hit you; if you were &amp;quot;extra tough&amp;quot; then they'd still hit you but it would hurt less when they did, which is more like armor in that case.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. Even if you narrate it as something other than dodging, Defense will always be your ability to not get hit by things, not your ability to withstand getting hit by things. And no matter how you narrate it, Defense comes from being alert, agile, and fit. Getting your full defense against firearms means your natural ability to avoid being hit due to your alertness, agility, and physical skill are unhampered by the fact that the thing you're avoiding travels faster than sound. Which, to me, is a bit of an odd ability for Werewolves to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T17:27:48-07:00","id":141072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=141064#post141064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This. Even if you narrate it as something other than dodging, Defense will always be your ability to not get hit by things, not your ability to withstand getting hit by things. And no matter how you narrate it, Defense comes from being alert, agile, and fit. Getting your full defense against firearms means your natural ability to avoid being hit due to your alertness, agility, and physical skill are unhampered by the fact that the thing you're avoiding travels faster than sound. Which, to me, is a bit of an odd ability for Werewolves to have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precedent for applying Defense against firearms includes &quot;you are made of water&quot; and &quot;you are a spirit.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a reason Dodge isn't the name of the passive Trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T17:57:56-07:00","id":141080,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin, Defense in NWoD incorporates the effect of the soak roll from the Storyteller system (the parent system that the Storytelling system is based upon), it was probably the rules change that got the most discussion when the NWoD came out. That's what I base my interpretation and description on. If Defense was strictly about the physical ability to dodge attacks then it wouldn't make sense that wound penalties don't affect Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T18:09:37-07:00","id":141087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=141080#post141080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin, Defense in NWoD incorporates the effect of the soak roll from the Storyteller system (the parent system that the Storytelling system is based upon), it was probably the rules change that got the most discussion when the NWoD came out. That's what I base my interpretation and description on. If Defense was strictly about the physical ability to dodge attacks then it wouldn't make sense that wound penalties don't affect Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ahh, that would be the source of my confusion having not played oWoD. Nonetheless, if what is happening is that the werewolf is being hit by bullets but is not being damaged by them, it seems weird to me to rationalize it into fitting as Defense when there's already a mechanic specifically designed to represent that ability - ballistic armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T19:08:58-07:00","id":141156,"title":"","content":"They wouldn't necessarily be taking the full impact of the hits, grazing and flesh wounds that don't actually affect your health track (without invoking extra mechanics) were what I had in mind with my statements. It would have helped if I had been a bit clearer or more descriptive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T19:47:38-07:00","id":141179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=141156#post141156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wouldn't necessarily be taking the full impact of the hits, grazing and flesh wounds that don't actually affect your health track (without invoking extra mechanics) were what I had in mind with my statements. It would have helped if I had been a bit clearer or more descriptive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, like the abstract AC system in D&amp;D, a miss isn't necessarily a complete miss. It may or may not make contact, but if it does it's a glancing or grazing blow, not serious enough to count as actual damage. But then you're still turning what would otherwise have been a direct hit <i>from a bullet</i> into a grazing blow. Unless you can move at supersonic speeds, that is not possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T21:09:56-07:00","id":141214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=141179#post141179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, like the abstract AC system in D&amp;D, a miss isn't necessarily a complete miss. It may or may not make contact, but if it does it's a glancing or grazing blow, not serious enough to count as actual damage. But then you're still turning what would otherwise have been a direct hit <i>from a bullet</i> into a grazing blow. Unless you can move at supersonic speeds, that is not possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aim dodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T22:57:24-07:00","id":141271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=141214#post141214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aim dodging.</div> </div> </div> </div>:/ I guess... It's still just not the kind of thing I ever pictured a werewolf doing. I get the desire to not make guns the go-to weapon for hunting werewolves (even though that is pretty consistent with most werewolf fiction. Silver bullets are <i>the</i> werewolf hunter's weapon, or silver bolts in a fantasy setting). But I just think that goal can be achieved in a way that doesn't involve werewolves moving like spiderman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T23:35:42-07:00","id":141282,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't incorporate arguments from 2004 about changes made between owod and nwod, I just use what's in the modern books. So Defense is &quot;moving out of the way while trying to hit someone else at the same time&quot; per the core WOD book. Weaponry Dodge, Brawling Dodge, and later Athletics Dodge altered the Dodge mechanic. The GMC Defense trait is identical to nWOD's Athletics Dodge: You add your Athletics score to your Defense, which was the lower of Wits/Dexterity, and subtract that from the incoming attack roll, and this meant a greater ability to *move out of the way*, nothing about being tougher.<br /> <br /> Since we're moving into yet another set of rules with GMC, I really think we should move any arguments and bases of rules into at least nWOD and throwing out anything from oWOD in these arguments. It's more than enough to keep 1 version back, which goes back 10 years, rather than everyone being expected to know internet arguments/explanations from 10+ years ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T00:10:54-07:00","id":141294,"title":"","content":"Oh! Hey. Guys. Guys. I just remembered something.<br /> <br /> All-out attacks.<br /> <br /> If I'm not misremembering the archetypes, the typical context in which the silver bullet hits home has the werewolf desperate and/or lost to feral monstrosity, yes?<br /> <br /> (It is 3AM and I am tired, so I cannot speak for the surety of this hypothesis.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T00:22:03-07:00","id":141297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=141271#post141271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">:/ I guess... It's still just not the kind of thing I ever pictured a werewolf doing. I get the desire to not make guns the go-to weapon for hunting werewolves (even though that is pretty consistent with most werewolf fiction. Silver bullets are <i>the</i> werewolf hunter's weapon, or silver bolts in a fantasy setting). But I just think that goal can be achieved in a way that doesn't involve werewolves moving like spiderman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truthfully I'm not really sold on the defense against guns thing either, just for that reason. Personally I'd prefer them to gain armor against everything but silver weaponry, representing the wall of hyper dense muscle you'd now have to get through in order to really harm them. I would gladly accept using the higher of wits and dex in order to simulate animal like reflexes, but I don't really care much applying defense against bullets. I get what they're going for but I can't help but wonder if there's a better way to go about it. I'll think on it a bit more.<br /> <br /> Though slightly off topic I do want to point out that I feel that caving into pressure and changing the claws from being supernatural to mundane was nothing but a detriment to the werewolf line as a whole. This is more of a thematic complaint than a mechanical one, because the damage type wasn't really mechanically important anyways, but I feel it is extremely awkward for only a portion of a werewolves natural weaponry to be considered supernatural. If you're going to give, at least give in a way that maintains internal consistency and have neither teeth nor claws be supernatural. While I still feel that thematically the line would be best off with both claws and teeth being considered supernatural weaponry, if you can't do that then don't set it in some weird half state, just let it be one way or the other. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 05-18-2014, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T07:22:15-07:00","id":141559,"title":"","content":"I agree completely. While I would prefer all bashing to all lethal, either is better than this weird compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T03:36:25-07:00","id":169683,"title":"","content":"As first real fight in Gauru broke out on our game session this problem emerge. If Claws in Gauru ( and all other forms for it ) does 1L damage lower than Bite ( that don't need Grappling ), why to use them? Wouldn't be more logical to all the time just Bite everyone?<br /> <br /> Myself, I would made both natural weapons as +1L Damage, only Bite would have Armor Piercing 1. This way Gauru would mostly used Claws, but when enemy was tougher, or more damage needed to be done, he would long for Biting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T08:36:50-07:00","id":169790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=169683#post169683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As first real fight in Gauru broke out on our game session this problem emerge. If Claws in Gauru ( and all other forms for it ) does 1L damage lower than Bite ( that don't need Grappling ), why to use them? Wouldn't be more logical to all the time just Bite everyone?<br /> <br /> Myself, I would made both natural weapons as +1L Damage, only Bite would have Armor Piercing 1. This way Gauru would mostly used Claws, but when enemy was tougher, or more damage needed to be done, he would long for Biting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't usually wanna bite toxic spirits/claimed, and tasting living flesh could very well be a trigger for Kuruth for you. Off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T18:02:03-07:00","id":170228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=169790#post169790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't usually wanna bite toxic spirits/claimed, and tasting living flesh could very well be a trigger for Kuruth for you. Off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you fight more in the human-ish shapes, it's more useful to create fetishes for attacking with your hands. Gauntlets, bracers, bands wrapped around your arms, whatever. <br /> <br /> But yeah, my take is mostly that there are some things you don't want in your mouth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T19:30:45-07:00","id":170339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=169683#post169683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't be more logical to all the time just Bite everyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because apparently you group plays nice when it comes to combat. I would rule that if they attempted to bite something and rolled a dramatic failure, that they could potentially bite something not so fun and lose the ability to bite for the following turn. That, and I also rule that any opponent that has any sort of spikes, protrusions, or other such defense would be a horrifying idea to use bite against. Ever see a dog vs a porcupine? Same thing. Now granted that as it currently stands, bite does give the better dice pool, but that doesn't always mean it is a good idea<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T19:42:19-07:00","id":170345,"title":"","content":"I think damage should be increased.<br /> <br /> But in gauru form you can wield klaives which could do more damage and do more than damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T20:34:44-07:00","id":170362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=170345#post170345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think damage should be increased.<br /> <br /> But in gauru form you can wield klaives which could do more damage and do more than damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you wield Klaives in Gauru form? I haven't read a whole lot of Werewolf books, but the description in the core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A klaive is a hand-to-hand weapon \u2014 a sword, dagger, spear, axe, hammer or other implement of destruction. A werewolf in the throes of Rage isn\u2019t capable of using such delicate, finesse weapons, and klaives are made for the sort of life-and-death situations in which Rage is quick to rise. </div> </div> </div>would seem to imply that you cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T21:51:52-07:00","id":170395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are often sized such that they can be used most effectively in Dalu form, yet also useful in Gauru. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T22:02:50-07:00","id":170403,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T04:28:55-07:00","id":170554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=169683#post169683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As first real fight in Gauru broke out on our game session this problem emerge. If Claws in Gauru ( and all other forms for it ) does 1L damage lower than Bite ( that don't need Grappling ), why to use them? Wouldn't be more logical to all the time just Bite everyone?<br /> <br /> Myself, I would made both natural weapons as +1L Damage, only Bite would have Armor Piercing 1. This way Gauru would mostly used Claws, but when enemy was tougher, or more damage needed to be done, he would long for Biting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. I think Gauru Claws are supposed to have an Initiative bonus, it might have been missed/been removed though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T09:21:51-07:00","id":170816,"title":"","content":"How do you handle multiple weapons in a fight? you bit last turn, when do you apply the claws bonus? after your action? at the start of next turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T09:38:37-07:00","id":170821,"title":"","content":"I believe (and I'll need to check the GMC core to confirm) that when you switch weapons during a combat, the Initiative modifier of the new weapon is applied to your Initiative the round after you first use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T10:21:43-07:00","id":170857,"title":"","content":"I know normally a weapon's initiative modifier applies as long as you're holding the weapon, even if you're not actively using it. But I don't think that really makes sense for natural weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T12:07:21-07:00","id":170948,"title":"","content":"Changes in Initiative penalty take place on the next turn (you can't drop a -3 Init weapon and suddenly go before the other guy).<br /> <br /> Multiple weapons are only addressed in the GMC rules regarding pairs (increase the penalty of the highest one by 1 if you have two).<br /> <br /> The problem is that unarmed is assumed to not modify Initiative at all. So 'natural weapons' if they fall into 'unarmed' for the purposes of Initiative would just default to no impact on Initiative mods (they don't add a penalty and they don't count towards multiple weapon penalties assuming that readying more than 2 is possible and extrapolates from the existing rules).<br /> <br /> I'd assume that's why any Initiative bonus to claws got cut. If they count as unarmed for the purposes of Initiative penalties, they're already a step above dual-wielding two 1L weapons (which would have a penalty of -2 or -3 depending what you're using).<br /> <br /> None of this really gives a reason to claw over bite, but that never really bothered me because wolves don't default to their claws as their primary weapons. Claws are back-up weapons for when biting isn't a good (or available) idea is fine for me. It's not like having those claws costs you anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T21:56:35-07:00","id":172438,"title":"","content":"I still find it really awkward that some parts of a werewolfs shapeshifted body is considered supernatural and some parts aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T22:27:34-07:00","id":172470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=172438#post172438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it really awkward that some parts of a werewolfs shapeshifted body is considered supernatural and some parts aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you also find it awkward that there is an entire other world they deal with where symbolism takes precedence over things like biology and physics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T23:20:11-07:00","id":172504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=172470#post172470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you also find it awkward that there is an entire other world they deal with where symbolism takes precedence over things like biology and physics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, not in the least.<br /> <br /> I just find it awkward that some supernatural elements of a werewolf aren't considered to be supernatural mechanically while others are. Yes, I know someones going to try to say that real life wolves mostly rely on their teeth or something like that, but that doesn't really feel like an appropriate excuse to me. Every inch of a spirit wolf is supernatural, so to me it seems like when a werewolf shapeshifts and takes on aspects of said supernatural spirit entity that the traits they gain should be supernatural in nature. I would even be fine with none of their traits being considered supernatural since I could reason that even though they're part spirit beast they're bodies, even when shapeshifted, still maintain their mundane human natures. I can even go along with just having their natural weapons be supernatural, since I'd see that as them partially gaining their half spirit natures supernatural hunting tools, and I'd be fine with that. But having just part of it like this feels same game mechanic-y. It's further aggravated by knowing the reason it's in that weird state.<br /> <br /> For some reason this is one of those little nit picky things that are disproportionately jarring for me. Mechanically it will almost never matter, and in the situations where it does come up it is neither overpowered nor underpowered regardless of what part of their body is or isn't considered supernatural. It's just something that nags at me every time I think about the Idigam Chronicles. It's also easily houseruled, so regardless it's unlikely to ever be a real problem, but holy hell does it aggravate me for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T00:57:27-07:00","id":172528,"title":"","content":"Werewolves aren't spirits. They're beings that are part spirit. They also aren't more or less spirit in any given form than others.<br /> <br /> I think you're too hung up on the word &quot;supernatural&quot; here. Vampires and werewolves are supernatural. If you're going to interpret this are broadly as you seem to be, a vampire's punch should be a supernatural attack and a werewolf in Dalu kicking you should be a supernatural attack. Because they're attacks made by something that is only possible because of supernatural power.<br /> <br /> The point of designating something as a supernatural attack/weapon/etc. rather than an attack/etc. used by a supernatural creature is that this attack/weapon is supernaturally special on its own.<br /> <br /> And with that comes the simple point that the line between supernatural attack/weapon only needs to follow the arbitrary and fictional logic of the people writing the game. If the writers decide that bites are supernaturally potent due to the symbolism of wolves and claws aren't? Then that's how it works. Just like elbows, fists, and headbutts aren't special either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T06:10:32-07:00","id":172695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=172528#post172528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves aren't spirits. They're beings that are part spirit. They also aren't more or less spirit in any given form than others.<br /> <br /> I think you're too hung up on the word &quot;supernatural&quot; here. Vampires and werewolves are supernatural. If you're going to interpret this are broadly as you seem to be, a vampire's punch should be a supernatural attack and a werewolf in Dalu kicking you should be a supernatural attack. Because they're attacks made by something that is only possible because of supernatural power.<br /> <br /> The point of designating something as a supernatural attack/weapon/etc. rather than an attack/etc. used by a supernatural creature is that this attack/weapon is supernaturally special on its own.<br /> <br /> And with that comes the simple point that the line between supernatural attack/weapon only needs to follow the arbitrary and fictional logic of the people writing the game. If the writers decide that bites are supernaturally potent due to the symbolism of wolves and claws aren't? Then that's how it works. Just like elbows, fists, and headbutts aren't special either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The arbitrary nature of this happens to feel a lot more forced/artificial than the other aspects of the setting/line. Sure, you can go along with it being true 'just because' but that leaves a rather bad taste in my mouth. You and some others may be willing to just casually overlook such things and accept it 'just because' but it's something that really grates on me. Though as I've said, mechanically it's irrelevant either way, so I'll either just learn to deal with it, houserule it, or just stick to mage, vampire, and changeling (Which will hopefully also get a GMC update).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T08:53:34-07:00","id":172848,"title":"","content":"Oh, great. This argument again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:01:36-07:00","id":172856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=172848#post172848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, great. This argument again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dreaded seeing this thread resurrected in the first place because I figured it would pop back up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T09:34:56-07:00","id":172903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=172695#post172695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The arbitrary nature of this happens to feel a lot more forced/artificial than the other aspects of the setting/line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such are the dangers of paying attention to open development blogs. You get to see why things work and changes being made rather than just the final product where everything is laid out as-is.<br /> <br /> We get it. You don't like the reasoning for this choice and it decreases your appreciation of the rules changes. But that's all you're managing to say. You're not making an sort of meaningful or insightful commentary on why things should be changed. And you're getting pretty accusatory about other people's feelings about this.<br /> <br /> You're also making a rather big fuss over... the type of damage one of a werewolf's natural weapons in some of their forms do when interacting with other supernatural critters. This is not the end of the world. If this is really going to make WtF unplayable for you... seriously try to put what you're saying in a bit more context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T12:10:21-07:00","id":173042,"title":"","content":"The reasoning is a whiny outcry of &quot;OMFG URATHA OP!1!&quot;.<br /> <br /> I find it annoying too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T12:35:11-07:00","id":173064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=173042#post173042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reasoning is a whiny outcry of &amp;quot;OMFG URATHA OP!1!&amp;quot;. I find it annoying too.</div> </div> </div> </div> In Ashenrogue's defense, he specifically stated he didn't think it had any significant impact on power either way. He just finds it weird that some of their natural weaponry counts as supernatural and some does not. Plus, if I recall correctly, he's in the &quot;teeth and claws should both be supernatural&quot; camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T13:45:48-07:00","id":173118,"title":"","content":"To be fair... It IS weird. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T13:58:08-07:00","id":173130,"title":"","content":"The question I would pose to that though, is it weird because of 20+ years of WOD werewolves having supernaturally awesome claws and teeth and it has been changed, or is it weird because of something specific about drawing the line at teeth only?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T14:11:11-07:00","id":173140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=173130#post173130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I would pose to that though, is it weird because of 20+ years of WOD werewolves having supernaturally awesome claws and teeth and it has been changed, or is it weird because of something specific about drawing the line at teeth only?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond the vampire fan-base outcry? Bite a vampire, he forces himself to bleed. Bond stage 1, and take swooning and addiction.<br /> <br /> It's the classic enemy you don't WANT to bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T14:44:48-07:00","id":173186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=173130#post173130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question I would pose to that though, is it weird because of 20+ years of WOD werewolves having supernaturally awesome claws and teeth and it has been changed, or is it weird because of something specific about drawing the line at teeth only?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't been playing WoD for 20+ years. I've only been playing for like 6, and in that time I played maybe a dozen sessions of W:tF and absolutely no W:tA. I don't really have any preconceived notions about what WoD werewolves teeth and claws are like. I think it's weird that either their teeth or claws are supernatural, but not half as weird as just their teeth being supernatural and not their claws. So, you know, YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T16:45:54-07:00","id":173327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=173140#post173140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beyond the vampire fan-base outcry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, that isn't anything actually weird about the division itself in the context of the game. That's frustration with the devs caving to rather weak criticisms about supernatural interactions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bite a vampire, he forces himself to bleed. Bond stage 1, and take swooning and addiction.<br /> <br /> It's the classic enemy you don't WANT to bite. </div> </div> </div>Fortunately werewolves have a lot of tools for dealing with things they don't want to bite besides claws... Fetish weapons... or just using Dalu and human tools (fire!) over lupine forms. Or getting your pack's Totem to smack the vampire around. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:01:11-07:00","id":173397,"title":"","content":"To quote DaveB in the Mage thread, balance between the games takes a backseat to balance within the game world it's self. After all, it's far more worrying if the Iron Masters are doing the Bone Shadow's job much better than they vs a Kindred Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:10:44-07:00","id":173403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=173327#post173327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...] just using Dalu and human tools over lupine forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words: Bashing damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-18-2014, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:20:45-07:00","id":173430,"title":"","content":"One of the arguments against the, 'they're OP' side,was pointing out that anyone could use fire and do aggravated damage, so how is having them do lethal with their supernatural weapons overpowered?<br /> <br /> It doesn't really seem like totems will be something you can just sic on enemies like that, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T19:06:49-07:00","id":173480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=173403#post173403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two words: Bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two words:<br /> <br /> Flame thrower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T07:24:59-07:00","id":174107,"title":"","content":"My Two Words... <i><b>Crispy Critter</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T12:29:30-07:00","id":174433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=172903#post172903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Such are the dangers of paying attention to open development blogs. You get to see why things work and changes being made rather than just the final product where everything is laid out as-is.<br /> <br /> We get it. You don't like the reasoning for this choice and it decreases your appreciation of the rules changes. But that's all you're managing to say. You're not making an sort of meaningful or insightful commentary on why things should be changed. And you're getting pretty accusatory about other people's feelings about this.<br /> <br /> You're also making a rather big fuss over... the type of damage one of a werewolf's natural weapons in some of their forms do when interacting with other supernatural critters. This is not the end of the world. If this is really going to make WtF unplayable for you... seriously try to put what you're saying in a bit more context.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just the reasoning behind it that I don't like, it's the end result. As people have pointed out, even ignoring the reasoning this half way state of things is weird. While I don't like the cause of the weird state, the cause isn't the issue, the problem is the end result. The fact that it comes off as weird/awkward is the problem in and of itself. Like I said, had they said that neither teeth nor claws counted as supernatural weaponry I would have grumbled a bit but accepted it easily enough because it would have felt consistent. The only reason I even still care is because this half state just feels really artificial and wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:00:43-07:00","id":174485,"title":"","content":"I'm not seeing how there's a significant difference between the reasoning and the end result.<br /> <br /> And I'll bad to a previous point:<br /> <br /> Why are you ok with the &quot;half-state&quot; of fists vs. teeth? Why are claws special compared to all of the other natural weapons a werewolf has? Lethal vs. Bashing damage is no longer a matter of &quot;blunt&quot; vs. &quot;sharp&quot; any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T13:55:47-07:00","id":174539,"title":"","content":"So Teeth Trump Claws Trump Fists?<br /> <br /> And there is a Simple Gift that makes Fists Lethal (so why not claws too?). Does that make Claws Supernatural for the same gift? And do Teeth become Aggravated (since they are already Supernaturally Lethal)?<br /> <br /> Claws/Teeth for Shapes other than Human and Urhan should be supernaturally Lethal. I can live without Aggravated. *shrug*<br /> It isn't a matter of Sharp vs. Blunt, you are correct... It is a matter that These Forms are Supernatural, and do not exist outside nature... I see a HUGE difference in regards to that comparison.<br /> <br /> So what that it takes a Discipline for the Vampire to get there (The Vampiric FORM is inherently Natural - it is a human after all, and protean 2 does not change that, since it gives benefits inherent in Nature, which is why they need Protean 4 for supernatural changes), I don't care about Vampires and their peasly Disciplines anyways. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-19-2014, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:00:04-07:00","id":174543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174485#post174485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing how there's a significant difference between the reasoning and the end result.<br /> <br /> And I'll bad to a previous point:<br /> <br /> Why are you ok with the &quot;half-state&quot; of fists vs. teeth? Why are claws special compared to all of the other natural weapons a werewolf has? Lethal vs. Bashing damage is no longer a matter of &quot;blunt&quot; vs. &quot;sharp&quot; any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me at least, it's because I don't really consider fists weapons. Though we're in tricky territory, since perhaps from the wolf's perspective (and the Werewolf's) teeth and claws are just as much non-weapons in the same way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T14:24:50-07:00","id":174560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174485#post174485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not seeing how there's a significant difference between the reasoning and the end result.<br /> <br /> And I'll bad to a previous point:<br /> <br /> Why are you ok with the &quot;half-state&quot; of fists vs. teeth? Why are claws special compared to all of the other natural weapons a werewolf has? Lethal vs. Bashing damage is no longer a matter of &quot;blunt&quot; vs. &quot;sharp&quot; any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because fists aren't something a werewolf gains through supernatural means while the flesh rending claws and a set of massive predatory teeth are. Punching gains more damage through indirect supernatural modification (enhanced strength), whereas the claws and teeth, weapons directly changed/enhanced by their shapeshifting, are the tools actually used to deal the damage. It's the difference between a mage using Forces to hit someone with magic created force and using magic to grab a tree branch and hit someone with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T15:35:02-07:00","id":174628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174560#post174560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because fists aren't something a werewolf gains through supernatural means while the flesh rending claws and a set of massive predatory teeth are. Punching gains more damage through indirect supernatural modification (enhanced strength), whereas the claws and teeth, weapons directly changed/enhanced by their shapeshifting, are the tools actually used to deal the damage. It's the difference between a mage using Forces to hit someone with magic created force and using magic to grab a tree branch and hit someone with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those fists are still supernaturally changed, as are elbows and everything else. The claws are nails that are enhanced in a similar way as are the teeth. Or are you saying that humans don't have fingernails and teeth also?<br /> <br /> I don't see why a werewolf needs to inherently be able to do something to another template period. Why is it even considered that werewolves can bypass that? Why is that a prerequisite to being able to hurt spirits? Why aren't they mutually exclusive situations? What designates a supernatural change from a physical when said physical changes are the result of supernatural power? You want to talk about arbitrary nerfing, I'll talk about arbitrary creation concepts. Why would werewolves inherently be able to hurt something in a special way that inherently doesn't have shit to do with them?<br /> <br /> Because predators? Father/Mother Wolf's story didn't have anything to do with vampires or other monsters, pretty sure that was exclusively spirits and humans. What does that have to do with an unnatural, unspiritual being that has nothing more to do with spirits than just what its actions cause (And then so, likely less than the human population of any given city). Hell elder vampires even have to get a merit just to make use of Werewolf blood, and feeding is kind of Vampire's niche.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I was all for Gauru having both Teeth and Claws, but was reluctant on the other two intermediate forms.<br /> <br /> Also, I had really hoped this wouldn't come up again, especially months later when everyone I had on my side hasn't posted for months.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:01:29-07:00","id":174670,"title":"","content":"I don't see this as being about sides. Though I'm closer to your opinion on these things Rani.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think the last few posts have more than adequately shown that the &quot;half state&quot; thing is a completely arbitrary. There isn't actually a good reason why any natural &quot;weapons&quot; should be special. The solutions are none of them count as supernatural on their own, all of them do, or only some of them do. Everyone seems comfortable with the answer of &quot;some&quot; but there's a lot of resistance to just accepting that where you set the &quot;some&quot; line is arbitrary. You can make up a reason for any of them.<br /> <br /> Teeth are the only special ones because of the symbolism of wolves is about their bites.<br /> <br /> Teeth and claws are the only special ones because they represent that savage fury of predatory spirits.<br /> <br /> Etc.<br /> <br /> None of these are actually better than the other. They're all incredibly easy to change if you don't like them. And... have exceedingly little impact on the game since at the moment it only matters for werewolves vs. vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T16:58:24-07:00","id":174700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174670#post174670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And... have exceedingly little impact on the game since at the moment it only matters for werewolves vs. vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> And ephemeral entities, presumably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T17:19:28-07:00","id":174708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174700#post174700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And ephemeral entities, presumably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily, they're easily mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:17:56-07:00","id":174786,"title":"","content":"Well I've just been assuming that werewolves being able to negate vampire damage downgrading was a side effect of being able to do the same to spirits. Or are we talking about something else? Because I'm not sure what &quot;mutually exclusive&quot; is referring to here, specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T18:49:18-07:00","id":174817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174786#post174786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I've just been assuming that werewolves being able to negate vampire damage downgrading was a side effect of being able to do the same to spirits. Or are we talking about something else? Because I'm not sure what &quot;mutually exclusive&quot; is referring to here, specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Protean 4 is able to deal lethal damage to vampires also, but it doesn't hit ephemeral entities. One doesn't necessarily mean the other. That has been part of my argument throughout most of the earlier parts of this thread. Just because it does something to one, doesn't mean that it works equivalently to the other. I'm saying that being able to inflict damage to spirits, doesn't necessarily mean that it does lethal to vampires. You can have one without the other.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I still think Gauru should be able to use both claws and teeth for lethal against vampires, I just didn't think the other two intermediates should, it seemed very reminiscent of the OWoD days and I didn't particularly like that and a general bad trend to start (Adding an innate, without drawback, kills this other line ability that costs no exp).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:03:54-07:00","id":174871,"title":"","content":"Well, forums ate my post and I don't care enough to retype my text wall so I'll give you the short version.<br /> <br /> A werewolves fists haven't really changed in a way that is mechanically relevant, while the teeth and claws have been directly altered to become better killing tools. While werewolves do gain increased strength the damage from supernatural strength increases is applied indirectly, usually through mundane means. Again, a Forces mage hitting something with telekinetic force would be constitute as a supernatural attack, while the same person using telekinesis to launch a stick (even a stick enchanted to turn water into wine) at someone would not (unless the stick was enchanted to do increased damage or apply damage in supernatural ways). Now note that I wouldn't necessarily mind if a werewolves entire body were considered a supernaturally charged weapon designed for hunting (which sounds pretty cool now that I type it out), but I do have a problem with their teeth being considered supernatural weaponry when they have another set of natural weapons that are enhanced by the same process, in the same fashion, and for the same reasons yet don't count as such.<br /> <br /> As for other templates, screw the other templates. Screw mage, screw changeling, screw vampire, and screw every other splat that isn't the focus of this development. This isn't about them. This is about making werewolf the best damn game it can be, and they are irrelevant to that. I don't care who or what is weak to/strong against supernatural weaponry (or anything werewolves may or may not have tbh), this argument is to get a fix for the awkward state werewolf natural weaponry is currently in internally. Ignoring any other gameline, I feel that having only one part of their modified assets count as supernatural, while not necessarily mechanically detrimental. to be a flaw. They were changed by the same process, in pretty much the same way, to perform the same function. I can't really see an acceptable justification for the decision to have one of them be considered supernaturally potent while the other isn't. It lacks internal consistency that can easily be fixed, and the fix doesn't really chance the system balance one way or the other. All I ask is that they be equalized, whether they're both to be considered supernatural or they're both to be considered mundane is totally up for discussion, but I really feel that this weird half state has to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:27:22-07:00","id":174904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174871#post174871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for other templates, screw the other templates. Screw mage, screw changeling, screw vampire, and screw every other splat that isn't the focus of this development. This isn't about them. This is about making werewolf the best damn game it can be, and they are irrelevant to that. I don't care who or what is weak to/strong against supernatural weaponry (or anything werewolves may or may not have tbh), this argument is to get a fix for the awkward state werewolf natural weaponry is currently in internally.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, currently the only thing in the game that gives a damn whether or not a werewolf's teeth, claws, or anything else is supernatural or not, is vampires. If &quot;supernatural weapon&quot; was a quality that other parts of the system checked for, I would agree with you. However, as it currently stands, the only difference a thing being supernatural or not makes is what kind of damage it deals to vampires, which makes it impossible to discuss whether or not something should be supernatural without bringing vampires into it. If it wasn't for vampires' damage reduction, there would be absolutely no reason to bother pointing out that they're supernatural (or, for that matter, any reason not to), and therefore no reason for this discussion to take place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T20:40:33-07:00","id":174914,"title":"","content":"@AshenRogue<br /> <br /> Just like all your arguing the first time around eh?<br /> <br /> Well, enlarged hands, knuckles, and other aspects, especially when armored in Guaru (unless that changes) seem enhanced to me.<br /> <br /> My problem is the arbitrary use of 'supernatural' as automatically bypassing another splats also innate ability. Why can't they simply be able to deal with spirit and werewolf focused enemies in one way, and leave crossover stuff up to GM's? Why does being able to do lethal damage to spirits have to translate to doing lethal damage to vampires other than for an arbitrary reason? Why is it so different than another ability that has to be invested in to replicate pretty well the same effects? You wanna swing around definitions of supernatural and mundane, but we don't really have any definition of what actually constitutes one or the other beyond one aspect in Vampire.<br /> <br /> Games are developed with internal consistency, but to say they don't borrow concepts from one another, especially previous works is willful ignorance.<br /> <br /> Why does a werewolf innate trait have to ignore an innate trait that may or may not even exist in werewolf? While it might come into play in regards to the hosts, I don't see it likely being the same, and I don't see the need for &quot;Harms spirits&quot; to be the same as &quot;Harms vampires which aren't necessarily even an inherent part of werewolf's setting&quot;. There apparently is going to be a gift that is going to wreck vampires, and I have no issue with something that requires an experience investment for use against a niche enemy. The same is true about elder vampires who want to benefit from werewolf blood.<br /> <br /> Now this is again something I don't understand as why its even pertinent to the Werewolf line, when it could just be that its damage applies to spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 06-19-2014, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:10:39-07:00","id":174930,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Sin-Eaters are going to be the only other splat to fit into the sacred prey of the tribes.<br /> <br /> I think bending to the cries of the crowd was disappointing. But they didn't change any of the things I thought should be changed so maybe I'm just bitter.<br /> Either way, people can play them however they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-20-2014, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:20:23-07:00","id":174939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174700#post174700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And ephemeral entities, presumably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemeral entities downgrade all lethal damage to bashing unless otherwise stated (generally Banes). It doesn't matter if the source of lethal is a gun or supernatural claws.<br /> <br /> Though the Idigam Chronicles seem to be including plenty to address this in regards to making sure werewolves have anti-spirit stuff, but that's specified by things that allow werewolves to do better than bashing to spirits explicitly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:44:22-07:00","id":174946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174930#post174930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the Sin-Eaters are going to be the only other splat to fit into the sacred prey of the tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually really hoping there's a similar line in the Hunters in Darkness' writeup comparing vampires to the Hosts. I guess Iron Masters considering them the worst parts of humanity would be fine too, but the former would fit in perfectly with the crossover game I'm planning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:02:29-07:00","id":174955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174946#post174946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually really hoping there's a similar line in the Hunters in Darkness' writeup comparing vampires to the Hosts. I guess Iron Masters considering them the worst parts of humanity would be fine too, but the former would fit in perfectly with the crossover game I'm planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them perhaps. I think most Iron Masters would realize that Vampires come with the territory and are actually quite useful if you can get them away from their pretty politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:03:36-07:00","id":174956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174939#post174939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ephemeral entities downgrade all lethal damage to bashing unless otherwise stated (generally Banes). It doesn't matter if the source of lethal is a gun or supernatural claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that any different from how vampires receive damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:26:37-07:00","id":174988,"title":"","content":"Um... there's pretty big difference between downgrades all lethal damage with exceptions (how ephemeral entities is phrased), and downgrades lethal damage from mundane weapons with exceptions (how vampires are phrased).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T22:53:05-07:00","id":174999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174946#post174946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually really hoping there's a similar line in the Hunters in Darkness' writeup comparing vampires to the Hosts. I guess Iron Masters considering them the worst parts of humanity would be fine too, but the former would fit in perfectly with the crossover game I'm planning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume Iron Masters get mages as they supernatural stereotype - Awakened are <b>still</b> humans, for all it it. Or maybe Hunters, the humans fighting the Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T23:13:37-07:00","id":175011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174904#post174904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, currently the only thing in the game that gives a damn whether or not a werewolf's teeth, claws, or anything else is supernatural or not, is vampires. If &quot;supernatural weapon&quot; was a quality that other parts of the system checked for, I would agree with you. However, as it currently stands, the only difference a thing being supernatural or not makes is what kind of damage it deals to vampires, which makes it impossible to discuss whether or not something should be supernatural without bringing vampires into it. If it wasn't for vampires' damage reduction, there would<br /> be absolutely no reason to bother pointing out that they're supernatural (or, for that matter, any reason not to), and therefore no reason for this discussion to take place.</div> </div> </div> </div>They got shafted for being the first line, as usual. We'll see how single Spirit Mages go around making entire packs look like red haired step-childs when they twist their pack's totem into a fancy new familiar of them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T23:34:41-07:00","id":175018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175011#post175011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They got shafted for being the first line, as usual. We'll see how single Spirit Mages go around making entire packs look like red haired step-childs when they twist their pack's totem into a fancy new familiar of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no doubt. I mean, buffing vampires in the new edition was a nice thought, but I'm sure every line that gets updated will want fancy new toys, and by the time they're all GMC compliant I expect there will be as much power disparity across the lines as ever, just with everyone being even stronger. Which is honestly fine with me, I never really cared about cross-line balance anyway, and even though Vampire is my favorite line, I have no problem with them being the weakest. Would be nice if there was some logical consistency on what counted as supernatural and what didn't though. We'll see how that goes as more games get updated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T02:03:05-07:00","id":175073,"title":"","content":"Urgh. Can't... resist... engaging.<br /> <br /> This is not a werewolf issue. This will only come up when werewolves fight vamps. <i>That is it.</i> Other properties of the bite/claw are yet to be revealed.<br /> <br /> It is not about what damage the werewolves do: <i>it is about what damage vamps receive</i>. All beasts and fowl we have heard about <i>but one</i> take lethal from weapons. Including werewolf claws and bites.<br /> <br /> But vamps have their own approach to how they take weapon damage. For some reason, the werewolf developer felt it worth registering how werewolf natural weapons interact with an as yet exclusively vamp ability. <br /> <br /> Supernatural/non-supernatural is as yet fluff we have not seen substantiated; we are writing out own material in our heads and then panicking about it. <br /> <br /> We do know we have been promised fluff that will make sense of the werewolves intersplat-specific ability.<br /> <br /> Oh god, what have I done.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:01:56-07:00","id":175172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=174914#post174914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@AshenRogue<br /> <br /> Just like all your arguing the first time around eh?<br /> <br /> Well, enlarged hands, knuckles, and other aspects, especially when armored in Guaru (unless that changes) seem enhanced to me.<br /> <br /> My problem is the arbitrary use of 'supernatural' as automatically bypassing another splats also innate ability. Why can't they simply be able to deal with spirit and werewolf focused enemies in one way, and leave crossover stuff up to GM's? Why does being able to do lethal damage to spirits have to translate to doing lethal damage to vampires other than for an arbitrary reason? Why is it so different than another ability that has to be invested in to replicate pretty well the same effects? You wanna swing around definitions of supernatural and mundane, but we don't really have any definition of what actually constitutes one or the other beyond one aspect in Vampire.<br /> <br /> Games are developed with internal consistency, but to say they don't borrow concepts from one another, especially previous works is willful ignorance.<br /> <br /> Why does a werewolf innate trait have to ignore an innate trait that may or may not even exist in werewolf? While it might come into play in regards to the hosts, I don't see it likely being the same, and I don't see the need for &quot;Harms spirits&quot; to be the same as &quot;Harms vampires which aren't necessarily even an inherent part of werewolf's setting&quot;. There apparently is going to be a gift that is going to wreck vampires, and I have no issue with something that requires an experience investment for use against a niche enemy. The same is true about elder vampires who want to benefit from werewolf blood.<br /> <br /> Now this is again something I don't understand as why its even pertinent to the Werewolf line, when it could just be that its damage applies to spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the first time I was arguing game balance and gameline integrity, this time I'm arguing internal consistency within the werewolf line itself.<br /> <br /> Yet the fists don't change in any meaningful way mechanically. They don't inflict lethal, they don't deal increased damage, they can't block blades or any other kind of attack any better than a normal humans hands can, etc. While they change a bit in order to support their new grown claws, and do increase in size, they alone don't really function any differently. There is little difference between getting punched by a werewolf in hishu and a werewolf in dalu other than the fact that the muscles in the persons arm and back are able to produce much more force when in dalu. That said, as previously stated, I wouldn't mind at all if they stated that a werewolves entire body was to be treated as a supernatural weapon. I could roll with that pretty easily. But as is, it's like having a werewolves legs be supernatural but not their arms, or the left side of their body but not their right, and that is just something that strikes me as really arbitrary and wrong.<br /> <br /> You can take the arbitrary nature of supernatural abilities bypassing vampire damage mitigation with the vampire line, since it's their that the ruling comes from. To be quite honest, they can completely remove the mention of vampires from the book entirely for all I care, in fact, I would prefer they do if only to alleviate the whining. If they want a werewolves natural weaponry to be considered supernaturally potent that's all well and good, STs can decide for themselves what that means for themselves in their own games. If they then decide that that is good enough to bypass vampire downgrade, assuming their are even vampires in their game, good for them. If they decide against it? Good for them. Take note that I'm not even necessarily arguing for the claws to also be considered supernatural, I would also readily accept werewolf teeth simply being considered mundane. I just want internal consistency at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 06-20-2014, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T08:46:43-07:00","id":175270,"title":"","content":"&quot;Not applied consistently&quot; and &quot;internally consistency&quot; are not the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:00:27-07:00","id":175495,"title":"","content":"The lethal to bashing downrade of normal weapon damage for vampires does not work for all cases, this is not an always work rule. Read the specific text carefully, it says ''most normal weapons'' , which means there are normal weapons that do lethal to vampires. So no big deal if a werewolf does lethal with fangs and claws because simply he can. Why bothering further ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3163-furrly","name":"Furrly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:24:00-07:00","id":175512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furrly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175495#post175495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lethal to bashing downrade of normal weapon damage for vampires does not work for all cases, this is not an always work rule. Read the specific text carefully, it says ''most normal weapons'' , which means there are normal weapons that do lethal to vampires. So no big deal if a werewolf does lethal with fangs and claws because simply he can. Why bothering further ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because supernatural or otherwise, it feels awkward for the damage their claws do to be downgraded and the damage their teeth so to not be downgraded. It would feel more consistent for neither to be downgraded or for both to be downgraded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:38:36-07:00","id":175516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furrly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175495#post175495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lethal to bashing downrade of normal weapon damage for vampires does not work for all cases, this is not an always work rule. Read the specific text carefully, it says ''most normal weapons'' , which means there are normal weapons that do lethal to vampires. So no big deal if a werewolf does lethal with fangs and claws because simply he can. Why bothering further ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: Is there an actual statement saying a chainsaw doesn't does lethal damage to vampires? Because if I go by my gut that shit should be Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:51:15-07:00","id":175524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175516#post175516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Question: Is there an actual statement saying a chainsaw doesn't does lethal damage to vampires? Because if I go by my gut that shit should be Lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is not, and I wouldn't blame you for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:54:12-07:00","id":175525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furrly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175495#post175495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lethal to bashing downrade of normal weapon damage for vampires does not work for all cases, this is not an always work rule. Read the specific text carefully, it says ''most normal weapons'' , which means there are normal weapons that do lethal to vampires. So no big deal if a werewolf does lethal with fangs and claws because simply he can. Why bothering further ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are normal weapons that would do lethal to vampires, but they're not the normal weapons most are going to be packing. Grenades certainly could, anything that would do agg to a human is lethal. If you want to take things out of context, then put more thought into the process. Why should a werewolf claw be the equivalent of a grenade against vampires? Why should werewolves have a goddamn thing to do with vampires anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, don't use a generalized statement like that without specifics to support an argument. It also says &quot;Most Non-supernatural weapons&quot; specifically not &quot;most normal weapons&quot;. Then there's the point that vampires even downgrade some magical agg damage (in this case I think things like boiling blood probably isn't going to be agg but might cause vitae loss and lethal damage).<br /> <br /> I personally don't see that big of an issue with the teeth and claws being different (Symbolically wolves attack with teeth, and spirits are all about symbolism). But then again I was pushing for both in Gauru and none from all other forms, devs just went with Teeth I think because of the potential drawback in relation to biting vampires, and I agree that was a poor choice.<br /> <br /> I would rather it not specify one way or the other against vampires, just that they affect spirits and spiritual entities with lethal damage and count as weapons against humans. I don't see why werewolves need to be able to bypass a vampire's innate states advantages, I don't see why vampires have anything to do with any concept with werewolf beyond a possible niche build. A sidebar saying &quot;It may or may not harm other entities that downgrade damage in a similar way to spirits&quot; would be acceptable too, but I'd rather see it relegated to just Gauru, or some merit/gift in regard to vampires (Maybe a Unnatural Affinity-like merit that lets werewolves bypass a protection per dot even). I just don't like the concept of one line immediately after a previous release having a sudden &quot;this innately trumps the previous&quot;. It sets a bad precedent.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's going to be some power-creep between lines such that they won't be that compatible in crossover (lookin at you Mage!), but it would be nice if they didn't just start throwing innate abilities that bypass other gamelines innate abilities by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T13:57:49-07:00","id":175529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Is there an actual statement saying a chainsaw doesn't does lethal damage to vampires? Because if I go by my gut that shit should be Lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does tear apart chunks of tissue, so yeah, probably Lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 06-20-2014, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T14:21:15-07:00","id":175540,"title":"","content":"We can at least agree that arguing about it isn't going to change the set opinions people have, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T14:22:20-07:00","id":175541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why werewolves need to be able to bypass a vampire's innate states advantages, I don't see why vampires have anything to do with any concept with werewolf beyond a possible niche build.</div> </div> </div> </div>Innate state advantages... That are clearly geared towards being an advantage when facing humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T17:00:20-07:00","id":175638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175541#post175541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Innate state advantages... That are clearly geared towards being an advantage when facing humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>And each other, its rather difficult without experience investment or leaning towards banes to do lethal damage to other vampires. Fangs yeah, but they have a significant drawback. Basically its high protean or high enough strength to be swinging size 5+ items, or specific fighting styles, sorcery can, but good luck with that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,