bcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176043#post176043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure? They didn't have it in the Blog but I don't think that ever came up, and a lot of stuff was &quot;Same as Forsaken core&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am sure. It was asked in the comments of that thread, IIRC, and Stew replied that they don't have armor in gauru anymore (isn't needed, with the epic regeneration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T11:49:35-07:00","id":176252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would rather it not specify one way or the other against vampires, just that they affect spirits and spiritual entities with lethal damage and count as weapons against humans. I don't see why werewolves need to be able to bypass a vampire's innate states advantages, I don't see why vampires have anything to do with any concept with werewolf beyond a possible niche build. A sidebar saying &quot;It may or may not harm other entities that downgrade damage in a similar way to spirits&quot; would be acceptable too, but I'd rather see it relegated to just Gauru, or some merit/gift in regard to vampires (Maybe a Unnatural Affinity-like merit that lets werewolves bypass a protection per dot even). I just don't like the concept of one line immediately after a previous release having a sudden &quot;this innately trumps the previous&quot;. It sets a bad precedent.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If that is your position, Then why should Vampires get to Blood Bond Werewolves Then? They are not Human, after all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:39:10-07:00","id":176288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are normal weapons that would do lethal to vampires, but they're not the normal weapons most are going to be packing. Grenades certainly could, anything that would do agg to a human is lethal. If you want to take things out of context, then put more thought into the process. Why should a werewolf claw be the equivalent of a grenade against vampires? Why should werewolves have a goddamn thing to do with vampires anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because werewolf claws are backed up by the Rage that kills gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't use a generalized statement like that without specifics to support an argument. It also says &quot;Most Non-supernatural weapons&quot; specifically not &quot;most normal weapons&quot;. Then there's the point that vampires even downgrade some magical agg damage (in this case I think things like boiling blood probably isn't going to be agg but might cause vitae loss and lethal damage).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a generalized statement, it is a statement of the Strix chronicles book. This statement of yours for ''non-supernatral-most normals'' is nonsensical.<br /> Non-supenratural IS normal.<br /> <br /> Where does it say about downgrating aggravated ? Surely not on the damage/healing section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't see that big of an issue with the teeth and claws being different (Symbolically wolves attack with teeth, and spirits are all about symbolism). But then again I was pushing for both in Gauru and none from all other forms, devs just went with Teeth I think because of the potential drawback in relation to biting vampires, and I agree that was a poor choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wolves indeed attack with teeth, I would agree that supernatural forms close to Rage like Dalu and Urshul should do lethal to vampires, I am not sure about Urhan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather it not specify one way or the other against vampires, just that they affect spirits and spiritual entities with lethal damage and count as weapons against humans. I don't see why werewolves need to be able to bypass a vampire's innate states advantages, I don't see why vampires have anything to do with any concept with werewolf beyond a possible niche build. A sidebar saying &quot;It may or may not harm other entities that downgrade damage in a similar way to spirits&quot; would be acceptable too, but I'd rather see it relegated to just Gauru, or some merit/gift in regard to vampires (Maybe a Unnatural Affinity-like merit that lets werewolves bypass a protection per dot even). I just don't like the concept of one line immediately after a previous release having a sudden &quot;this innately trumps the previous&quot;. It sets a bad precedent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are half spirit, as such they do damage to supernaturals as spirits do. Plus begin to accept all supernaturals to do lethal to vampires with natural weaponry, the hosts, materialized spirits, etc etc. This is the world of werewolf, a world of lethality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175525#post175525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there's going to be some power-creep between lines such that they won't be that compatible in crossover (lookin at you Mage!), but it would be nice if they didn't just start throwing innate abilities that bypass other gamelines innate abilities by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect great changes in Mage. The game needs new mood, I want to see more component needing magic and spell using ones, not just ''I think and it happens'', this is not magic. Player you want to cast a spell ? Learn the spell rhymes first !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3163-furrly","name":"Furrly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:44:20-07:00","id":176290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=175905#post175905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, no more Armor in Gauru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank the moon the sun and all celestials of the entire cosmos !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3163-furrly","name":"Furrly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:46:04-07:00","id":176293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176252#post176252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that is your position, Then why should Vampires get to Blood Bond Werewolves Then? They are not Human, after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought werewoles could only be addicted to vitae not blood bonded, this is how it originally was in Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3163-furrly","name":"Furrly","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T12:58:48-07:00","id":176318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176252#post176252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If that is your position, Then why should Vampires get to Blood Bond Werewolves Then? They are not Human, after all...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Blood Bond works on other vampires too, not just humans. Its a tool that really only gives dicepool penalties. Werewolves buffing via Flaring Renown is a good equivalent in that regard, but with the opposite effect (buffing the werewolf, rather than penalizing the victim(which it can do, but is more of an equivalent of vampire predatory aura).<br /> <br /> That is pretty well in the same boat, though unlike the werewolf claw thing, it is a wide ranging capability, able to apply to everything, whereas the supernatural damage currently only applies to possible werewolf specific antagonists, and vampires. Its basically a targeted 'vampire killer' capability the way it was originally developed. With the current iteration, its still vampire killer, but has the drawback of being a bite, and I don't particularly like that its one or the other, when personally I thought both teeth and claws should have been Gauru only in regards to vampires. I still don't know why it couldn't just have been &quot;Hurts spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mind you werewolves do have other capabilities that vampires do not, just as vampires do. Vampires aren't going to be attacking from the Shadow, nor will they be able to follow. Vampires and werewolves both have a form of predatory aura (renown flaring's hunt capability that werewolves have), in the case of Werewolf, this is far more powerful. They don't have to be able to innately target vampires to be optimized for their own game. Fire and sunlight are much more common than silver, and spirit negotiations are very unlikely to happen with vampires.<br /> <br /> So much wanting to push a &quot;Can kill vampires&quot; capability, when there's a wide range of advantages they have that can be leveraged against vampires and other groups. Tailoring capabilities specifically to combat another splat is a bad trend to start in any case, especially when there's unlikely anything short of maybe Promethean and maybe Mummy and those are big maybes, if they get updates. Most likely the majority of splats will require some Arcana/Transmutation/etc to do the same.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the &quot;Blood Bond affects other supernaturals&quot; ruling came from this argument, and as a potential drawback for hurting vampires with the bite. It wasn't even given an official ruling until this and its basically clone in the Vampire forum came up with such contentious arguing.<br /> <br /> Nearly everything has a healing capability, if werewolf claws/bites took double time/resource trait to heal, that would be better than something that really applies to just one other splat.<br /> <br /> Also, in the blog there was no mention of them losing the Armor. Also liked your earlier suggestion of an essence per scene to make them supernatural weapons in regard to vampires/spirits/whatever. A cost would have been preferable to scrapping claws altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 06-21-2014, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T13:24:04-07:00","id":176339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furrly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176288#post176288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because werewolf claws are backed up by the Rage that kills gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't Apocalypse. Rage has very little to do with ANYTHING. Werewolf claws can hurt 'gods' because the gods your talking about are SPIRITS, and werewolves are part SPIRIT.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not a generalized statement, it is a statement of the Strix chronicles book. This statement of yours for ''non-supernatral-most normals'' is nonsensical.<br /> Non-supenratural IS normal.<br /> <br /> Where does it say about downgrating aggravated ? Surely not on the damage/healing section. </div> </div> </div>Immortality, Injury, and Mortality, pg 90. Don't try to think your going to beat me on Vampire mechanics. Your basically also ignoring that there is easily a difference in shapeshifted forms from vampire don't even all do lethal damage to vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, Strix are closer tied to vampires than spirits are, and Strix only ever take bashing damage from agg damage, and no damage from anything else. (I'm going to ask in vampire forum about strix and higher ranking strix/spirits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wolves indeed attack with teeth, I would agree that supernatural forms close to Rage like Dalu and Urshul should do lethal to vampires, I am not sure about Urhan. </div> </div> </div>Again, this isn't Apocalypse. Death Rage and the Rage your talking about are very very different things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves are half spirit, as such they do damage to supernaturals as spirits do. Plus begin to accept all supernaturals to do lethal to vampires with natural weaponry, the hosts, materialized spirits, etc etc. This is the world of werewolf, a world of lethality. </div> </div> </div>And what do you think a world where you have to prey on others specifically, required, not optional, is? Unlike werewolves who can hunt, but don't necessarily have to, they could just as well not do anything that is part of the werewolf line. On the other hand Vampires HAVE to hunt, and if they don't, they WILL kill and it WILL be violent. There is no mechanic that forces werewolves to do any of those things like vampires have.<br /> <br /> Mind you if werewolves aren't hunting, it makes for a very boring chronicle (and what the hell kind of ST is going to run that?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I expect great changes in Mage. The game needs new mood, I want to see more component needing magic and spell using ones, not just ''I think and it happens'', this is not magic. Player you want to cast a spell ? Learn the spell rhymes first !!! </div> </div> </div>I do too, but I doubt its going to be anything like your thinking. Improvised magic is very much going to be a major part of it, rotes will be more important but not absolute. Its still going to be very much about shaping the world with your imagination, while styles may be emphasized I doubt they're going to be necessary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T14:50:01-07:00","id":176442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176339#post176339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't Apocalypse. Rage has very little to do with ANYTHING. Werewolf claws can hurt 'gods' because the gods your talking about are SPIRITS, and werewolves are part SPIRIT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to Red Claw, the very first Talon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176339#post176339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortality, Injury, and Mortality, pg 90. Don't try to think your going to beat me on Vampire mechanics. Your basically also ignoring that there is easily a difference in shapeshifted forms from vampire don't even all do lethal damage to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, you wanna compare an entire race of shapeshifters with a clan of vampires that happen to have some shapeshifting tricks?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176339#post176339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Strix are closer tied to vampires than spirits are, and Strix only ever take bashing damage from agg damage, and no damage from anything else. (I'm going to ask in vampire forum about strix and higher ranking strix/spirits).</div> </div> </div> </div>Says who?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176339#post176339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this isn't Apocalypse. Death Rage and the Rage your talking about are very very different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the game is still a &quot;Game of Savage Fury&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176339#post176339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what do you think a world where you have to prey on others specifically, required, not optional, is? Unlike werewolves who can hunt, but don't necessarily have to, they could just as well not do anything that is part of the werewolf line. On the other hand Vampires HAVE to hunt, and if they don't, they WILL kill and it WILL be violent. There is no mechanic that forces werewolves to do any of those things like vampires have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't have to? well shit. I guess I read &quot;The Wolf Must...&quot; Flipping &quot;... Hunt&quot; wrong then.<br /> <br /> Oh wait, failing to hunt is a Breaking Point towards Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 06-21-2014, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T15:00:50-07:00","id":176448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176442#post176442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Says who?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Book. Apparently the only thing thats actually good at fighting Strix are the Khaibit, and other Strix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't have to? well shit. I guess I read &quot;The Wolf Must...&quot; Flipping &quot;... Hunt&quot; wrong then.<br /> <br /> Oh wait, failing to hunt is a Breaking Point towards Humanity. </div> </div> </div>Please point me to where Werewolves have to engage in their hunt or end up dead/effectively dead? Sure they might become too human as far as Harmony goes, but there's nothing that forces it. Vampires on the other hand drop like stones when they haven't fed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 06-21-2014, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T15:05:28-07:00","id":176452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176448#post176448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Book. Please point me to where Werewolves have to engage in their hunt or end up dead/effectively dead? Sure they might become too human as far as Harmony goes, but there's nothing that forces it. Vampires on the other hand drop like stones when they haven't fed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Although a vampire doesn't have to hunt to feed, and it's often much more efficient for them to farm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T15:19:52-07:00","id":176461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176452#post176452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although a vampire doesn't have to hunt to feed, and it's often much more efficient for them to farm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A vampire doesn't have to kill to feed. Even among a herd its still to some extent hunting, selecting the right prey among the herd, the actual feeding. Even if they offer themselves up to you (Basically the same as hunting in a night club) its still hunting, its just easier if they're already there.<br /> <br /> Because someone comes up with an easier way to hunt, doesn't mean its not technically a hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T16:59:49-07:00","id":176538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176461#post176461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A vampire doesn't have to kill to feed. Even among a herd its still to some extent hunting, selecting the right prey among the herd, the actual feeding. Even if they offer themselves up to you (Basically the same as hunting in a night club) its still hunting, its just easier if they're already there. Because someone comes up with an easier way to hunt, doesn't mean its not technically a hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div> I guess in the same sense that working at a slaughterhouse is hunting. Which is to say, not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T18:33:31-07:00","id":176619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176538#post176538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I guess in the same sense that working at a slaughterhouse is hunting. Which is to say, not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still requires gathering the herd in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T19:50:37-07:00","id":176651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176318#post176318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe Blood Bond works on other vampires too, not just humans. Its a tool that really only gives dicepool penalties. Werewolves buffing via Flaring Renown is a good equivalent in that regard, but with the opposite effect (buffing the werewolf, rather than penalizing the victim(which it can do, but is more of an equivalent of vampire predatory aura).<br /> <br /> That is pretty well in the same boat, though unlike the werewolf claw thing, it is a wide ranging capability, able to apply to everything, whereas the supernatural damage currently only applies to possible werewolf specific antagonists, and vampires. Its basically a targeted 'vampire killer' capability the way it was originally developed. With the current iteration, its still vampire killer, but has the drawback of being a bite, and I don't particularly like that its one or the other, when personally I thought both teeth and claws should have been Gauru only in regards to vampires. I still don't know why it couldn't just have been &quot;Hurts spirits&quot;.<br /> <br /> Mind you werewolves do have other capabilities that vampires do not, just as vampires do. Vampires aren't going to be attacking from the Shadow, nor will they be able to follow. Vampires and werewolves both have a form of predatory aura (renown flaring's hunt capability that werewolves have), in the case of Werewolf, this is far more powerful. They don't have to be able to innately target vampires to be optimized for their own game. Fire and sunlight are much more common than silver, and spirit negotiations are very unlikely to happen with vampires.<br /> <br /> So much wanting to push a &quot;Can kill vampires&quot; capability, when there's a wide range of advantages they have that can be leveraged against vampires and other groups. Tailoring capabilities specifically to combat another splat is a bad trend to start in any case, especially when there's unlikely anything short of maybe Promethean and maybe Mummy and those are big maybes, if they get updates. Most likely the majority of splats will require some Arcana/Transmutation/etc to do the same.<br /> <br /> Also, I think the &quot;Blood Bond affects other supernaturals&quot; ruling came from this argument, and as a potential drawback for hurting vampires with the bite. It wasn't even given an official ruling until this and its basically clone in the Vampire forum came up with such contentious arguing.<br /> <br /> Nearly everything has a healing capability, if werewolf claws/bites took double time/resource trait to heal, that would be better than something that really applies to just one other splat.<br /> <br /> Also, in the blog there was no mention of them losing the Armor. Also liked your earlier suggestion of an essence per scene to make them supernatural weapons in regard to vampires/spirits/whatever. A cost would have been preferable to scrapping claws altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div>But by your own reasoning one line shouldn't say a damn thing about how something they do specifically affects another line. By that logic Vampire shouldn't say a damn thing about what does and doesn't affect werewolves/mages/whatever. That should be left up to the ST. Do you agree with that? Do you agree that werewolves shouldn't explicitly be subject to the bloodbond? If you don't, you're being a bit of a hypocrite. If you're fine with that you're saying it's fine for vampire to call out werewolf and explicitly say that one of their features (for better or for worse) messes with them when you so strongly fight against the reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:06:08-07:00","id":176655,"title":"","content":"I do agree, and the book DOESN'T. Its not there. Nowhere in there does it talk about it. That was a ruling that came out of this bullshit &quot;Werewolves bypass vampire protection&quot; conversation in the first place. It wasn't even a ruling until that very point, instead it had previously been ruled otherwise until this discussion came up! Hell it probably would have stayed as &quot;No&quot; except this damn conversation. And after that ruling I didn't care nearly as much. In fact, I don't care either way now because of that, but I still think its poor design to create something that specifically targets another PC splat and only that one.<br /> <br /> Your ignoring whole swaths of my argument on the second part of that though. If something effects one, it should effect everything. If werewolf claws deal lethal to vampires, they should ignore any similar protections and downgradings mage armor should provide, ignore bezoars or whatever they are, be un-bulwarkable(isn't that what sin-eaters do with damage? downgrading lethal to bashing by flooding with plasm?) Etc etc.<br /> <br /> But currently it has no purpose other than specifically vampires and werewolf antagonists. It's highly doubtful mages will have a mage armor that works similar enough, though death or life, and then thats an invested power. Then there's the whole thing about whether or not this or that will have an equivalent. We don't know if anything past Mage will even get a chronicle book!<br /> <br /> As stands, its specifically an ability that fucks over vampires in regards to other player characters. It could just as easily be something that only effects spirits and spirit associated things, but no, it effects vampires and only vampires also.<br /> <br /> What would you think if Promethean's wasteland made werewolves healing less effective, or disquiet? What if 1 essence was always 1 lethal wound when effected by disquiet regardless of primal urge, but didn't have an effect on any other gameline? What if it turned off their bashing damage healing altogether?<br /> <br /> Now if Promethean, Geist, Changeling, and Mummy ever get chronicle books, then there may be more, but even then its still iffy on how that would work or even if it would apply in a similar way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 06-21-2014, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:14:55-07:00","id":176659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176655#post176655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your ignoring whole swaths of my argument on the second part of that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the interest of being true to my nature as a loud hypocritical whiner:<br /> <br /> <b>You're kind of <i>both</i> doing this. Could the lot of you possibly see your way to more completely doing it by <i>ceasing this circular and fruitless argument that is going to convince precisely fuckbody?</i></b><br /> <br /> Because that would be lovely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T20:23:32-07:00","id":176668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176659#post176659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the interest of being true to my nature as a loud hypocritical whiner:<br /> <br /> <b>You're kind of <i>both</i> doing this. Could the lot of you possibly see your way to more completely doing it by <i>ceasing this circular and fruitless argument that is going to convince precisely fuckbody?</i></b><br /> <br /> Because that would be lovely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Satchel has Spoken! I'm done. Going back to watching anime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:24:56-07:00","id":176710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176655#post176655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree, and the book DOESN'T. Its not there. Nowhere in there does it talk about it. That was a ruling that came out of this bullshit &quot;Werewolves bypass vampire protection&quot; conversation in the first place. It wasn't even a ruling until that very point, instead it had previously been ruled otherwise until this discussion came up! Hell it probably would have stayed as &quot;No&quot; except this damn conversation. And after that ruling I didn't care nearly as much. In fact, I don't care either way now because of that, but I still think its poor design to create something that specifically targets another PC splat and only that one.<br /> <br /> Your ignoring whole swaths of my argument on the second part of that though. If something effects one, it should effect everything. If werewolf claws deal lethal to vampires, they should ignore any similar protections and downgradings mage armor should provide, ignore bezoars or whatever they are, be un-bulwarkable(isn't that what sin-eaters do with damage? downgrading lethal to bashing by flooding with plasm?) Etc etc.<br /> <br /> But currently it has no purpose other than specifically vampires and werewolf antagonists. It's highly doubtful mages will have a mage armor that works similar enough, though death or life, and then thats an invested power. Then there's the whole thing about whether or not this or that will have an equivalent. We don't know if anything past Mage will even get a chronicle book!<br /> <br /> As stands, its specifically an ability that fucks over vampires in regards to other player characters. It could just as easily be something that only effects spirits and spirit associated things, but no, it effects vampires and only vampires also.<br /> <br /> What would you think if Promethean's wasteland made werewolves healing less effective, or disquiet? What if 1 essence was always 1 lethal wound when effected by disquiet regardless of primal urge, but didn't have an effect on any other gameline? What if it turned off their bashing damage healing altogether?<br /> <br /> Now if Promethean, Geist, Changeling, and Mummy ever get chronicle books, then there may be more, but even then its still iffy on how that would work or even if it would apply in a similar way.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is currently how it is being ruled is it not? Regardless of why, the precedence has already been set. Yet you argue so passionately against one case while pointedly ignoring the other.<br /> <br /> And you keep saying it specifically targets one splat, which is incorrect. It targets nothing. What it does it make a werewolves natural weaponry count as supernatural for <i>any</i> and <i>all</i> effects/situations in which it would matter. Whether it is a situation that currently exists or will exist in the future, whether it interacts with a mechanic/ability possessed by other werewolves/spirits/vampires/mages/sin-eaters/whatever, whether the results of it them being supernatural are good or bad for the werewolf, it would apply against everything <i>evenly</i>.<br /> <br /> If mages required Prime to shield against any supernatural effect it would apply against that. If hunters were packing something that shielded them against supernatural weaponry a werewolves teeth and claws would be rendered ineffective by that. If demons have something that tracks down active supernatural effects/weaponry then they would be able to lock onto a werewolf in any of its intermediary forms. The fact of the matter is that it <i>does</i> apply to every situation in which such things would be checked, whether the check would be brought forth by mechanics or by narrative, and it will always apply in the same way, by testing positively. Now let me tell you what it does not do. It does <i>not</i> ignore innate mechanics of any other splat. It does <i>not</i> only apply against a single source, it does <i>not</i> change or alter any other mechanic from any other source in any other book regardless of which splat said book belongs to.<br /> <br /> As for your example, I wouldn't mind at all if Wasteland had a healing stunting effect, in fact it sounds like a valid mechanic. But as with the werewolf mechanics it would have to apply against every target in which it could be applied. In which case if it were healing effects in general, it would apply to everything that could heal that was subject to the effect. Even something like limiting essence expenditure specifically would be fine (if odd for them specifically to have it) as long as it applied to all expenditures of essence. Werewolves would be limited, mages trying to convert essence into mana or use it for other things would be limited, spirits would be limited, etc. I would be fine with something that specifically designed to deal more damage to wolves and wolf-like creatures. But such a thing would again, have to apply against everything that could fit that criteria. Werewolves, shapeshifted mages/vampires, etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 06-22-2014, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:47:09-07:00","id":176719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176710#post176710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet you argue so passionately against one case while pointedly ignoring the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindly ignore both to the point of arguing not at all; this discussion is only productive if your aim is in being an eyesore. Endeavor to be less boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-22-2014, 12:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T21:53:20-07:00","id":176733,"title":"","content":"About no Armor thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176247#post176247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I am sure. It was asked in the comments of that thread, IIRC, and Stew replied that they don't have armor in gauru anymore (isn't needed, with the epic regeneration).</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you found that and quote? I want to show it to players, as they will cringe I made rules up, again.<br /> <br /> Also, even without Armor, I think that Primal Urge number of Lethals in turn is enough for fights. Bigger, nastier werewolves ( with larger Primal Urge ) have big advantage but they are beatable, if character is more experienced ( higher Attributes and Skills ) or lucky one in combat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-22-2014, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T22:22:43-07:00","id":176748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/124026-idigam-chronicles-weekly-discussion-shapeshifting?p=176719#post176719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindly ignore both to the point of arguing not at all; this discussion is only productive if your aim is in being an eyesore. Endeavor to be less boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't feel that we've quite seen eye to eye on the subject yet so I will continue to discuss it as long as I remain interested in arguing my point and someone has a counter argument in which I disagree with. If you're bored with said argument let it be known that I'm not forcing you to read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T23:58:26-07:00","id":176793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally p